art": 937.7199999999999, "end": 944.04, "text": " contradiction, or entropy, which is S, is injected into the system. Okay. This creates an entropy", "tokens": [51011, 34937, 11, 420, 30867, 11, 597, 307, 318, 11, 307, 36967, 666, 264, 1185, 13, 1033, 13, 639, 7829, 364, 30867, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057455135428387184, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298368904488214e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 92480, "start": 944.04, "end": 950.8399999999999, "text": " gradient. Think of it as a slope from high disorder to low disorder. That gradient drives the vector flow,", "tokens": [51327, 16235, 13, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 257, 13525, 490, 1090, 13399, 281, 2295, 13399, 13, 663, 16235, 11754, 264, 8062, 3095, 11, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057455135428387184, "compression_ratio": 1.6147540983606556, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298368904488214e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 95084, "start": 950.84, "end": 956.0600000000001, "text": " the V. So the river flows down the mountain of entropy. Beautifully put. And that becker flow,", "tokens": [50365, 264, 691, 13, 407, 264, 6810, 12867, 760, 264, 6937, 295, 30867, 13, 10584, 15386, 829, 13, 400, 300, 312, 9178, 3095, 11, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06263258076515518, "compression_ratio": 1.5892255892255893, "no_speech_prob": 2.100592052731165e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 95084, "start": 956.1800000000001, "end": 960.6600000000001, "text": " in turn, transports and accumulates the scalar mass, the phi. Hang on. I need to make sure I'm", "tokens": [50632, 294, 1261, 11, 5495, 82, 293, 12989, 26192, 264, 39684, 2758, 11, 264, 13107, 13, 14070, 322, 13, 286, 643, 281, 652, 988, 286, 478, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06263258076515518, "compression_ratio": 1.5892255892255893, "no_speech_prob": 2.100592052731165e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 95084, "start": 960.6600000000001, "end": 964.46, "text": " hearing you correctly. You're saying gravity. The thing holding me in this chair right now,", "tokens": [50856, 4763, 291, 8944, 13, 509, 434, 1566, 12110, 13, 440, 551, 5061, 385, 294, 341, 6090, 558, 586, 11, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06263258076515518, "compression_ratio": 1.5892255892255893, "no_speech_prob": 2.100592052731165e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 95084, "start": 964.58, "end": 969.2800000000001, "text": " the thing keeping the earth orbiting the sun, doesn't exist as a fundamental pull. That's what", "tokens": [51052, 264, 551, 5145, 264, 4120, 48985, 264, 3295, 11, 1177, 380, 2514, 382, 257, 8088, 2235, 13, 663, 311, 437, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06263258076515518, "compression_ratio": 1.5892255892255893, "no_speech_prob": 2.100592052731165e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 95084, "start": 969.2800000000001, "end": 973.3000000000001, "text": " the math suggests. It's just a mathematical draft, like wind in a tunnel caused by the universe", "tokens": [51287, 264, 5221, 13409, 13, 467, 311, 445, 257, 18894, 11206, 11, 411, 2468, 294, 257, 13186, 7008, 538, 264, 6445, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06263258076515518, "compression_ratio": 1.5892255892255893, "no_speech_prob": 2.100592052731165e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 97330, "start": 973.3, "end": 980.5799999999999, "text": " trying to resolve chaos. That is exactly what the RSVP theory proposes. The force you feel is gravity", "tokens": [50365, 1382, 281, 14151, 14158, 13, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 2365, 4201, 13, 440, 3464, 291, 841, 307, 12110, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06674778938293457, "compression_ratio": 1.6356275303643724, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 97330, "start": 980.5799999999999, "end": 987.2199999999999, "text": " is constitutively identified with the entropic descent of these flow trajectories. Wow. A test", "tokens": [50729, 307, 23079, 325, 3413, 9234, 365, 264, 948, 39173, 23475, 295, 613, 3095, 18257, 2083, 13, 3153, 13, 316, 1500, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06674778938293457, "compression_ratio": 1.6356275303643724, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 97330, "start": 987.2199999999999, "end": 992.9, "text": " particle, say an apple falling from a tree, is not being pulled by the mass of the earth. It is", "tokens": [51061, 12359, 11, 584, 364, 10606, 7440, 490, 257, 4230, 11, 307, 406, 885, 7373, 538, 264, 2758, 295, 264, 4120, 13, 467, 307, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06674778938293457, "compression_ratio": 1.6356275303643724, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 97330, "start": 992.9, "end": 998.9599999999999, "text": " literally being pushed by the entropy gradient along the Lamfordine flow. Pushed by entropy? Right. The mass of", "tokens": [51345, 3736, 885, 9152, 538, 264, 30867, 16235, 2051, 264, 18825, 7404, 533, 3095, 13, 18229, 292, 538, 30867, 30, 1779, 13, 440, 2758, 295, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06674778938293457, "compression_ratio": 1.6356275303643724, "no_speech_prob": 1.489249262104364e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 99896, "start": 998.96, "end": 1005.48, "text": " the earth is just a dense accumulation of phi that shapes that local entropy gradient. You are falling", "tokens": [50365, 264, 4120, 307, 445, 257, 18011, 35647, 295, 13107, 300, 10854, 300, 2654, 30867, 16235, 13, 509, 366, 7440, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060540471121529556, "compression_ratio": 1.6019417475728155, "no_speech_prob": 1.741107800469488e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 99896, "start": 1005.48, "end": 1010.2, "text": " down a thermodynamic slope. Okay. That sounds beautifully poetic, but does that actually hold", "tokens": [50691, 760, 257, 8810, 34988, 13525, 13, 1033, 13, 663, 3263, 16525, 41080, 11, 457, 775, 300, 767, 1797, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060540471121529556, "compression_ratio": 1.6019417475728155, "no_speech_prob": 1.741107800469488e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 99896, "start": 1010.2, "end": 1014.1, "text": " up mathematically against what we already know? It really does. Because we have Einstein's general", "tokens": [50927, 493, 44003, 1970, 437, 321, 1217, 458, 30, 467, 534, 775, 13, 1436, 321, 362, 23486, 311, 2674, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060540471121529556, "compression_ratio": 1.6019417475728155, "no_speech_prob": 1.741107800469488e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 99896, "start": 1014.1, "end": 1020.1800000000001, "text": " relativity. It works. GPS works because of it. If fliction says gravity is just fluid thermodynamics,", "tokens": [51122, 45675, 13, 467, 1985, 13, 19462, 1985, 570, 295, 309, 13, 759, 932, 4105, 1619, 12110, 307, 445, 9113, 8810, 35483, 11, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060540471121529556, "compression_ratio": 1.6019417475728155, "no_speech_prob": 1.741107800469488e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 99896, "start": 1020.6600000000001, "end": 1024.72, "text": " does it break Einstein? This is where the physics community would likely sit up and pay attention", "tokens": [51450, 775, 309, 1821, 23486, 30, 639, 307, 689, 264, 10649, 1768, 576, 3700, 1394, 493, 293, 1689, 3202, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.060540471121529556, "compression_ratio": 1.6019417475728155, "no_speech_prob": 1.741107800469488e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 102472, "start": 1024.72, "end": 1030.08, "text": " because it doesn't break Einstein. It derives him. It derives him. That is the beauty of the math", "tokens": [50365, 570, 309, 1177, 380, 1821, 23486, 13, 467, 1163, 1539, 796, 13, 467, 1163, 1539, 796, 13, 663, 307, 264, 6643, 295, 264, 5221, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06783493103519563, "compression_ratio": 1.6254071661237786, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856398225683188e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 102472, "start": 1030.08, "end": 1036.68, "text": " in the paper. If you take the RSVP field equations and you push them to what's called their quasi-static", "tokens": [50633, 294, 264, 3035, 13, 759, 291, 747, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 2519, 11787, 293, 291, 2944, 552, 281, 437, 311, 1219, 641, 20954, 12, 34632, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06783493103519563, "compression_ratio": 1.6254071661237786, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856398225683188e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 102472, "start": 1036.68, "end": 1042.0, "text": " limit. Meaning what, like taking a snapshot where things are barely moving? Exactly. You assume the", "tokens": [50963, 4948, 13, 19948, 437, 11, 411, 1940, 257, 30163, 689, 721, 366, 10268, 2684, 30, 7587, 13, 509, 6552, 264, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06783493103519563, "compression_ratio": 1.6254071661237786, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856398225683188e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 102472, "start": 1042.0, "end": 1047.68, "text": " vector flow is extremely slow, barely changing. If you analyze the equations under that constraint,", "tokens": [51229, 8062, 3095, 307, 4664, 2964, 11, 10268, 4473, 13, 759, 291, 12477, 264, 11787, 833, 300, 25534, 11, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06783493103519563, "compression_ratio": 1.6254071661237786, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856398225683188e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 102472, "start": 1047.94, "end": 1052.94, "text": " they reduce exactly to Eric Verlinde's theory of entropic gravity. Oh, I've heard of that. Yeah.", "tokens": [51526, 436, 5407, 2293, 281, 9336, 4281, 75, 8274, 311, 5261, 295, 948, 39173, 12110, 13, 876, 11, 286, 600, 2198, 295, 300, 13, 865, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06783493103519563, "compression_ratio": 1.6254071661237786, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856398225683188e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 105294, "start": 1052.94, "end": 1058.52, "text": " Verlinde proposed a few years ago that gravity is an emergent thermodynamic phenomenon where force", "tokens": [50365, 4281, 75, 8274, 10348, 257, 1326, 924, 2057, 300, 12110, 307, 364, 4345, 6930, 8810, 34988, 14029, 689, 3464, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679423277043114, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980582742519678e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 105294, "start": 1058.52, "end": 1064.9, "text": " equals temperature times the gradient of entropy. Fliction's RSVP equations yield Verlinde's theory", "tokens": [50644, 6915, 4292, 1413, 264, 16235, 295, 30867, 13, 3235, 4105, 311, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 11257, 4281, 75, 8274, 311, 5261, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679423277043114, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980582742519678e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 105294, "start": 1064.9, "end": 1070.68, "text": " perfectly. That's wild, but it goes further than Verlinde, doesn't it? Much further. If you take", "tokens": [50963, 6239, 13, 663, 311, 4868, 11, 457, 309, 1709, 3052, 813, 4281, 75, 8274, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 12313, 3052, 13, 759, 291, 747, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679423277043114, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980582742519678e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 105294, "start": 1070.68, "end": 1076.4, "text": " the RSVP equations to the stiff limit where the medium strongly resists expansion or compression", "tokens": [51252, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 281, 264, 15451, 4948, 689, 264, 6399, 10613, 725, 1751, 11260, 420, 19355, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679423277043114, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980582742519678e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 105294, "start": 1076.4, "end": 1082.5800000000002, "text": " and you apply the flow congruence across a local Rindler horizon. Okay, time out. A Rindler horizon", "tokens": [51538, 293, 291, 3079, 264, 3095, 8882, 84, 655, 2108, 257, 2654, 497, 471, 1918, 18046, 13, 1033, 11, 565, 484, 13, 316, 497, 471, 1918, 18046, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679423277043114, "compression_ratio": 1.64, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980582742519678e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 108258, "start": 1082.58, "end": 1087.6599999999999, "text": " for our listeners who aren't quantum physicists, that's basically an artificial boundary of what", "tokens": [50365, 337, 527, 23274, 567, 3212, 380, 13018, 48716, 11, 300, 311, 1936, 364, 11677, 12866, 295, 437, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055536059645919116, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750175465402029e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 108258, "start": 1087.6599999999999, "end": 1091.6399999999999, "text": " an accelerating observer can see, right? Correct. Like if I'm in a rocket ship accelerating near", "tokens": [50619, 364, 34391, 27878, 393, 536, 11, 558, 30, 12753, 13, 1743, 498, 286, 478, 294, 257, 13012, 5374, 34391, 2651, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055536059645919116, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750175465402029e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 108258, "start": 1091.6399999999999, "end": 1096.3799999999999, "text": " the speed of light, there's a horizon behind me where light can never catch up to me. Exactly.", "tokens": [50818, 264, 3073, 295, 1442, 11, 456, 311, 257, 18046, 2261, 385, 689, 1442, 393, 1128, 3745, 493, 281, 385, 13, 7587, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055536059645919116, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750175465402029e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 108258, "start": 1096.54, "end": 1102.86, "text": " It's a localized boundary of observability created by acceleration. If you map the RSVP fluid flow", "tokens": [51063, 467, 311, 257, 44574, 12866, 295, 9951, 2310, 2942, 538, 17162, 13, 759, 291, 4471, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 9113, 3095, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055536059645919116, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750175465402029e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 108258, "start": 1102.86, "end": 1109.1399999999999, "text": " across that thermodynamic boundary, it perfectly recovers Ted Jacobson's famous 1995 derivation.", "tokens": [51379, 2108, 300, 8810, 34988, 12866, 11, 309, 6239, 7759, 840, 14985, 44068, 266, 311, 4618, 22601, 10151, 399, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.055536059645919116, "compression_ratio": 1.5973597359735974, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750175465402029e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 110914, "start": 1109.14, "end": 1114.8000000000002, "text": " And what did Jacobson show? He showed that you could derive the Einstein field equations of general", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 630, 44068, 266, 855, 30, 634, 4712, 300, 291, 727, 28446, 264, 23486, 2519, 11787, 295, 2674, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06494627327754579, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040521333750892e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 110914, "start": 1114.8000000000002, "end": 1120.46, "text": " relativity purely from thermodynamics. So Einstein's equations, the geometry of curving", "tokens": [50648, 45675, 17491, 490, 8810, 35483, 13, 407, 23486, 311, 11787, 11, 264, 18426, 295, 1262, 798, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06494627327754579, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040521333750892e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 110914, "start": 1120.46, "end": 1127.5800000000002, "text": " spacetime, are completely hidden inside Fliction's fluid dynamics. Correct. It unifies the thermodynamic", "tokens": [50931, 39404, 9764, 11, 366, 2584, 7633, 1854, 3235, 4105, 311, 9113, 15679, 13, 12753, 13, 467, 517, 11221, 264, 8810, 34988, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06494627327754579, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040521333750892e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 110914, "start": 1127.5800000000002, "end": 1135.3600000000001, "text": " and geometric views of gravity into a single fluid dynamic medium. RSVP is essentially the parent equation.", "tokens": [51287, 293, 33246, 6809, 295, 12110, 666, 257, 2167, 9113, 8546, 6399, 13, 25855, 53, 47, 307, 4476, 264, 2596, 5367, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06494627327754579, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040521333750892e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 113536, "start": 1135.36, "end": 1140.4799999999998, "text": " And Einstein is just a special case. Einstein's relativity is just what happens when you run that", "tokens": [50365, 400, 23486, 307, 445, 257, 2121, 1389, 13, 23486, 311, 45675, 307, 445, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 1190, 300, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05830192565917969, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457248553352952e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 113536, "start": 1140.4799999999998, "end": 1146.82, "text": " parent equation under specific stiff observable conditions. That is massive. If everything is this", "tokens": [50621, 2596, 5367, 833, 2685, 15451, 9951, 712, 4487, 13, 663, 307, 5994, 13, 759, 1203, 307, 341, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05830192565917969, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457248553352952e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 113536, "start": 1146.82, "end": 1153.34, "text": " fluid driven by entropy, how does that explain LAP1b? Well, let's look at it. Because in the standard", "tokens": [50938, 9113, 9555, 538, 30867, 11, 577, 775, 300, 2903, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 30, 1042, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 309, 13, 1436, 294, 264, 3832, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05830192565917969, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457248553352952e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 113536, "start": 1153.34, "end": 1159.2199999999998, "text": " model of cosmology, the lambda-cold dark matter model galaxies form through a bottom-up random hierarchical", "tokens": [51264, 2316, 295, 22207, 1793, 11, 264, 13607, 12, 1291, 348, 2877, 1871, 2316, 28755, 1254, 807, 257, 2767, 12, 1010, 4974, 35250, 804, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05830192565917969, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457248553352952e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 113536, "start": 1159.2199999999998, "end": 1164.3999999999999, "text": " merging. Little clumps of dark matter smashed together, they get bigger, their gravity draws in gas,", "tokens": [51558, 44559, 13, 8022, 596, 16951, 295, 2877, 1871, 33269, 1214, 11, 436, 483, 3801, 11, 641, 12110, 20045, 294, 4211, 11, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05830192565917969, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457248553352952e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 116440, "start": 1164.4, "end": 1170.0, "text": " that gas makes stars. It's a messy, chaotic collision course. Right. But LAP1b doesn't really fit that.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 4211, 1669, 6105, 13, 467, 311, 257, 16191, 11, 27013, 24644, 1164, 13, 1779, 13, 583, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 1177, 380, 534, 3318, 300, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0884384272391336, "compression_ratio": 1.5643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.124902467523504e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 116440, "start": 1170.0800000000002, "end": 1177.3000000000002, "text": " It's too isolated, too pristine, too unstirred. Under the RSVP framework, LAP1b's formation isn't a random", "tokens": [50649, 467, 311, 886, 14621, 11, 886, 582, 42745, 11, 886, 18799, 347, 986, 13, 6974, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 11, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 311, 11723, 1943, 380, 257, 4974, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0884384272391336, "compression_ratio": 1.5643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.124902467523504e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 116440, "start": 1177.3000000000002, "end": 1185.5600000000002, "text": " collision at all. It is described by a process called SIED, scalar eruption via entropic differential.", "tokens": [51010, 24644, 412, 439, 13, 467, 307, 7619, 538, 257, 1399, 1219, 29083, 4731, 11, 39684, 42584, 5766, 948, 39173, 15756, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0884384272391336, "compression_ratio": 1.5643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.124902467523504e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 116440, "start": 1186.1200000000001, "end": 1190.8200000000002, "text": " Scalar eruption? That sounds like a rash. I know. It's a very technical term. Think of it more like", "tokens": [51451, 2747, 12031, 42584, 30, 663, 3263, 411, 257, 40357, 13, 286, 458, 13, 467, 311, 257, 588, 6191, 1433, 13, 6557, 295, 309, 544, 411, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0884384272391336, "compression_ratio": 1.5643939393939394, "no_speech_prob": 2.124902467523504e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 119082, "start": 1190.82, "end": 1196.32, "text": " condensation. Condensation. Okay. Instead of random clumps smashing together, structure forms via", "tokens": [50365, 2224, 35292, 13, 21793, 35292, 13, 1033, 13, 7156, 295, 4974, 596, 16951, 43316, 1214, 11, 3877, 6422, 5766, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0851674472584444, "compression_ratio": 1.579591836734694, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300918747140677e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 119082, "start": 1196.32, "end": 1203.6, "text": " regulated instability. Imagine the scalar field, the phi, as a perfectly smooth, flat surface of a pond.", "tokens": [50640, 26243, 34379, 13, 11739, 264, 39684, 2519, 11, 264, 13107, 11, 382, 257, 6239, 5508, 11, 4962, 3753, 295, 257, 17384, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0851674472584444, "compression_ratio": 1.579591836734694, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300918747140677e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 119082, "start": 1203.78, "end": 1208.6399999999999, "text": " Got the visual. As entropy accumulates in the environment, it changes the local free energy", "tokens": [51013, 5803, 264, 5056, 13, 1018, 30867, 12989, 26192, 294, 264, 2823, 11, 309, 2962, 264, 2654, 1737, 2281, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0851674472584444, "compression_ratio": 1.579591836734694, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300918747140677e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 119082, "start": 1208.6399999999999, "end": 1214.26, "text": " landscape. At a certain threshold, the smooth background becomes thermodynamically unstable,", "tokens": [51256, 9661, 13, 1711, 257, 1629, 14678, 11, 264, 5508, 3678, 3643, 8810, 21399, 984, 23742, 11, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0851674472584444, "compression_ratio": 1.579591836734694, "no_speech_prob": 1.2300918747140677e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 121426, "start": 1214.26, "end": 1219.84, "text": " and structure suddenly erupts or pops into existence. Like water droplets forming. Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 3877, 5800, 20999, 39280, 420, 16795, 666, 9123, 13, 1743, 1281, 41573, 15745, 13, 7587, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04642521909305027, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796973104609258e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 121426, "start": 1220.02, "end": 1225.12, "text": " Like condensation suddenly forming on a cold glass on a humid day. The condensation doesn't just form", "tokens": [50653, 1743, 2224, 35292, 5800, 15745, 322, 257, 3554, 4276, 322, 257, 34649, 786, 13, 440, 2224, 35292, 1177, 380, 445, 1254, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04642521909305027, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796973104609258e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 121426, "start": 1225.12, "end": 1230.6, "text": " one giant drop. It forms specific little droplets of a certain size. Which is exactly what the math", "tokens": [50908, 472, 7410, 3270, 13, 467, 6422, 2685, 707, 41573, 295, 257, 1629, 2744, 13, 3013, 307, 2293, 437, 264, 5221, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04642521909305027, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796973104609258e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 121426, "start": 1230.6, "end": 1236.12, "text": " predicts. The instability in the RSVP equations is band limited. There is a specific mathematical", "tokens": [51182, 6069, 82, 13, 440, 34379, 294, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 307, 4116, 5567, 13, 821, 307, 257, 2685, 18894, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04642521909305027, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796973104609258e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 121426, "start": 1236.12, "end": 1241.58, "text": " correlation length determined by the gradient of the free energy. So there's a Goldilocks zone for size?", "tokens": [51458, 20009, 4641, 9540, 538, 264, 16235, 295, 264, 1737, 2281, 13, 407, 456, 311, 257, 6731, 388, 35507, 6668, 337, 2744, 30, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04642521909305027, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796973104609258e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 124158, "start": 1241.58, "end": 1248.76, "text": " Right. Below that scale, growth is too slow to matter. Above that scale, growth is actively suppressed", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 36261, 300, 4373, 11, 4599, 307, 886, 2964, 281, 1871, 13, 32691, 300, 4373, 11, 4599, 307, 13022, 42645, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07114864745230046, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832377084022074e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 124158, "start": 1248.76, "end": 1255.6999999999998, "text": " by the mathematics. Therefore, structure naturally erupts at this preferred mathematically pure spatial", "tokens": [50724, 538, 264, 18666, 13, 7504, 11, 3877, 8195, 20999, 39280, 412, 341, 16494, 44003, 6075, 23598, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07114864745230046, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832377084022074e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 124158, "start": 1255.6999999999998, "end": 1262.3, "text": " scale. So LAP-1b isn't a random survivor of a chaotic collision process. It didn't merge into existence.", "tokens": [51071, 4373, 13, 407, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 65, 1943, 380, 257, 4974, 25953, 295, 257, 27013, 24644, 1399, 13, 467, 994, 380, 22183, 666, 9123, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07114864745230046, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832377084022074e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 124158, "start": 1262.56, "end": 1268.02, "text": " No. It is an isolated mode that erupted, condensed out of the background, right at its natural correlation", "tokens": [51414, 883, 13, 467, 307, 364, 14621, 4391, 300, 20999, 25383, 11, 36398, 484, 295, 264, 3678, 11, 558, 412, 1080, 3303, 20009, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07114864745230046, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832377084022074e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 124158, "start": 1268.02, "end": 1269.54, "text": " length. And because it was so isolated.", "tokens": [51687, 4641, 13, 400, 570, 309, 390, 370, 14621, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07114864745230046, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832377084022074e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 126954, "start": 1269.54, "end": 1275.26, "text": " It condensed before the surrounding medium had undergone enough entropic processing to stir it", "tokens": [50365, 467, 36398, 949, 264, 11498, 6399, 632, 833, 39743, 1547, 948, 39173, 9007, 281, 8946, 309, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1758557651819808, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 2.05194194968783e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 126954, "start": 1275.26, "end": 1279.5, "text": " up and overwrite it. It's a mathematically pure condensation of early reality.", "tokens": [50651, 493, 293, 670, 21561, 309, 13, 467, 311, 257, 44003, 6075, 2224, 35292, 295, 2440, 4103, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1758557651819808, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 2.05194194968783e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 126954, "start": 1279.5, "end": 1286.24, "text": " Okay, let's take a breath. Because if RSVP accurately derives Einstein's gravity from entropy and beautifully", "tokens": [50863, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 6045, 13, 1436, 498, 25855, 53, 47, 20095, 1163, 1539, 23486, 311, 12110, 490, 30867, 293, 16525, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1758557651819808, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 2.05194194968783e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 126954, "start": 1286.24, "end": 1292.56, "text": " models early galaxy formation as condensation, that alone is a Nobel-level physics breakthrough.", "tokens": [51200, 5245, 2440, 17639, 11723, 382, 2224, 35292, 11, 300, 3312, 307, 257, 24611, 12, 12418, 10649, 22397, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1758557651819808, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 2.05194194968783e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 126954, "start": 1292.72, "end": 1293.24, "text": " Undoubtedly.", "tokens": [51524, 2719, 32135, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1758557651819808, "compression_ratio": 1.5173745173745175, "no_speech_prob": 2.05194194968783e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 129324, "start": 1293.24, "end": 1298.24, "text": " But this is where fliction leaves the realm of pure astrophysics and ventures into something that feels", "tokens": [50365, 583, 341, 307, 689, 932, 4105, 5510, 264, 15355, 295, 6075, 5357, 11741, 41732, 293, 6931, 1303, 666, 746, 300, 3417, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 129324, "start": 1298.24, "end": 1303.82, "text": " almost dangerous. The monographs claim that contemporary physics, cognitive science, and social", "tokens": [50615, 1920, 5795, 13, 440, 1108, 3108, 82, 3932, 300, 14878, 10649, 11, 15605, 3497, 11, 293, 2093, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 129324, "start": 1303.82, "end": 1306.24, "text": " theory share a structural disability.", "tokens": [50894, 5261, 2073, 257, 15067, 11090, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 129324, "start": 1306.58, "end": 1308.1, "text": " Those are strong words in the paper.", "tokens": [51032, 3950, 366, 2068, 2283, 294, 264, 3035, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 129324, "start": 1308.48, "end": 1314.68, "text": " They really are. They accuse modern science of keeping identical mathematical motifs quarantined from", "tokens": [51127, 814, 534, 366, 13, 814, 43610, 4363, 3497, 295, 5145, 14800, 18894, 2184, 18290, 41240, 2001, 490, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 129324, "start": 1314.68, "end": 1317.2, "text": " each other, treating them as mere analogies.", "tokens": [51437, 1184, 661, 11, 15083, 552, 382, 8401, 16660, 530, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11938589362687962, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.158829105064486e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 131720, "start": 1317.2, "end": 1321.92, "text": " Yes. This is where fliction introduces the ontological translation matrix.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 639, 307, 689, 932, 4105, 31472, 264, 6592, 4383, 12853, 8141, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 131720, "start": 1321.92, "end": 1322.92, "text": " The translation matrix?", "tokens": [50601, 440, 12853, 8141, 30, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 131720, "start": 1322.92, "end": 1330.0, "text": " The core argument is that cosmological expansion, cognitive inference in your brain, and institutional", "tokens": [50651, 440, 4965, 6770, 307, 300, 22207, 4383, 11260, 11, 15605, 38253, 294, 428, 3567, 11, 293, 18391, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 131720, "start": 1330.0, "end": 1332.92, "text": " drift in a government are not just similar concepts.", "tokens": [51005, 19699, 294, 257, 2463, 366, 406, 445, 2531, 10392, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 131720, "start": 1332.92, "end": 1333.92, "text": " Just identical.", "tokens": [51151, 1449, 14800, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 131720, "start": 1333.92, "end": 1338.92, "text": " They are identical mathematical processes operating on the exact same RSVP substrate.", "tokens": [51201, 814, 366, 14800, 18894, 7555, 7447, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 25855, 53, 47, 27585, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16679745215874214, "compression_ratio": 1.6108597285067874, "no_speech_prob": 2.003444068629512e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 133892, "start": 1338.92, "end": 1344.98, "text": " See, I have to push back here. Are we really saying a galaxy, a human brain, and a government", "tokens": [50365, 3008, 11, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 510, 13, 2014, 321, 534, 1566, 257, 17639, 11, 257, 1952, 3567, 11, 293, 257, 2463, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 133892, "start": 1344.98, "end": 1348.78, "text": " bureaucracy are the same thing? Because that sounds like a giant metaphor.", "tokens": [50668, 44671, 366, 264, 912, 551, 30, 1436, 300, 3263, 411, 257, 7410, 19157, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 133892, "start": 1349.0600000000002, "end": 1350.0, "text": " It does sound like one.", "tokens": [50872, 467, 775, 1626, 411, 472, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 133892, "start": 1350.04, "end": 1354.1000000000001, "text": " It sounds like a poet looked at a picture of a neural network and a picture of a galaxy", "tokens": [50921, 467, 3263, 411, 257, 20874, 2956, 412, 257, 3036, 295, 257, 18161, 3209, 293, 257, 3036, 295, 257, 17639, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 133892, "start": 1354.1000000000001, "end": 1357.8600000000001, "text": " supercluster and said, look, they both look like webs. They must be the same.", "tokens": [51124, 1687, 3474, 8393, 293, 848, 11, 574, 11, 436, 1293, 574, 411, 2859, 13, 814, 1633, 312, 264, 912, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 133892, "start": 1357.8600000000001, "end": 1364.48, "text": " It is a totally valid skepticism, but fliction anticipates it. The author is explicit. It is decidedly", "tokens": [51312, 467, 307, 257, 3879, 7363, 19128, 26356, 11, 457, 932, 4105, 10416, 1024, 309, 13, 440, 3793, 307, 13691, 13, 467, 307, 3047, 356, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08068920771280924, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 2.184594736012735e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 136448, "start": 1364.48, "end": 1372.0, "text": " not an analogy. Not an analogy. Not an analogy. The relativistic scalar vector plenum is the", "tokens": [50365, 406, 364, 21663, 13, 1726, 364, 21663, 13, 1726, 364, 21663, 13, 440, 21960, 3142, 39684, 8062, 499, 268, 449, 307, 264, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 136448, "start": 1372.0, "end": 1377.68, "text": " underlying mathematical substrate for all of them. The coupled partial differential equations", "tokens": [50741, 14217, 18894, 27585, 337, 439, 295, 552, 13, 440, 29482, 14641, 15756, 11787, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 136448, "start": 1377.68, "end": 1383.28, "text": " governing the scalar, vector, and entropy fields are mathematically identical at the two derivative", "tokens": [51025, 30054, 264, 39684, 11, 8062, 11, 293, 30867, 7909, 366, 44003, 14800, 412, 264, 732, 13760, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 136448, "start": 1383.28, "end": 1385.1200000000001, "text": " order across all these domains.", "tokens": [51305, 1668, 2108, 439, 613, 25514, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 136448, "start": 1385.1200000000001, "end": 1387.92, "text": " So the equations literally do not change.", "tokens": [51397, 407, 264, 11787, 3736, 360, 406, 1319, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 136448, "start": 1387.92, "end": 1393.28, "text": " The math is exactly the same. The only thing that changes is the ontological translation, how", "tokens": [51537, 440, 5221, 307, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 440, 787, 551, 300, 2962, 307, 264, 6592, 4383, 12853, 11, 577, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460846492222377, "compression_ratio": 1.8306451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 2.0122438871422732e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 139328, "start": 1393.28, "end": 1399.04, "text": " the variables phi, v, s map to our specific domain of observational reality.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 9102, 13107, 11, 371, 11, 262, 4471, 281, 527, 2685, 9274, 295, 9951, 1478, 4103, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 139328, "start": 1399.04, "end": 1401.68, "text": " Okay, let's test this translation motrix. Let's take the brain.", "tokens": [50653, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1500, 341, 12853, 2184, 6579, 13, 961, 311, 747, 264, 3567, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 139328, "start": 1401.68, "end": 1402.08, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50785, 1779, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 139328, "start": 1402.08, "end": 1407.44, "text": " How do phi, the stuff, v, the flow, and s, the friction, map onto my mind?", "tokens": [50805, 1012, 360, 13107, 11, 264, 1507, 11, 371, 11, 264, 3095, 11, 293, 262, 11, 264, 17710, 11, 4471, 3911, 452, 1575, 30, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 139328, "start": 1407.44, "end": 1413.36, "text": " In the cognitive domain, which Flix designates as p-semantic, the translation is fascinating.", "tokens": [51073, 682, 264, 15605, 9274, 11, 597, 3235, 970, 1715, 1024, 382, 280, 12, 19872, 7128, 11, 264, 12853, 307, 10343, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 139328, "start": 1413.36, "end": 1418.24, "text": " The scalar potential, phi, translates meaning density or compressed representation.", "tokens": [51369, 440, 39684, 3995, 11, 13107, 11, 28468, 3620, 10305, 420, 30353, 10290, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 139328, "start": 1418.24, "end": 1419.12, "text": " Meaning density.", "tokens": [51613, 19948, 10305, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630169120994774, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266228172757356e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 141912, "start": 1419.12, "end": 1424.2399999999998, "text": " It is the accumulated coherence of your mental models, the facts you know, the concepts you", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 31346, 26528, 655, 295, 428, 4973, 5245, 11, 264, 9130, 291, 458, 11, 264, 10392, 291, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 141912, "start": 1424.2399999999998, "end": 1426.8799999999999, "text": " understand, the stable structures of your worldview.", "tokens": [50621, 1223, 11, 264, 8351, 9227, 295, 428, 41141, 13, 50753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 141912, "start": 1426.8799999999999, "end": 1428.3999999999999, "text": " Okay, so the mass of my knowledge.", "tokens": [50753, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 2758, 295, 452, 3601, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 141912, "start": 1428.3999999999999, "end": 1432.3999999999999, "text": " Yes. The vector flow, v, becomes directed inference. This is your sense of agency.", "tokens": [50829, 1079, 13, 440, 8062, 3095, 11, 371, 11, 3643, 12898, 38253, 13, 639, 307, 428, 2020, 295, 7934, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 141912, "start": 1432.3999999999999, "end": 1433.04, "text": " Oh, the agency.", "tokens": [51029, 876, 11, 264, 7934, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 141912, "start": 1433.04, "end": 1438.4799999999998, "text": " It's the active transport of your attention and effort. It is your conscious drive moving", "tokens": [51061, 467, 311, 264, 4967, 5495, 295, 428, 3202, 293, 4630, 13, 467, 307, 428, 6648, 3332, 2684, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 141912, "start": 1438.4799999999998, "end": 1439.76, "text": " through your mental landscape.", "tokens": [51333, 807, 428, 4973, 9661, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1214219584609523, "compression_ratio": 1.6978723404255318, "no_speech_prob": 1.943039479312958e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 143976, "start": 1439.76, "end": 1441.04, "text": " And what about s?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 466, 262, 30, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 143976, "start": 1441.04, "end": 1447.44, "text": " Entropy density, s, translates to your representational budget. This is the uncertainty, the surprise,", "tokens": [50429, 3951, 27514, 10305, 11, 262, 11, 28468, 281, 428, 2906, 1478, 4706, 13, 639, 307, 264, 15697, 11, 264, 6365, 11, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 143976, "start": 1447.44, "end": 1451.84, "text": " or the contradiction in your environment that your brain is desperately trying to resolve.", "tokens": [50749, 420, 264, 34937, 294, 428, 2823, 300, 428, 3567, 307, 23726, 1382, 281, 14151, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 143976, "start": 1451.84, "end": 1457.12, "text": " Wait, wait. So my sense of agency, my actual willpower, the feeling of me deciding to focus", "tokens": [50969, 3802, 11, 1699, 13, 407, 452, 2020, 295, 7934, 11, 452, 3539, 486, 9513, 11, 264, 2633, 295, 385, 17990, 281, 1879, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 143976, "start": 1457.12, "end": 1462.72, "text": " on a problem, is mathematically identical to gravity pushing an apple down a hill.", "tokens": [51233, 322, 257, 1154, 11, 307, 44003, 14800, 281, 12110, 7380, 364, 10606, 760, 257, 10997, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 143976, "start": 1462.72, "end": 1464.96, "text": " That is exactly what the translation implies.", "tokens": [51513, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 264, 12853, 18779, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10670803561068998, "compression_ratio": 1.5940959409594095, "no_speech_prob": 1.585630281589201e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 146496, "start": 1464.96, "end": 1470.0, "text": " It's just the vector flow trying to resolve an entropy gradient in my neural architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 445, 264, 8062, 3095, 1382, 281, 14151, 364, 30867, 16235, 294, 452, 18161, 9482, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 146496, "start": 1470.0, "end": 1474.16, "text": " Precisely. Your agency is the lamfridine flow of the cognitive fluid.", "tokens": [50617, 48746, 736, 13, 2260, 7934, 307, 264, 24688, 5779, 327, 533, 3095, 295, 264, 15605, 9113, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 146496, "start": 1474.16, "end": 1478.72, "text": " The paper formalizes this through what it calls the CLIO projection,", "tokens": [50825, 440, 3035, 9860, 5660, 341, 807, 437, 309, 5498, 264, 12855, 15167, 22743, 11, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 146496, "start": 1478.72, "end": 1480.88, "text": " the constrained learning and inference optimizer.", "tokens": [51053, 264, 38901, 2539, 293, 38253, 5028, 6545, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 146496, "start": 1480.88, "end": 1481.92, "text": " CLIO.", "tokens": [51161, 12855, 15167, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 146496, "start": 1481.92, "end": 1486.88, "text": " It states that the brain operates via gradient flow to minimize a specific loss functional.", "tokens": [51213, 467, 4368, 300, 264, 3567, 22577, 5766, 16235, 3095, 281, 17522, 257, 2685, 4470, 11745, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 146496, "start": 1486.88, "end": 1489.76, "text": " And this is where Flixion ties into established neuroscience.", "tokens": [51461, 400, 341, 307, 689, 3235, 970, 313, 14039, 666, 7545, 42762, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 146496, "start": 1490.32, "end": 1493.76, "text": " Theorem 5.4 in the text provides a rigorous mathematical proof", "tokens": [51633, 440, 37956, 1025, 13, 19, 294, 264, 2487, 6417, 257, 29882, 18894, 8177, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10891620183395127, "compression_ratio": 1.5987261146496816, "no_speech_prob": 1.882971643191178e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 149376, "start": 1493.76, "end": 1499.92, "text": " that the RSVP loss functional is perfectly dual to Carl Fristen's variational free energy.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 4470, 11745, 307, 6239, 11848, 281, 14256, 1526, 4821, 311, 3034, 1478, 1737, 2281, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 149376, "start": 1499.92, "end": 1502.8, "text": " Carl Fristen's free energy principle.", "tokens": [50673, 14256, 1526, 4821, 311, 1737, 2281, 8665, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 149376, "start": 1502.8, "end": 1505.04, "text": " Okay, this is a huge deal in neuroscience.", "tokens": [50817, 1033, 11, 341, 307, 257, 2603, 2028, 294, 42762, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 149376, "start": 1505.04, "end": 1506.0, "text": " It's foundational.", "tokens": [50929, 467, 311, 32195, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 149376, "start": 1506.0, "end": 1511.2, "text": " For those who aren't familiar, Fristen's theory basically argues that all biological systems,", "tokens": [50977, 1171, 729, 567, 3212, 380, 4963, 11, 1526, 4821, 311, 5261, 1936, 38218, 300, 439, 13910, 3652, 11, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 149376, "start": 1511.2, "end": 1516.48, "text": " especially human brains, are fundamentally driven to minimize surprise,", "tokens": [51237, 2318, 1952, 15442, 11, 366, 17879, 9555, 281, 17522, 6365, 11, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603071100571576, "compression_ratio": 1.5682819383259912, "no_speech_prob": 2.167277208392493e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 151648, "start": 1516.48, "end": 1524.08, "text": " to make their internal models of the world perfectly match the unpredictable, chaotic, outside world.", "tokens": [50365, 281, 652, 641, 6920, 5245, 295, 264, 1002, 6239, 2995, 264, 31160, 11, 27013, 11, 2380, 1002, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 151648, "start": 1524.08, "end": 1529.52, "text": " Yes. Let me give an example of how Fristen's principle works and how it maps to RSVP.", "tokens": [50745, 1079, 13, 961, 385, 976, 364, 1365, 295, 577, 1526, 4821, 311, 8665, 1985, 293, 577, 309, 11317, 281, 25855, 53, 47, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 151648, "start": 1529.52, "end": 1530.64, "text": " Please do.", "tokens": [51017, 2555, 360, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 151648, "start": 1530.64, "end": 1534.56, "text": " Imagine waking up in the middle of the night in a totally dark hotel room.", "tokens": [51073, 11739, 20447, 493, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 264, 1818, 294, 257, 3879, 2877, 7622, 1808, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 151648, "start": 1535.3600000000001, "end": 1537.52, "text": " Your brain has a model of your bedroom at home,", "tokens": [51309, 2260, 3567, 575, 257, 2316, 295, 428, 11211, 412, 1280, 11, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 151648, "start": 1537.52, "end": 1542.16, "text": " but the sensory input you are receiving, the spatial layout, does not match.", "tokens": [51417, 457, 264, 27233, 4846, 291, 366, 10040, 11, 264, 23598, 13333, 11, 775, 406, 2995, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12280657739922551, "compression_ratio": 1.5607843137254902, "no_speech_prob": 2.142329065882298e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 154216, "start": 1542.16, "end": 1545.2, "text": " You expect your nightstand to be on the left, but it's not.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2066, 428, 1818, 1115, 281, 312, 322, 264, 1411, 11, 457, 309, 311, 406, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 154216, "start": 1545.2, "end": 1550.64, "text": " Right. That mismatches entropy. It is surprise. It is a high state of variational free energy.", "tokens": [50517, 1779, 13, 663, 23220, 852, 279, 30867, 13, 467, 307, 6365, 13, 467, 307, 257, 1090, 1785, 295, 3034, 1478, 1737, 2281, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 154216, "start": 1550.64, "end": 1552.96, "text": " And it feels stressful. You're totally disoriented.", "tokens": [50789, 400, 309, 3417, 19108, 13, 509, 434, 3879, 717, 27414, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 154216, "start": 1552.96, "end": 1555.6000000000001, "text": " Exactly. The entropy gradient is steep.", "tokens": [50905, 7587, 13, 440, 30867, 16235, 307, 16841, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 154216, "start": 1555.6000000000001, "end": 1559.76, "text": " According to Fristen, you have two ways to resolve this and minimize the free energy.", "tokens": [51037, 7328, 281, 1526, 4821, 11, 291, 362, 732, 2098, 281, 14151, 341, 293, 17522, 264, 1737, 2281, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 154216, "start": 1559.76, "end": 1562.48, "text": " You can change your internal model to match the world.", "tokens": [51245, 509, 393, 1319, 428, 6920, 2316, 281, 2995, 264, 1002, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 154216, "start": 1562.48, "end": 1567.1200000000001, "text": " You grope around, feel the unfamiliar nightstand, and realize, ah, I'm in a hotel.", "tokens": [51381, 509, 4634, 494, 926, 11, 841, 264, 29415, 1818, 1115, 11, 293, 4325, 11, 3716, 11, 286, 478, 294, 257, 7622, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08413390350341797, "compression_ratio": 1.6319444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.2885831684610336e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 156712, "start": 1567.12, "end": 1572.8799999999999, "text": " Or you can change the world to match your model. You find the light switch, turn it on, and force", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 291, 393, 1319, 264, 1002, 281, 2995, 428, 2316, 13, 509, 915, 264, 1442, 3679, 11, 1261, 309, 322, 11, 293, 3464, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 156712, "start": 1572.8799999999999, "end": 1578.4799999999998, "text": " the environment to become predictable. Both are actions driven to reduce surprise.", "tokens": [50653, 264, 2823, 281, 1813, 27737, 13, 6767, 366, 5909, 9555, 281, 5407, 6365, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 156712, "start": 1578.4799999999998, "end": 1583.6799999999998, "text": " And Fliction is saying that entire process, that desperate drive to minimize surprise,", "tokens": [50933, 400, 3235, 4105, 307, 1566, 300, 2302, 1399, 11, 300, 17601, 3332, 281, 17522, 6365, 11, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 156712, "start": 1583.6799999999998, "end": 1586.9599999999998, "text": " is just the RSVP equation playing out in meat?", "tokens": [51193, 307, 445, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 5367, 2433, 484, 294, 4615, 30, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 156712, "start": 1586.9599999999998, "end": 1593.12, "text": " Fliction shows that Fristen's principle is just a localized manifestation of the RSVP equations", "tokens": [51357, 3235, 4105, 3110, 300, 1526, 4821, 311, 8665, 307, 445, 257, 44574, 29550, 295, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 156712, "start": 1593.12, "end": 1595.52, "text": " operating on the finite manifold of your skull.", "tokens": [51665, 7447, 322, 264, 19362, 47138, 295, 428, 11743, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07817673014703198, "compression_ratio": 1.6900369003690037, "no_speech_prob": 1.950802366867954e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 159552, "start": 1595.52, "end": 1600.6399999999999, "text": " Wow. The human brain is literally a physical manifestation of entropy gradient descent.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 440, 1952, 3567, 307, 3736, 257, 4001, 29550, 295, 30867, 16235, 23475, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 159552, "start": 1601.2, "end": 1605.76, "text": " When you grope around in the dark for that light switch, your directed inference, the V,", "tokens": [50649, 1133, 291, 4634, 494, 926, 294, 264, 2877, 337, 300, 1442, 3679, 11, 428, 12898, 38253, 11, 264, 691, 11, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 159552, "start": 1605.76, "end": 1611.04, "text": " is flowing down the gradient of uncertainty, the S to build a stable map of meeting the phi.", "tokens": [50877, 307, 13974, 760, 264, 16235, 295, 15697, 11, 264, 318, 281, 1322, 257, 8351, 4471, 295, 3440, 264, 13107, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 159552, "start": 1611.04, "end": 1613.52, "text": " So I am practically a falling universe.", "tokens": [51141, 407, 286, 669, 15667, 257, 7440, 6445, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 159552, "start": 1613.52, "end": 1617.44, "text": " You are just like a falling universe. Your cognitive architecture is mathematically identical to one.", "tokens": [51265, 509, 366, 445, 411, 257, 7440, 6445, 13, 2260, 15605, 9482, 307, 44003, 14800, 281, 472, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 159552, "start": 1617.44, "end": 1620.56, "text": " That is deeply unsettling, but incredibly elegant.", "tokens": [51461, 663, 307, 8760, 43964, 1688, 11, 457, 6252, 21117, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 159552, "start": 1620.56, "end": 1624.0, "text": " Okay. That covers the cosmos and the mind, the macro and the micro.", "tokens": [51617, 1033, 13, 663, 10538, 264, 41794, 293, 264, 1575, 11, 264, 18887, 293, 264, 4532, 13, 51789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1251402213925221, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.585286155819654e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 162400, "start": 1624.0, "end": 1625.84, "text": " But what about human society?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 466, 1952, 4086, 30, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 162400, "start": 1625.84, "end": 1627.12, "text": " Society's work is very practical.", "tokens": [50457, 13742, 311, 589, 307, 588, 8496, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 162400, "start": 1627.12, "end": 1633.92, "text": " What about the DMV or a massive corporation? The translation matrix tackles institutions too.", "tokens": [50521, 708, 466, 264, 15322, 53, 420, 257, 5994, 22197, 30, 440, 12853, 8141, 9426, 904, 8142, 886, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 162400, "start": 1633.92, "end": 1639.36, "text": " The paper calls this the sphere pop calculus. Let's map the variables again, this time to the", "tokens": [50861, 440, 3035, 5498, 341, 264, 16687, 1665, 33400, 13, 961, 311, 4471, 264, 9102, 797, 11, 341, 565, 281, 264, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 162400, "start": 1639.36, "end": 1644.8, "text": " institutional domain. In the institutional domain, designated P institution, the translation", "tokens": [51133, 18391, 9274, 13, 682, 264, 18391, 9274, 11, 21688, 430, 7818, 11, 264, 12853, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 162400, "start": 1644.8, "end": 1651.36, "text": " shifts again. The scalar field phi becomes the institutional core or mass. The mass of the institution.", "tokens": [51405, 19201, 797, 13, 440, 39684, 2519, 13107, 3643, 264, 18391, 4965, 420, 2758, 13, 440, 2758, 295, 264, 7818, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16084526524399267, "compression_ratio": 1.8211382113821137, "no_speech_prob": 1.70075921662044e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 165136, "start": 1651.36, "end": 1656.8799999999999, "text": " It is the accumulated resources, the physical buildings, the rule books, the solid unmoving", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 31346, 3593, 11, 264, 4001, 7446, 11, 264, 4978, 3642, 11, 264, 5100, 517, 3280, 798, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293240012703361, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234849836010978e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 165136, "start": 1656.8799999999999, "end": 1658.8, "text": " instructions of the organization. Makes sense.", "tokens": [50641, 9415, 295, 264, 4475, 13, 25245, 2020, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293240012703361, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234849836010978e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 165136, "start": 1658.8, "end": 1665.36, "text": " The vector field V translates to institutional drive or trajectory. What is the organization", "tokens": [50737, 440, 8062, 2519, 691, 28468, 281, 18391, 3332, 420, 21512, 13, 708, 307, 264, 4475, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293240012703361, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234849836010978e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 165136, "start": 1665.36, "end": 1670.4799999999998, "text": " actively trying to achieve? Their mission statement, basically. Right. And the entropy field,", "tokens": [51065, 13022, 1382, 281, 4584, 30, 6710, 4447, 5629, 11, 1936, 13, 1779, 13, 400, 264, 30867, 2519, 11, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293240012703361, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234849836010978e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 165136, "start": 1670.4799999999998, "end": 1677.28, "text": " S, is institutional friction. The disorder, the market forces, the external chaos pushing against the", "tokens": [51321, 318, 11, 307, 18391, 17710, 13, 440, 13399, 11, 264, 2142, 5874, 11, 264, 8320, 14158, 7380, 1970, 264, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293240012703361, "compression_ratio": 1.6745098039215687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234849836010978e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 167728, "start": 1677.28, "end": 1682.08, "text": " boundaries of the institution. And the paper models institutions as thermodynamic spheres,", "tokens": [50365, 13180, 295, 264, 7818, 13, 400, 264, 3035, 5245, 8142, 382, 8810, 34988, 41225, 11, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09550107849968804, "compression_ratio": 1.7077464788732395, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736302436096365e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 167728, "start": 1682.08, "end": 1686.96, "text": " thus sphere pop mechanics. Yes. Think of an institution, whether it's a small startup,", "tokens": [50605, 8807, 16687, 1665, 12939, 13, 1079, 13, 6557, 295, 364, 7818, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 257, 1359, 18578, 11, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09550107849968804, "compression_ratio": 1.7077464788732395, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736302436096365e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 167728, "start": 1686.96, "end": 1692.6399999999999, "text": " a university, or a nation state, as a bounded sphere of scalar coherence, trying its best to resist the", "tokens": [50849, 257, 5454, 11, 420, 257, 4790, 1785, 11, 382, 257, 37498, 16687, 295, 39684, 26528, 655, 11, 1382, 1080, 1151, 281, 4597, 264, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09550107849968804, "compression_ratio": 1.7077464788732395, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736302436096365e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 167728, "start": 1692.6399999999999, "end": 1698.16, "text": " ambient entropy of the world. Trying not to fall apart. Exactly. And Flixian details a fascinating", "tokens": [51133, 22997, 30867, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 20180, 406, 281, 2100, 4936, 13, 7587, 13, 400, 3235, 970, 952, 4365, 257, 10343, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09550107849968804, "compression_ratio": 1.7077464788732395, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736302436096365e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 167728, "start": 1698.16, "end": 1703.84, "text": " specific mechanic regarding how these spheres interact, particularly when they try to merge. Mergers and", "tokens": [51409, 2685, 23860, 8595, 577, 613, 41225, 4648, 11, 4098, 562, 436, 853, 281, 22183, 13, 6124, 9458, 293, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09550107849968804, "compression_ratio": 1.7077464788732395, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736302436096365e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 170384, "start": 1703.84, "end": 1709.36, "text": " acquisitions, but explained through physics. Exactly. Think about when two massive companies", "tokens": [50365, 17883, 2451, 11, 457, 8825, 807, 10649, 13, 7587, 13, 6557, 466, 562, 732, 5994, 3431, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10022280432961204, "compression_ratio": 1.5381679389312977, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966051381659078e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 170384, "start": 1709.36, "end": 1716.3999999999999, "text": " try to merge. According to Sphere Pop Calculus, they only successfully integrate if the thermodynamic", "tokens": [50641, 853, 281, 22183, 13, 7328, 281, 318, 6605, 10215, 3511, 36002, 11, 436, 787, 10727, 13365, 498, 264, 8810, 34988, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10022280432961204, "compression_ratio": 1.5381679389312977, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966051381659078e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 170384, "start": 1716.3999999999999, "end": 1722.8799999999999, "text": " pressure, the external entropy, the market forces demanding efficiency, overcomes a specific internal", "tokens": [50993, 3321, 11, 264, 8320, 30867, 11, 264, 2142, 5874, 19960, 10493, 11, 670, 9055, 257, 2685, 6920, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10022280432961204, "compression_ratio": 1.5381679389312977, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966051381659078e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 170384, "start": 1722.8799999999999, "end": 1730.3999999999999, "text": " metric that Flixian terms ritual resistance, denoted as R sub T. Ritual resistance. I absolutely love that", "tokens": [51317, 20678, 300, 3235, 970, 952, 2115, 13792, 7335, 11, 1441, 23325, 382, 497, 1422, 314, 13, 497, 270, 901, 7335, 13, 286, 3122, 959, 300, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10022280432961204, "compression_ratio": 1.5381679389312977, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966051381659078e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 173040, "start": 1730.4, "end": 1735.44, "text": " term. So ritual acts as a hardening agent for the boundary of the institutional sphere.", "tokens": [50365, 1433, 13, 407, 13792, 10672, 382, 257, 1152, 4559, 9461, 337, 264, 12866, 295, 264, 18391, 16687, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07000458941740148, "compression_ratio": 1.7683823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 2.9035599879295715e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 173040, "start": 1736.0, "end": 1740.0800000000002, "text": " How does that work mechanically? Think of ritual resistance like surface tension on a droplet", "tokens": [50645, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 4236, 984, 30, 6557, 295, 13792, 7335, 411, 3753, 8980, 322, 257, 3789, 14657, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07000458941740148, "compression_ratio": 1.7683823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 2.9035599879295715e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 173040, "start": 1740.0800000000002, "end": 1745.1200000000001, "text": " of water, but for bureaucracy. Surface tension for bureaucracy. The paper mathematically shows that", "tokens": [50849, 295, 1281, 11, 457, 337, 44671, 13, 36052, 8980, 337, 44671, 13, 440, 3035, 44003, 3110, 300, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07000458941740148, "compression_ratio": 1.7683823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 2.9035599879295715e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 173040, "start": 1745.1200000000001, "end": 1750.48, "text": " ritual resistance grows logarithmically to counter entropy. Every meeting that could have been an email,", "tokens": [51101, 13792, 7335, 13156, 41473, 32674, 984, 281, 5682, 30867, 13, 2048, 3440, 300, 727, 362, 668, 364, 3796, 11, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07000458941740148, "compression_ratio": 1.7683823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 2.9035599879295715e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 173040, "start": 1750.48, "end": 1755.1200000000001, "text": " every bureaucratic form that must be filed in triplicate, every traditional corporate retreat,", "tokens": [51369, 633, 26360, 25198, 1254, 300, 1633, 312, 18789, 294, 1376, 4770, 473, 11, 633, 5164, 10896, 15505, 11, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07000458941740148, "compression_ratio": 1.7683823529411764, "no_speech_prob": 2.9035599879295715e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 175512, "start": 1755.12, "end": 1760.8799999999999, "text": " every arbitrary approval process. These are rituals. The things everyone hates doing. Yes, they are", "tokens": [50365, 633, 23211, 13317, 1399, 13, 1981, 366, 29082, 13, 440, 721, 1518, 23000, 884, 13, 1079, 11, 436, 366, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07251648420698187, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 2.3433793967797545e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 175512, "start": 1760.8799999999999, "end": 1768.2399999999998, "text": " nonproductive actions that cost energy to perform. But that energy isn't wasted. It hardens the boundary", "tokens": [50653, 2107, 14314, 20221, 5909, 300, 2063, 2281, 281, 2042, 13, 583, 300, 2281, 1943, 380, 19496, 13, 467, 1152, 694, 264, 12866, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07251648420698187, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 2.3433793967797545e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 175512, "start": 1768.2399999999998, "end": 1773.84, "text": " of the institutional sphere. So it serves a purpose. It creates surface tension that prevents the internal", "tokens": [51021, 295, 264, 18391, 16687, 13, 407, 309, 13451, 257, 4334, 13, 467, 7829, 3753, 8980, 300, 22367, 264, 6920, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07251648420698187, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 2.3433793967797545e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 175512, "start": 1773.84, "end": 1781.12, "text": " configuration, the Phi, from being easily overwritten by external chaos. It's basically an institutional", "tokens": [51301, 11694, 11, 264, 41435, 11, 490, 885, 3612, 670, 26859, 538, 8320, 14158, 13, 467, 311, 1936, 364, 18391, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07251648420698187, "compression_ratio": 1.6377952755905512, "no_speech_prob": 2.3433793967797545e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 178112, "start": 1781.12, "end": 1786.9599999999998, "text": " immune system. It keeps the outside world from messing up the inside rules. But I imagine it also prevents", "tokens": [50365, 11992, 1185, 13, 467, 5965, 264, 2380, 1002, 490, 23258, 493, 264, 1854, 4474, 13, 583, 286, 3811, 309, 611, 22367, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08145040512084961, "compression_ratio": 1.5415162454873645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652294114963498e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 178112, "start": 1786.9599999999998, "end": 1792.1599999999999, "text": " the institution from changing. Yes, it absolutely does. So let's look at a real-world example through", "tokens": [50657, 264, 7818, 490, 4473, 13, 1079, 11, 309, 3122, 775, 13, 407, 718, 311, 574, 412, 257, 957, 12, 13217, 1365, 807, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08145040512084961, "compression_ratio": 1.5415162454873645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652294114963498e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 178112, "start": 1792.1599999999999, "end": 1800.1599999999999, "text": " this lens. Take the infamous AOL-Time Warner merger in the early 2000s. Ah, a classic disaster. Often cited as", "tokens": [50917, 341, 6765, 13, 3664, 264, 30769, 316, 5046, 12, 22233, 31769, 48002, 294, 264, 2440, 8132, 82, 13, 2438, 11, 257, 7230, 11293, 13, 20043, 30134, 382, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08145040512084961, "compression_ratio": 1.5415162454873645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652294114963498e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 178112, "start": 1800.1599999999999, "end": 1806.56, "text": " one of the worst corporate integrations in history. The external market forces, the thermodynamic pressure,", "tokens": [51317, 472, 295, 264, 5855, 10896, 3572, 763, 294, 2503, 13, 440, 8320, 2142, 5874, 11, 264, 8810, 34988, 3321, 11, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08145040512084961, "compression_ratio": 1.5415162454873645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652294114963498e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 180656, "start": 1806.56, "end": 1810.8799999999999, "text": " dictated that they should merge. Yeah, the internet was booming. Media was changing. Right. It made", "tokens": [50365, 12569, 770, 300, 436, 820, 22183, 13, 865, 11, 264, 4705, 390, 45883, 13, 14741, 390, 4473, 13, 1779, 13, 467, 1027, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08368870128284801, "compression_ratio": 1.6433333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275410702649596e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 180656, "start": 1810.8799999999999, "end": 1815.6, "text": " absolute financial sense to combine the spheres. But the internal cultures were wildly different.", "tokens": [50581, 8236, 4669, 2020, 281, 10432, 264, 41225, 13, 583, 264, 6920, 12951, 645, 34731, 819, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08368870128284801, "compression_ratio": 1.6433333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275410702649596e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 180656, "start": 1815.6, "end": 1821.6799999999998, "text": " AOL was this fast-moving, aggressive internet company, and Time Warner was a traditional slow-moving", "tokens": [50817, 316, 5046, 390, 341, 2370, 12, 3280, 798, 11, 10762, 4705, 2237, 11, 293, 6161, 31769, 390, 257, 5164, 2964, 12, 3280, 798, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08368870128284801, "compression_ratio": 1.6433333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275410702649596e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 180656, "start": 1821.6799999999998, "end": 1828.72, "text": " legacy media conglomerate. Exactly. Their internal rituals, their specific ways of operating,", "tokens": [51121, 11711, 3021, 416, 7191, 14301, 473, 13, 7587, 13, 6710, 6920, 29082, 11, 641, 2685, 2098, 295, 7447, 11, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08368870128284801, "compression_ratio": 1.6433333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275410702649596e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 180656, "start": 1828.72, "end": 1835.52, "text": " communicating, and approving decisions, were deeply entrenched. Their ritual resistance was massive.", "tokens": [51473, 17559, 11, 293, 2075, 798, 5327, 11, 645, 8760, 948, 42388, 13, 6710, 13792, 7335, 390, 5994, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08368870128284801, "compression_ratio": 1.6433333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7275410702649596e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 183552, "start": 1835.52, "end": 1840.4, "text": " So they were like two hard marbles. So when they tried to push the two spheres together,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 645, 411, 732, 1152, 1849, 8806, 13, 407, 562, 436, 3031, 281, 2944, 264, 732, 41225, 1214, 11, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08336765249979865, "compression_ratio": 1.7602996254681649, "no_speech_prob": 2.2530970145151485e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 183552, "start": 1840.4, "end": 1845.68, "text": " the thermodynamic pressure of the market couldn't overcome the boundary hardened by that surface tension.", "tokens": [50609, 264, 8810, 34988, 3321, 295, 264, 2142, 2809, 380, 10473, 264, 12866, 42605, 538, 300, 3753, 8980, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08336765249979865, "compression_ratio": 1.7602996254681649, "no_speech_prob": 2.2530970145151485e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 183552, "start": 1845.68, "end": 1850.6399999999999, "text": " They just couldn't break through. The equations of sphere pop calculus show that if the gradient", "tokens": [50873, 814, 445, 2809, 380, 1821, 807, 13, 440, 11787, 295, 16687, 1665, 33400, 855, 300, 498, 264, 16235, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08336765249979865, "compression_ratio": 1.7602996254681649, "no_speech_prob": 2.2530970145151485e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 183552, "start": 1850.6399999999999, "end": 1855.44, "text": " of the external entropy field cannot overcome the internal scalar boundary constraint,", "tokens": [51121, 295, 264, 8320, 30867, 2519, 2644, 10473, 264, 6920, 39684, 12866, 25534, 11, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08336765249979865, "compression_ratio": 1.7602996254681649, "no_speech_prob": 2.2530970145151485e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 183552, "start": 1856.08, "end": 1861.52, "text": " the variables simply do not integrate. The merger failed. The spheres literally bounced off", "tokens": [51393, 264, 9102, 2935, 360, 406, 13365, 13, 440, 48002, 7612, 13, 440, 41225, 3736, 46482, 766, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08336765249979865, "compression_ratio": 1.7602996254681649, "no_speech_prob": 2.2530970145151485e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 186152, "start": 1861.52, "end": 1865.84, "text": " each other instead of combining. And they shed massive amounts of energy. In this case, billions", "tokens": [50365, 1184, 661, 2602, 295, 21928, 13, 400, 436, 14951, 5994, 11663, 295, 2281, 13, 682, 341, 1389, 11, 17375, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058387263615926104, "compression_ratio": 1.613821138211382, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279165294772914e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 186152, "start": 1865.84, "end": 1871.28, "text": " of dollars in the process. Because the math is the same. The RSVP equations don't care if it's two", "tokens": [50581, 295, 3808, 294, 264, 1399, 13, 1436, 264, 5221, 307, 264, 912, 13, 440, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 500, 380, 1127, 498, 309, 311, 732, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058387263615926104, "compression_ratio": 1.613821138211382, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279165294772914e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 186152, "start": 1871.28, "end": 1876.8799999999999, "text": " droplets of water failing to mix due to surface tension, two galaxies failing to merge their dark", "tokens": [50853, 41573, 295, 1281, 18223, 281, 2890, 3462, 281, 3753, 8980, 11, 732, 28755, 18223, 281, 22183, 641, 2877, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058387263615926104, "compression_ratio": 1.613821138211382, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279165294772914e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 186152, "start": 1876.8799999999999, "end": 1883.12, "text": " matter halos, or two multinational corporations failing to merge because their HR departments hate each", "tokens": [51133, 1871, 7523, 329, 11, 420, 732, 45872, 1478, 17676, 18223, 281, 22183, 570, 641, 19460, 15326, 4700, 1184, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058387263615926104, "compression_ratio": 1.613821138211382, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279165294772914e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 188312, "start": 1883.12, "end": 1888.08, "text": " other. It's the same failure of thermodynamic integration. It is identically the same physics.", "tokens": [50365, 661, 13, 467, 311, 264, 912, 7763, 295, 8810, 34988, 10980, 13, 467, 307, 2473, 984, 264, 912, 10649, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07353696417301259, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 2.3065577225978018e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 188312, "start": 1889.1999999999998, "end": 1893.84, "text": " Okay, this brings us to what I think is the most profound part of the monographs. Whether it's a", "tokens": [50669, 1033, 11, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 286, 519, 307, 264, 881, 14382, 644, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 82, 13, 8503, 309, 311, 257, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07353696417301259, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 2.3065577225978018e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 188312, "start": 1893.84, "end": 1899.52, "text": " supernova throwing out carbon but holding on to oxygen, or a brain forming a new memory to reduce", "tokens": [50901, 1687, 39486, 10238, 484, 5954, 457, 5061, 322, 281, 9169, 11, 420, 257, 3567, 15745, 257, 777, 4675, 281, 5407, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07353696417301259, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 2.3065577225978018e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 188312, "start": 1899.52, "end": 1906.3999999999999, "text": " surprise, or an institution hardening its rituals to survive a market crash. These systems all step forward", "tokens": [51185, 6365, 11, 420, 364, 7818, 1152, 4559, 1080, 29082, 281, 7867, 257, 2142, 8252, 13, 1981, 3652, 439, 1823, 2128, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07353696417301259, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 2.3065577225978018e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 190640, "start": 1906.4, "end": 1912.4, "text": " in time, and they never step backward. You can't unring a bell, you can't unexplode a star, you can't", "tokens": [50365, 294, 565, 11, 293, 436, 1128, 1823, 23897, 13, 509, 393, 380, 517, 2937, 257, 4549, 11, 291, 393, 380, 11572, 564, 1429, 257, 3543, 11, 291, 393, 380, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10056268362174357, "compression_ratio": 1.6366559485530547, "no_speech_prob": 1.560722254559388e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 190640, "start": 1912.4, "end": 1918.96, "text": " unmerge a company. We all intuitively accept that time flows in one direction, but why? That is the", "tokens": [50665, 517, 936, 432, 257, 2237, 13, 492, 439, 46506, 3241, 300, 565, 12867, 294, 472, 3513, 11, 457, 983, 30, 663, 307, 264, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10056268362174357, "compression_ratio": 1.6366559485530547, "no_speech_prob": 1.560722254559388e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 190640, "start": 1918.96, "end": 1924.8000000000002, "text": " deepest, most persistent question in physics. Why is there an arrow of time if the fundamental equations", "tokens": [50993, 28288, 11, 881, 24315, 1168, 294, 10649, 13, 1545, 307, 456, 364, 11610, 295, 565, 498, 264, 8088, 11787, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10056268362174357, "compression_ratio": 1.6366559485530547, "no_speech_prob": 1.560722254559388e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 190640, "start": 1924.8000000000002, "end": 1929.76, "text": " of quantum mechanics are time-reversible? Because they are reversible, right, at the micro level. Yes.", "tokens": [51285, 295, 13018, 12939, 366, 565, 12, 265, 840, 964, 30, 1436, 436, 366, 44788, 11, 558, 11, 412, 264, 4532, 1496, 13, 1079, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10056268362174357, "compression_ratio": 1.6366559485530547, "no_speech_prob": 1.560722254559388e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 190640, "start": 1929.76, "end": 1935.92, "text": " The RSVP plenum tackles this head-on. And Flixian proves the arrow of time mathematically through a", "tokens": [51533, 440, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 9426, 904, 341, 1378, 12, 266, 13, 400, 3235, 970, 952, 25019, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 44003, 807, 257, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10056268362174357, "compression_ratio": 1.6366559485530547, "no_speech_prob": 1.560722254559388e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 193592, "start": 1935.92, "end": 1940.8000000000002, "text": " concept called the adjunction defect. The adjunction defect. This is where we prove why time only", "tokens": [50365, 3410, 1219, 264, 614, 10010, 882, 16445, 13, 440, 614, 10010, 882, 16445, 13, 639, 307, 689, 321, 7081, 983, 565, 787, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043368637561798096, "compression_ratio": 1.7253521126760563, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796912389287598e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 193592, "start": 1940.8000000000002, "end": 1945.92, "text": " moved forward. Let's dig into this. To do this, Flixian introduces what category theorists call", "tokens": [50609, 4259, 2128, 13, 961, 311, 2528, 666, 341, 13, 1407, 360, 341, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 31472, 437, 7719, 27423, 1751, 818, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043368637561798096, "compression_ratio": 1.7253521126760563, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796912389287598e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 193592, "start": 1945.92, "end": 1952.88, "text": " a variational adjunction. It is a relationship between two spaces. The continuous fluid reality", "tokens": [50865, 257, 3034, 1478, 614, 10010, 882, 13, 467, 307, 257, 2480, 1296, 732, 7673, 13, 440, 10957, 9113, 4103, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043368637561798096, "compression_ratio": 1.7253521126760563, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796912389287598e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 193592, "start": 1952.88, "end": 1958.8000000000002, "text": " of the RSVP fields, which is the whole truth, and the discrete observable history space, which are the", "tokens": [51213, 295, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 7909, 11, 597, 307, 264, 1379, 3494, 11, 293, 264, 27706, 9951, 712, 2503, 1901, 11, 597, 366, 264, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043368637561798096, "compression_ratio": 1.7253521126760563, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796912389287598e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 193592, "start": 1958.8000000000002, "end": 1963.8400000000001, "text": " measurable events. The fluid versus the snapshots. To move between these two, Flixian defines two", "tokens": [51509, 43615, 3931, 13, 440, 9113, 5717, 264, 19206, 27495, 13, 1407, 1286, 1296, 613, 732, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 23122, 732, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.043368637561798096, "compression_ratio": 1.7253521126760563, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796912389287598e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 196384, "start": 1963.84, "end": 1970.1599999999999, "text": " mathematical operators. First, the discretization functor, which we'll call F. Second, the reconstruction", "tokens": [50365, 18894, 19077, 13, 2386, 11, 264, 25656, 2144, 1019, 1672, 11, 597, 321, 603, 818, 479, 13, 5736, 11, 264, 31565, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07399189124986963, "compression_ratio": 1.5852713178294573, "no_speech_prob": 1.8317946985646483e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 196384, "start": 1970.1599999999999, "end": 1975.1999999999998, "text": " operator, which we'll call G. Let's ground this so we don't get lost in the math. Take us back to LAP", "tokens": [50681, 12973, 11, 597, 321, 603, 818, 460, 13, 961, 311, 2727, 341, 370, 321, 500, 380, 483, 2731, 294, 264, 5221, 13, 3664, 505, 646, 281, 441, 4715, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07399189124986963, "compression_ratio": 1.5852713178294573, "no_speech_prob": 1.8317946985646483e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 196384, "start": 1975.1999999999998, "end": 1981.04, "text": " 1B and that faint population third supernova. The star explodes, the oxygen falls back into the black", "tokens": [50933, 502, 33, 293, 300, 21104, 4415, 2636, 1687, 39486, 13, 440, 3543, 42610, 11, 264, 9169, 8804, 646, 666, 264, 2211, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07399189124986963, "compression_ratio": 1.5852713178294573, "no_speech_prob": 1.8317946985646483e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 196384, "start": 1981.04, "end": 1987.84, "text": " hole, the carbon escapes. Flixian categorizes this specific, irreversible moment as a refuse event.", "tokens": [51225, 5458, 11, 264, 5954, 43769, 13, 3235, 970, 952, 19250, 5660, 341, 2685, 11, 16014, 840, 964, 1623, 382, 257, 16791, 2280, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07399189124986963, "compression_ratio": 1.5852713178294573, "no_speech_prob": 1.8317946985646483e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 198784, "start": 1987.84, "end": 1994.0, "text": " Yes. A refuse event is a critical operator in this framework. Imagine two completely different", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 316, 16791, 2280, 307, 257, 4924, 12973, 294, 341, 8388, 13, 11739, 732, 2584, 819, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05887105373235849, "compression_ratio": 1.7093425605536332, "no_speech_prob": 1.335449003984912e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 198784, "start": 1994.0, "end": 1999.12, "text": " continuous trajectories in the fluid of reality. Two different stars, maybe with slightly different", "tokens": [50673, 10957, 18257, 2083, 294, 264, 9113, 295, 4103, 13, 4453, 819, 6105, 11, 1310, 365, 4748, 819, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05887105373235849, "compression_ratio": 1.7093425605536332, "no_speech_prob": 1.335449003984912e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 198784, "start": 1999.12, "end": 2004.72, "text": " internal densities, but they arrive at the exact same instantaneous state at time t0. So if you pause", "tokens": [50929, 6920, 24505, 1088, 11, 457, 436, 8881, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 45596, 1785, 412, 565, 256, 15, 13, 407, 498, 291, 10465, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05887105373235849, "compression_ratio": 1.7093425605536332, "no_speech_prob": 1.335449003984912e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 198784, "start": 2004.72, "end": 2009.9199999999998, "text": " the universe right now, they look identical. They look identical. But because of a hidden historical", "tokens": [51209, 264, 6445, 558, 586, 11, 436, 574, 14800, 13, 814, 574, 14800, 13, 583, 570, 295, 257, 7633, 8584, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05887105373235849, "compression_ratio": 1.7093425605536332, "no_speech_prob": 1.335449003984912e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 198784, "start": 2009.9199999999998, "end": 2016.0, "text": " constraint, a difference in how they got to that state 1 trajectory has its forward continuation", "tokens": [51469, 25534, 11, 257, 2649, 294, 577, 436, 658, 281, 300, 1785, 502, 21512, 575, 1080, 2128, 29357, 51773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05887105373235849, "compression_ratio": 1.7093425605536332, "no_speech_prob": 1.335449003984912e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 201600, "start": 2016.0, "end": 2021.68, "text": " dynamically blocked. Look like oxygen falling back. Exactly. The oxygen is sucked back in. It is", "tokens": [50365, 43492, 15470, 13, 2053, 411, 9169, 7440, 646, 13, 7587, 13, 440, 9169, 307, 26503, 646, 294, 13, 467, 307, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08244044522205031, "compression_ratio": 1.6623931623931625, "no_speech_prob": 2.028031605497138e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 201600, "start": 2021.68, "end": 2028.96, "text": " refused entry into the future state space. So even if two things look absolutely identical in the", "tokens": [50649, 14654, 8729, 666, 264, 2027, 1785, 1901, 13, 407, 754, 498, 732, 721, 574, 3122, 14800, 294, 264, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08244044522205031, "compression_ratio": 1.6623931623931625, "no_speech_prob": 2.028031605497138e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 201600, "start": 2028.96, "end": 2034.72, "text": " present moment, their admissible futures can be entirely different based purely on their hidden", "tokens": [51013, 1974, 1623, 11, 641, 5910, 41073, 26071, 393, 312, 7696, 819, 2361, 17491, 322, 641, 7633, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08244044522205031, "compression_ratio": 1.6623931623931625, "no_speech_prob": 2.028031605497138e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 201600, "start": 2034.72, "end": 2041.52, "text": " history. Exactly. The paper states identity is history. It proves that any state-based observation", "tokens": [51301, 2503, 13, 7587, 13, 440, 3035, 4368, 6575, 307, 2503, 13, 467, 25019, 300, 604, 1785, 12, 6032, 14816, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08244044522205031, "compression_ratio": 1.6623931623931625, "no_speech_prob": 2.028031605497138e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 204152, "start": 2041.52, "end": 2046.6399999999999, "text": " looking at the system only as it is right now, without access to its entire past trajectory,", "tokens": [50365, 1237, 412, 264, 1185, 787, 382, 309, 307, 558, 586, 11, 1553, 2105, 281, 1080, 2302, 1791, 21512, 11, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08950163091270669, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.579451847089075e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 204152, "start": 2046.6399999999999, "end": 2051.6, "text": " is fundamentally flawed. Because you're missing the whole picture. The discretization functor,", "tokens": [50621, 307, 17879, 38823, 13, 1436, 291, 434, 5361, 264, 1379, 3036, 13, 440, 25656, 2144, 1019, 1672, 11, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08950163091270669, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.579451847089075e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 204152, "start": 2051.6, "end": 2057.28, "text": " f, is the mathematical process of taking that continuous, infinitely complex historical reality", "tokens": [50869, 283, 11, 307, 264, 18894, 1399, 295, 1940, 300, 10957, 11, 36227, 3997, 8584, 4103, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08950163091270669, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.579451847089075e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 204152, "start": 2057.28, "end": 2062.8, "text": " and projecting it into a finite, discrete set of measurable features. It's taking the messy continuum", "tokens": [51153, 293, 43001, 309, 666, 257, 19362, 11, 27706, 992, 295, 43615, 4122, 13, 467, 311, 1940, 264, 16191, 36120, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08950163091270669, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.579451847089075e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 204152, "start": 2062.8, "end": 2067.44, "text": " and forcing it into clean data points. That's precisely what it does. Let me try a technological", "tokens": [51429, 293, 19030, 309, 666, 2541, 1412, 2793, 13, 663, 311, 13402, 437, 309, 775, 13, 961, 385, 853, 257, 18439, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08950163091270669, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.579451847089075e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 206744, "start": 2067.44, "end": 2074.08, "text": " analogy here to explain f and g. Imagine I have a massive, uncompressed, ultra-high-resolution,", "tokens": [50365, 21663, 510, 281, 2903, 283, 293, 290, 13, 11739, 286, 362, 257, 5994, 11, 8585, 79, 3805, 11, 14808, 12, 21454, 12, 495, 3386, 11, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12410851950957397, "compression_ratio": 1.5378486055776892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652261588898323e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 206744, "start": 2074.08, "end": 2081.6, "text": " raw photograph file. It has billions of colors, infinite light data. That is the continuous reality.", "tokens": [50697, 8936, 8348, 3991, 13, 467, 575, 17375, 295, 4577, 11, 13785, 1442, 1412, 13, 663, 307, 264, 10957, 4103, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12410851950957397, "compression_ratio": 1.5378486055776892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652261588898323e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 206744, "start": 2081.6, "end": 2085.44, "text": " Okay, I see where you're going. But I need to email it to you, and the file is too big.", "tokens": [51073, 1033, 11, 286, 536, 689, 291, 434, 516, 13, 583, 286, 643, 281, 3796, 309, 281, 291, 11, 293, 264, 3991, 307, 886, 955, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12410851950957397, "compression_ratio": 1.5378486055776892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652261588898323e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 206744, "start": 2086.0, "end": 2092.32, "text": " So I apply the discretization map, f, I compress it into a low-quality jpeg, I throw away millions of", "tokens": [51293, 407, 286, 3079, 264, 25656, 2144, 4471, 11, 283, 11, 286, 14778, 309, 666, 257, 2295, 12, 11286, 361, 494, 70, 11, 286, 3507, 1314, 6803, 295, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12410851950957397, "compression_ratio": 1.5378486055776892, "no_speech_prob": 1.9652261588898323e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 209232, "start": 2092.32, "end": 2097.92, "text": " pixels, I average out the colors, I discretize the data to fit the constraint of the email attachment.", "tokens": [50365, 18668, 11, 286, 4274, 484, 264, 4577, 11, 286, 25656, 1125, 264, 1412, 281, 3318, 264, 25534, 295, 264, 3796, 19431, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07784283711360052, "compression_ratio": 1.6337579617834395, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540839677485649e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 209232, "start": 2097.92, "end": 2103.2000000000003, "text": " A perfect parallel for what observation does to physical reality. And then you receive the jpeg,", "tokens": [50645, 316, 2176, 8952, 337, 437, 14816, 775, 281, 4001, 4103, 13, 400, 550, 291, 4774, 264, 361, 494, 70, 11, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07784283711360052, "compression_ratio": 1.6337579617834395, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540839677485649e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 209232, "start": 2103.2000000000003, "end": 2109.6800000000003, "text": " and you have a super-advanced AI, the reconstruction operator, G. You ask the AI to look at that low-quality", "tokens": [50909, 293, 291, 362, 257, 1687, 12, 345, 85, 4864, 7318, 11, 264, 31565, 12973, 11, 460, 13, 509, 1029, 264, 7318, 281, 574, 412, 300, 2295, 12, 11286, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07784283711360052, "compression_ratio": 1.6337579617834395, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540839677485649e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 209232, "start": 2109.6800000000003, "end": 2115.04, "text": " jpeg, and guess what the original raw file looked like? To upscale it back to reality. Which AIs are", "tokens": [51233, 361, 494, 70, 11, 293, 2041, 437, 264, 3380, 8936, 3991, 2956, 411, 30, 1407, 493, 20033, 309, 646, 281, 4103, 13, 3013, 316, 6802, 366, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07784283711360052, "compression_ratio": 1.6337579617834395, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540839677485649e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 209232, "start": 2115.04, "end": 2120.56, "text": " getting very good at. Right. The AI can make a mathematically brilliant guess based on the data it has,", "tokens": [51501, 1242, 588, 665, 412, 13, 1779, 13, 440, 7318, 393, 652, 257, 44003, 10248, 2041, 2361, 322, 264, 1412, 309, 575, 11, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07784283711360052, "compression_ratio": 1.6337579617834395, "no_speech_prob": 1.2540839677485649e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 212056, "start": 2120.56, "end": 2125.7599999999998, "text": " optimizing its loss function perfectly. It can generate a beautiful high-res image. But no", "tokens": [50365, 40425, 1080, 4470, 2445, 6239, 13, 467, 393, 8460, 257, 2238, 1090, 12, 495, 3256, 13, 583, 572, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0761026382446289, "compression_ratio": 1.6047297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3827222786894078e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 212056, "start": 2125.7599999999998, "end": 2131.2799999999997, "text": " matter how good the AI is, it can never ever recreate the exact original raw file. The lost", "tokens": [50625, 1871, 577, 665, 264, 7318, 307, 11, 309, 393, 1128, 1562, 25833, 264, 1900, 3380, 8936, 3991, 13, 440, 2731, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0761026382446289, "compression_ratio": 1.6047297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3827222786894078e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 212056, "start": 2131.2799999999997, "end": 2136.4, "text": " pixel data is forever gone. That is an exceptionally precise mechanical analogy", "tokens": [50901, 19261, 1412, 307, 5680, 2780, 13, 663, 307, 364, 37807, 13600, 12070, 21663, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0761026382446289, "compression_ratio": 1.6047297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3827222786894078e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 212056, "start": 2136.4, "end": 2143.44, "text": " for theorem 5.5.2 in the monographs. The process of taking the continuous reality, compressing it into", "tokens": [51157, 337, 20904, 1025, 13, 20, 13, 17, 294, 264, 1108, 3108, 82, 13, 440, 1399, 295, 1940, 264, 10957, 4103, 11, 14778, 278, 309, 666, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0761026382446289, "compression_ratio": 1.6047297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3827222786894078e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 212056, "start": 2143.44, "end": 2149.44, "text": " observable events with F, and then attempting to reconstruct the reality with G, creates an ontological loop.", "tokens": [51509, 9951, 712, 3931, 365, 479, 11, 293, 550, 22001, 281, 31499, 264, 4103, 365, 460, 11, 7829, 364, 6592, 4383, 6367, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0761026382446289, "compression_ratio": 1.6047297297297298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3827222786894078e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 214944, "start": 2149.44, "end": 2154.64, "text": " An ontological loop. Fliction defines this loop as the comparison map, denoted by the Greek letter", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 6592, 4383, 6367, 13, 3235, 4105, 23122, 341, 6367, 382, 264, 9660, 4471, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 264, 10281, 5063, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08774618179567399, "compression_ratio": 1.722972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829590664459772e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 214944, "start": 2154.64, "end": 2162.16, "text": " eta. The comparison map is simply the reconstruction G applied to the discretization F. Now, if no", "tokens": [50625, 32415, 13, 440, 9660, 4471, 307, 2935, 264, 31565, 460, 6456, 281, 264, 25656, 2144, 479, 13, 823, 11, 498, 572, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08774618179567399, "compression_ratio": 1.722972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829590664459772e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 214944, "start": 2162.16, "end": 2167.04, "text": " information was ever lost, the comparison map would just be a perfect identity map. You get out exactly", "tokens": [51001, 1589, 390, 1562, 2731, 11, 264, 9660, 4471, 576, 445, 312, 257, 2176, 6575, 4471, 13, 509, 483, 484, 2293, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08774618179567399, "compression_ratio": 1.722972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829590664459772e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 214944, "start": 2167.04, "end": 2171.44, "text": " what you put in. Like unzipping a file and getting the exact original back. Right. But the math proves", "tokens": [51245, 437, 291, 829, 294, 13, 1743, 517, 89, 6297, 257, 3991, 293, 1242, 264, 1900, 3380, 646, 13, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 5221, 25019, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08774618179567399, "compression_ratio": 1.722972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829590664459772e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 214944, "start": 2171.44, "end": 2176.88, "text": " that's impossible. The paper has a no-go theorem. And what does that state? The no-go theorem proves that", "tokens": [51465, 300, 311, 6243, 13, 440, 3035, 575, 257, 572, 12, 1571, 20904, 13, 400, 437, 775, 300, 1785, 30, 440, 572, 12, 1571, 20904, 25019, 300, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08774618179567399, "compression_ratio": 1.722972972972973, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829590664459772e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 217688, "start": 2176.88, "end": 2182.48, "text": " perfect reconstruction is structurally impossible. For any finite feature map acting on an infinite", "tokens": [50365, 2176, 31565, 307, 6594, 6512, 6243, 13, 1171, 604, 19362, 4111, 4471, 6577, 322, 364, 13785, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06634521484375, "compression_ratio": 1.7577092511013215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4718980157965578e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 217688, "start": 2182.48, "end": 2189.04, "text": " dimensional configuration space, the discretization map F is what mathematicians call non-injective.", "tokens": [50645, 18795, 11694, 1901, 11, 264, 25656, 2144, 4471, 479, 307, 437, 32811, 2567, 818, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06634521484375, "compression_ratio": 1.7577092511013215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4718980157965578e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 217688, "start": 2189.04, "end": 2193.6, "text": " Meaning multiple different inputs mapped to the same output. Right. Multiple different starting", "tokens": [50973, 19948, 3866, 819, 15743, 33318, 281, 264, 912, 5598, 13, 1779, 13, 40056, 819, 2891, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06634521484375, "compression_ratio": 1.7577092511013215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4718980157965578e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 217688, "start": 2193.6, "end": 2198.48, "text": " realities can result in the exact same compressed JPEG. Multiple different histories can result in the", "tokens": [51201, 27785, 393, 1874, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 30353, 508, 5208, 38, 13, 40056, 819, 30631, 393, 1874, 294, 264, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06634521484375, "compression_ratio": 1.7577092511013215, "no_speech_prob": 1.4718980157965578e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 219848, "start": 2198.48, "end": 2204.32, "text": " exact same present state. So when the AI or the reconstruction operator G tries to recreate the", "tokens": [50365, 1900, 912, 1974, 1785, 13, 407, 562, 264, 7318, 420, 264, 31565, 12973, 460, 9898, 281, 25833, 264, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08002765973409016, "compression_ratio": 1.652542372881356, "no_speech_prob": 2.280500874946023e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 219848, "start": 2204.32, "end": 2210.72, "text": " past, it encounters a fundamental ambiguity. It has to pick a single canonical representative", "tokens": [50657, 1791, 11, 309, 26310, 257, 8088, 46519, 13, 467, 575, 281, 1888, 257, 2167, 46491, 12424, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08002765973409016, "compression_ratio": 1.652542372881356, "no_speech_prob": 2.280500874946023e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 219848, "start": 2210.72, "end": 2217.68, "text": " out of many possibilities. It is forced to guess. And the mathematical difference between the true", "tokens": [50977, 484, 295, 867, 12178, 13, 467, 307, 7579, 281, 2041, 13, 400, 264, 18894, 2649, 1296, 264, 2074, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08002765973409016, "compression_ratio": 1.652542372881356, "no_speech_prob": 2.280500874946023e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 219848, "start": 2217.68, "end": 2223.68, "text": " original continuous reality and the reconstructed guess is called the reconstruction defect or delta.", "tokens": [51325, 3380, 10957, 4103, 293, 264, 31499, 292, 2041, 307, 1219, 264, 31565, 16445, 420, 8289, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08002765973409016, "compression_ratio": 1.652542372881356, "no_speech_prob": 2.280500874946023e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 222368, "start": 2223.68, "end": 2230.0, "text": " The adjunction defect. The adjunction defect. Wow. Yes. And here is the monumental paradigm", "tokens": [50365, 440, 614, 10010, 882, 16445, 13, 440, 614, 10010, 882, 16445, 13, 3153, 13, 1079, 13, 400, 510, 307, 264, 43105, 24709, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09534922961531014, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968842118051056e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 222368, "start": 2230.0, "end": 2235.9199999999996, "text": " shifting conclusion affliction's work. Irreversibility, the fact that time only moves forward,", "tokens": [50681, 17573, 10063, 2096, 75, 4105, 311, 589, 13, 9151, 265, 840, 2841, 11, 264, 1186, 300, 565, 787, 6067, 2128, 11, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09534922961531014, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968842118051056e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 222368, "start": 2235.9199999999996, "end": 2241.2, "text": " is not just a phenomenological gloss. It's not just how we feel it. We don't just experience time", "tokens": [50977, 307, 406, 445, 257, 9388, 4383, 19574, 13, 467, 311, 406, 445, 577, 321, 841, 309, 13, 492, 500, 380, 445, 1752, 565, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09534922961531014, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968842118051056e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 222368, "start": 2241.2, "end": 2245.44, "text": " moving forward because our brains are wired that way or because it feels like it. Time moves forward", "tokens": [51241, 2684, 2128, 570, 527, 15442, 366, 27415, 300, 636, 420, 570, 309, 3417, 411, 309, 13, 6161, 6067, 2128, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09534922961531014, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968842118051056e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 222368, "start": 2245.44, "end": 2249.9199999999996, "text": " strictly because of the structural geometric theorem about the non-invertibility reconstruction. So it's", "tokens": [51453, 20792, 570, 295, 264, 15067, 33246, 20904, 466, 264, 2107, 12, 259, 3281, 2841, 31565, 13, 407, 309, 311, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09534922961531014, "compression_ratio": 1.7132867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968842118051056e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 224992, "start": 2249.92, "end": 2255.76, "text": " built into the math. Yeah. Every single time reality moves from a continuous fluid field", "tokens": [50365, 3094, 666, 264, 5221, 13, 865, 13, 2048, 2167, 565, 4103, 6067, 490, 257, 10957, 9113, 2519, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058118042645153696, "compression_ratio": 1.6958041958041958, "no_speech_prob": 2.133659785311104e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 224992, "start": 2255.76, "end": 2261.12, "text": " into a discrete observable event, whether that's a refuse event in a collapsing star,", "tokens": [50657, 666, 257, 27706, 9951, 712, 2280, 11, 1968, 300, 311, 257, 16791, 2280, 294, 257, 45339, 3543, 11, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058118042645153696, "compression_ratio": 1.6958041958041958, "no_speech_prob": 2.133659785311104e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 224992, "start": 2261.12, "end": 2268.08, "text": " a measurement in a quantum lab, or a memory forming in your hippocampus, infinite information is squeezed", "tokens": [50925, 257, 13160, 294, 257, 13018, 2715, 11, 420, 257, 4675, 15745, 294, 428, 27745, 905, 1215, 301, 11, 13785, 1589, 307, 39470, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058118042645153696, "compression_ratio": 1.6958041958041958, "no_speech_prob": 2.133659785311104e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 224992, "start": 2268.08, "end": 2273.6800000000003, "text": " into the null space, the mathematical kernel of the discretization map. It falls out of observable", "tokens": [51273, 666, 264, 18184, 1901, 11, 264, 18894, 28256, 295, 264, 25656, 2144, 4471, 13, 467, 8804, 484, 295, 9951, 712, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058118042645153696, "compression_ratio": 1.6958041958041958, "no_speech_prob": 2.133659785311104e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 224992, "start": 2273.6800000000003, "end": 2278.96, "text": " reality forever. And the shadow of that lost information is what we call entropy. I just need a second to", "tokens": [51553, 4103, 5680, 13, 400, 264, 8576, 295, 300, 2731, 1589, 307, 437, 321, 818, 30867, 13, 286, 445, 643, 257, 1150, 281, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058118042645153696, "compression_ratio": 1.6958041958041958, "no_speech_prob": 2.133659785311104e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 227896, "start": 2278.96, "end": 2284.32, "text": " process that. Entropy isn't just random heat or chaotic jiggling of atoms. Fleck Shannon measures", "tokens": [50365, 1399, 300, 13, 3951, 27514, 1943, 380, 445, 4974, 3738, 420, 27013, 361, 24542, 295, 16871, 13, 18612, 547, 28974, 8000, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09453912809783337, "compression_ratio": 1.6778523489932886, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269223823359933e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 227896, "start": 2284.32, "end": 2289.44, "text": " this informational loss mathematically using something called the Jensen-Shannon divergence,", "tokens": [50633, 341, 49391, 4470, 44003, 1228, 746, 1219, 264, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 47387, 11, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09453912809783337, "compression_ratio": 1.6778523489932886, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269223823359933e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 227896, "start": 2289.44, "end": 2294.88, "text": " which basically calculates the distance between two probability distributions, the true reality and", "tokens": [50889, 597, 1936, 4322, 1024, 264, 4560, 1296, 732, 8482, 37870, 11, 264, 2074, 4103, 293, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09453912809783337, "compression_ratio": 1.6778523489932886, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269223823359933e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 227896, "start": 2294.88, "end": 2301.36, "text": " the compressed data. Okay. Entropy is the precise measure theoretic shadow of the irreversible loss that", "tokens": [51161, 264, 30353, 1412, 13, 1033, 13, 3951, 27514, 307, 264, 13600, 3481, 14308, 299, 8576, 295, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 4470, 300, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09453912809783337, "compression_ratio": 1.6778523489932886, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269223823359933e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 227896, "start": 2301.36, "end": 2308.16, "text": " occurs when continuous reality is forced through discrete constraints. Reality is constantly agonizingly", "tokens": [51485, 11843, 562, 10957, 4103, 307, 7579, 807, 27706, 18491, 13, 33822, 307, 6460, 623, 266, 3319, 356, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09453912809783337, "compression_ratio": 1.6778523489932886, "no_speech_prob": 1.4269223823359933e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 230816, "start": 2308.16, "end": 2313.2, "text": " shedding its own history into the defect space. And that continuous shedding is the forward arrow of", "tokens": [50365, 49934, 1080, 1065, 2503, 666, 264, 16445, 1901, 13, 400, 300, 10957, 49934, 307, 264, 2128, 11610, 295, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057788968086242676, "compression_ratio": 1.5983935742971886, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 230816, "start": 2313.2, "end": 2319.04, "text": " time. Time isn't a dimension we travel through. Time is just the exhaust of reality compressing itself", "tokens": [50617, 565, 13, 6161, 1943, 380, 257, 10139, 321, 3147, 807, 13, 6161, 307, 445, 264, 14687, 295, 4103, 14778, 278, 2564, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057788968086242676, "compression_ratio": 1.5983935742971886, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 230816, "start": 2319.04, "end": 2325.2799999999997, "text": " into observable moments. It is the exhaust of discretization. Yes. So we have this massive,", "tokens": [50909, 666, 9951, 712, 6065, 13, 467, 307, 264, 14687, 295, 25656, 2144, 13, 1079, 13, 407, 321, 362, 341, 5994, 11, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057788968086242676, "compression_ratio": 1.5983935742971886, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 230816, "start": 2325.2799999999997, "end": 2331.7599999999998, "text": " elegant mathematical engine. It's constantly flowing, driven by the thermodynamic friction of entropy.", "tokens": [51221, 21117, 18894, 2848, 13, 467, 311, 6460, 13974, 11, 9555, 538, 264, 8810, 34988, 17710, 295, 30867, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057788968086242676, "compression_ratio": 1.5983935742971886, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 233176, "start": 2331.76, "end": 2338.2400000000002, "text": " It's accumulating mass and meaning, flowing down gradients, shedding history into the defect space to", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 12989, 12162, 2758, 293, 3620, 11, 13974, 760, 2771, 2448, 11, 49934, 2503, 666, 264, 16445, 1901, 281, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0800996720790863, "compression_ratio": 1.5813953488372092, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758281824209465e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 233176, "start": 2338.2400000000002, "end": 2344.7200000000003, "text": " create the forward march of time. And dictating the specific shapes of early galaxies, human minds,", "tokens": [50689, 1884, 264, 2128, 8368, 295, 565, 13, 400, 12569, 990, 264, 2685, 10854, 295, 2440, 28755, 11, 1952, 9634, 11, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0800996720790863, "compression_ratio": 1.5813953488372092, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758281824209465e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 233176, "start": 2344.7200000000003, "end": 2349.92, "text": " and corporate bureaucracies. Right. But what happens when the engine stalls? What happens when the flow", "tokens": [51013, 293, 10896, 26360, 12080, 530, 13, 1779, 13, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 2848, 50248, 30, 708, 2314, 562, 264, 3095, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0800996720790863, "compression_ratio": 1.5813953488372092, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758281824209465e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 233176, "start": 2349.92, "end": 2356.5600000000004, "text": " stops? That brings us to the final and perhaps most terrifying section of the monographs. Theorem 6.5,", "tokens": [51273, 10094, 30, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2572, 293, 4317, 881, 18106, 3541, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 82, 13, 440, 37956, 1386, 13, 20, 11, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0800996720790863, "compression_ratio": 1.5813953488372092, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758281824209465e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 235656, "start": 2356.56, "end": 2363.04, "text": " the universal death state. The unified failure modes of reality. The engine of reality requires a", "tokens": [50365, 264, 11455, 2966, 1785, 13, 440, 26787, 7763, 14068, 295, 4103, 13, 440, 2848, 295, 4103, 7029, 257, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611371300437233, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266953484031735e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 235656, "start": 2363.04, "end": 2368.64, "text": " constant injection of external contradiction, of entropy to keep the vector flow moving. The river", "tokens": [50689, 5754, 22873, 295, 8320, 34937, 11, 295, 30867, 281, 1066, 264, 8062, 3095, 2684, 13, 440, 6810, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611371300437233, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266953484031735e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 235656, "start": 2368.64, "end": 2374.0, "text": " only flows if there is a mountain. Fliction analyzes what happens mathematically in the Lamferdine regime", "tokens": [50969, 787, 12867, 498, 456, 307, 257, 6937, 13, 3235, 4105, 6459, 12214, 437, 2314, 44003, 294, 264, 18825, 612, 67, 533, 13120, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611371300437233, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266953484031735e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 235656, "start": 2374.0, "end": 2379.44, "text": " if that nigentropy injection halts. Without that driving thermodynamic differential, both the scalar", "tokens": [51237, 498, 300, 26996, 317, 27514, 22873, 7523, 1373, 13, 9129, 300, 4840, 8810, 34988, 15756, 11, 1293, 264, 39684, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611371300437233, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266953484031735e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 235656, "start": 2379.44, "end": 2385.52, "text": " gradients, the differences in density, and the vector gradients, the flow velocity decay exponentially to zero.", "tokens": [51509, 2771, 2448, 11, 264, 7300, 294, 10305, 11, 293, 264, 8062, 2771, 2448, 11, 264, 3095, 9269, 21039, 37330, 281, 4018, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08611371300437233, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266953484031735e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 238552, "start": 2385.52, "end": 2391.84, "text": " The mathematical landscape completely flattens out. The river becomes a stagnant pond. And because the RSVP", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18894, 9661, 2584, 932, 1591, 694, 484, 13, 440, 6810, 3643, 257, 32853, 394, 17384, 13, 400, 570, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029046525346472, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177780003770133e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 238552, "start": 2391.84, "end": 2397.36, "text": " equations uniquely map to all domains of existence, this gradient flattening creates characteristic", "tokens": [50681, 11787, 31474, 4471, 281, 439, 25514, 295, 9123, 11, 341, 16235, 24183, 278, 7829, 16282, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029046525346472, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177780003770133e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 238552, "start": 2397.36, "end": 2403.68, "text": " perfectly unified failure modes across cosmology, cognition, and human society. The three apocalypses.", "tokens": [50957, 6239, 26787, 7763, 14068, 2108, 22207, 1793, 11, 46905, 11, 293, 1952, 4086, 13, 440, 1045, 1882, 22665, 1878, 279, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029046525346472, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177780003770133e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 238552, "start": 2403.68, "end": 2410.16, "text": " Let's walk through them, starting with the biggest scale, cosmology. In the cosmological domain, Pcosmo,", "tokens": [51273, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 552, 11, 2891, 365, 264, 3880, 4373, 11, 22207, 1793, 13, 682, 264, 22207, 4383, 9274, 11, 430, 6877, 3280, 11, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09029046525346472, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.4177780003770133e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 241016, "start": 2410.16, "end": 2415.6, "text": " the mathematical failure mode, is the cosmic heat death. As entropy saturates the entire system and", "tokens": [50365, 264, 18894, 7763, 4391, 11, 307, 264, 27614, 3738, 2966, 13, 1018, 30867, 21160, 1024, 264, 2302, 1185, 293, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08566492171514602, "compression_ratio": 1.553903345724907, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251426825576793e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 241016, "start": 2415.6, "end": 2421.6, "text": " all energy gradients flatten out, the universe loses all structural coherence. So no more condensation,", "tokens": [50637, 439, 2281, 2771, 2448, 24183, 484, 11, 264, 6445, 18293, 439, 15067, 26528, 655, 13, 407, 572, 544, 2224, 35292, 11, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08566492171514602, "compression_ratio": 1.553903345724907, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251426825576793e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 241016, "start": 2421.6, "end": 2428.56, "text": " no more stars erupting. It fades into a desaturated volumetric point cloud. Just a homogenous, lukewarm,", "tokens": [50937, 572, 544, 6105, 20999, 662, 278, 13, 467, 32679, 666, 257, 730, 19493, 770, 1996, 449, 17475, 935, 4588, 13, 1449, 257, 3655, 45519, 11, 10438, 330, 49240, 11, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08566492171514602, "compression_ratio": 1.553903345724907, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251426825576793e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 241016, "start": 2428.56, "end": 2435.2799999999997, "text": " infinite soup of maximal entropy and absolutely zero Lamferdine flow. Okay, that is bleak, but it aligns with", "tokens": [51285, 13785, 7884, 295, 49336, 30867, 293, 3122, 4018, 18825, 612, 67, 533, 3095, 13, 1033, 11, 300, 307, 5408, 514, 11, 457, 309, 7975, 82, 365, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08566492171514602, "compression_ratio": 1.553903345724907, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251426825576793e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 243528, "start": 2435.28, "end": 2439.44, "text": " standard physics. We've known about the heat death of the universe for a while. Right, that's not new.", "tokens": [50365, 3832, 10649, 13, 492, 600, 2570, 466, 264, 3738, 2966, 295, 264, 6445, 337, 257, 1339, 13, 1779, 11, 300, 311, 406, 777, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914068797849259, "compression_ratio": 1.5719557195571956, "no_speech_prob": 3.1165749234812745e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 243528, "start": 2439.44, "end": 2445.36, "text": " But here is where Fliction's translation matrix makes a massive leap. Let's translate that exact same", "tokens": [50573, 583, 510, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 311, 12853, 8141, 1669, 257, 5994, 19438, 13, 961, 311, 13799, 300, 1900, 912, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914068797849259, "compression_ratio": 1.5719557195571956, "no_speech_prob": 3.1165749234812745e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 243528, "start": 2445.36, "end": 2451.6000000000004, "text": " mathematical flattening to biology. To the brain. In the cognitive domain P-semantic, we have to look at", "tokens": [50869, 18894, 24183, 278, 281, 14956, 13, 1407, 264, 3567, 13, 682, 264, 15605, 9274, 430, 12, 19872, 7128, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914068797849259, "compression_ratio": 1.5719557195571956, "no_speech_prob": 3.1165749234812745e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 243528, "start": 2451.6000000000004, "end": 2459.6800000000003, "text": " the flow vector, V. Remember, in the mind, V translates to directed inference, or human agency. Right, or willpower.", "tokens": [51181, 264, 3095, 8062, 11, 691, 13, 5459, 11, 294, 264, 1575, 11, 691, 28468, 281, 12898, 38253, 11, 420, 1952, 7934, 13, 1779, 11, 420, 486, 9513, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914068797849259, "compression_ratio": 1.5719557195571956, "no_speech_prob": 3.1165749234812745e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 245968, "start": 2459.68, "end": 2465.8399999999997, "text": " If the scalar gradients of meaning vanish, meaning grad phi goes to zero, the flow becomes decoupled.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 39684, 2771, 2448, 295, 3620, 43584, 11, 3620, 2771, 13107, 1709, 281, 4018, 11, 264, 3095, 3643, 979, 263, 15551, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06932331441522954, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.7474300001776855e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 245968, "start": 2465.8399999999997, "end": 2471.2799999999997, "text": " Without an active flow reward, without a gradient pulling you toward resolving surprise,", "tokens": [50673, 9129, 364, 4967, 3095, 7782, 11, 1553, 257, 16235, 8407, 291, 7361, 49940, 6365, 11, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06932331441522954, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.7474300001776855e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 245968, "start": 2471.2799999999997, "end": 2477.12, "text": " your cognitive agency simply collapses. The mind falls into a stagnant entropic equilibrium.", "tokens": [50945, 428, 15605, 7934, 2935, 48765, 13, 440, 1575, 8804, 666, 257, 32853, 394, 948, 39173, 15625, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06932331441522954, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.7474300001776855e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 245968, "start": 2477.12, "end": 2484.08, "text": " The paper explicitly calls it a CLIO dead end. A CLIO dead end. What does that look like in a person?", "tokens": [51237, 440, 3035, 20803, 5498, 309, 257, 12855, 15167, 3116, 917, 13, 316, 12855, 15167, 3116, 917, 13, 708, 775, 300, 574, 411, 294, 257, 954, 30, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06932331441522954, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.7474300001776855e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 248408, "start": 2484.08, "end": 2490.4, "text": " It is the exact mathematical definition of clinical brain deadness, or in a less absolute psychological", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 1900, 18894, 7123, 295, 9115, 3567, 3116, 1287, 11, 420, 294, 257, 1570, 8236, 14346, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07226214566073574, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042244131002971e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 248408, "start": 2490.4, "end": 2496.56, "text": " sense, severe catatonic depression. The landscape of meaning has flattened. There is no gradient", "tokens": [50681, 2020, 11, 8922, 3857, 267, 11630, 10799, 13, 440, 9661, 295, 3620, 575, 24183, 292, 13, 821, 307, 572, 16235, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07226214566073574, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042244131002971e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 248408, "start": 2496.56, "end": 2502.56, "text": " pulling your attention. No desire pushing your effort forward. Agency stops. Wait, but human agency is", "tokens": [50989, 8407, 428, 3202, 13, 883, 7516, 7380, 428, 4630, 2128, 13, 21649, 10094, 13, 3802, 11, 457, 1952, 7934, 307, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07226214566073574, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042244131002971e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 248408, "start": 2502.56, "end": 2509.44, "text": " biological. It's driven by ATP, neurotransmitters, dopamine, neurons firing. How can Fliction mathematically", "tokens": [51289, 13910, 13, 467, 311, 9555, 538, 39202, 11, 43286, 25392, 3508, 1559, 11, 37219, 11, 22027, 16045, 13, 1012, 393, 3235, 4105, 44003, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07226214566073574, "compression_ratio": 1.5725190839694656, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042244131002971e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 250944, "start": 2509.44, "end": 2514.4, "text": " equate clinical depression in a biological organism with the literal thermodynamic heat death of the", "tokens": [50365, 1267, 473, 9115, 10799, 294, 257, 13910, 24128, 365, 264, 20411, 8810, 34988, 3738, 2966, 295, 264, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059381704414840294, "compression_ratio": 1.6644518272425248, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017403091684207e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 250944, "start": 2514.4, "end": 2519.68, "text": " universe? Isn't that a step too far? It sounds like an overreach until you remember the Friston duality.", "tokens": [50613, 6445, 30, 6998, 380, 300, 257, 1823, 886, 1400, 30, 467, 3263, 411, 364, 670, 16226, 1826, 291, 1604, 264, 1526, 47345, 11848, 507, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059381704414840294, "compression_ratio": 1.6644518272425248, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017403091684207e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 250944, "start": 2519.68, "end": 2524.96, "text": " The biology, the ATP, the dopamine are just the physical substrate performing the computation of", "tokens": [50877, 440, 14956, 11, 264, 39202, 11, 264, 37219, 366, 445, 264, 4001, 27585, 10205, 264, 24903, 295, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059381704414840294, "compression_ratio": 1.6644518272425248, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017403091684207e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 250944, "start": 2524.96, "end": 2530.64, "text": " free energy minimization. They are just the water and the river. Exactly. The RSVP equations describe", "tokens": [51141, 1737, 2281, 4464, 2144, 13, 814, 366, 445, 264, 1281, 293, 264, 6810, 13, 7587, 13, 440, 25855, 53, 47, 11787, 6786, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059381704414840294, "compression_ratio": 1.6644518272425248, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017403091684207e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 250944, "start": 2530.64, "end": 2536.0, "text": " the geometry of the riverbed. When the landscape of meaning flattens, the dopamine stops flowing", "tokens": [51425, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 6810, 2883, 13, 1133, 264, 9661, 295, 3620, 932, 1591, 694, 11, 264, 37219, 10094, 13974, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059381704414840294, "compression_ratio": 1.6644518272425248, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017403091684207e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 253600, "start": 2536.0, "end": 2541.76, "text": " because there is no computational gradient to reward. The mathematical apocalypse precedes the", "tokens": [50365, 570, 456, 307, 572, 28270, 16235, 281, 7782, 13, 440, 18894, 42600, 16969, 279, 264, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10736259113658558, "compression_ratio": 1.776978417266187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2443329746740792e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 253600, "start": 2541.76, "end": 2548.08, "text": " biological one. No cosmic stars forming. No cognitive thoughts forming. It's the same zero. And", "tokens": [50653, 13910, 472, 13, 883, 27614, 6105, 15745, 13, 883, 15605, 4598, 15745, 13, 467, 311, 264, 912, 4018, 13, 400, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10736259113658558, "compression_ratio": 1.776978417266187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2443329746740792e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 253600, "start": 2548.08, "end": 2554.64, "text": " finally, society. The institutional domain. When the societal gradients flatten. In P institution,", "tokens": [50969, 2721, 11, 4086, 13, 440, 18391, 9274, 13, 1133, 264, 33472, 2771, 2448, 24183, 13, 682, 430, 7818, 11, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10736259113658558, "compression_ratio": 1.776978417266187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2443329746740792e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 253600, "start": 2554.64, "end": 2560.32, "text": " the vector flow represents institutional drive. And the curl of that flow, how it twists and interacts,", "tokens": [51297, 264, 8062, 3095, 8855, 18391, 3332, 13, 400, 264, 22591, 295, 300, 3095, 11, 577, 309, 35290, 293, 43582, 11, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10736259113658558, "compression_ratio": 1.776978417266187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2443329746740792e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 253600, "start": 2560.32, "end": 2565.92, "text": " represents vorticity. Vorticity, like a whirlpool. Vorticity is the active circulation of resources,", "tokens": [51581, 8855, 371, 477, 44198, 13, 691, 477, 44198, 11, 411, 257, 35706, 17374, 13, 691, 477, 44198, 307, 264, 4967, 23168, 295, 3593, 11, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10736259113658558, "compression_ratio": 1.776978417266187, "no_speech_prob": 2.2443329746740792e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 256592, "start": 2565.92, "end": 2571.6, "text": " ideas, and capital. When the societal gradients decay, vorticity halts completely. Sphere pop", "tokens": [50365, 3487, 11, 293, 4238, 13, 1133, 264, 33472, 2771, 2448, 21039, 11, 371, 477, 44198, 7523, 1373, 2584, 13, 318, 6605, 1665, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07235957580862694, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.201389678185839e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 256592, "start": 2571.6, "end": 2576.88, "text": " circulation stops. Institutional rigidity. Literally frozen rigidity. Without the thermodynamic", "tokens": [50649, 23168, 10094, 13, 2730, 41859, 8329, 17711, 13, 23768, 12496, 8329, 17711, 13, 9129, 264, 8810, 34988, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07235957580862694, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.201389678185839e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 256592, "start": 2576.88, "end": 2580.8, "text": " pressure of active flow to overcome boundaries, the institutions become completely trapped in their", "tokens": [50913, 3321, 295, 4967, 3095, 281, 10473, 13180, 11, 264, 8142, 1813, 2584, 14994, 294, 641, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07235957580862694, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.201389678185839e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 256592, "start": 2580.8, "end": 2585.76, "text": " own ritual resistance. The surface tension wins out completely. They can never merge. They can never", "tokens": [51109, 1065, 13792, 7335, 13, 440, 3753, 8980, 10641, 484, 2584, 13, 814, 393, 1128, 22183, 13, 814, 393, 1128, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07235957580862694, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.201389678185839e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 256592, "start": 2585.76, "end": 2592.08, "text": " adapt to new realities. They simply exist as static, heavily armored spheres of pure bureaucracy,", "tokens": [51357, 6231, 281, 777, 27785, 13, 814, 2935, 2514, 382, 13437, 11, 10950, 41879, 41225, 295, 6075, 44671, 11, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07235957580862694, "compression_ratio": 1.6944444444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.201389678185839e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 259208, "start": 2592.08, "end": 2597.7599999999998, "text": " consuming energy just to maintain their own surface tension, accomplishing absolutely nothing.", "tokens": [50365, 19867, 2281, 445, 281, 6909, 641, 1065, 3753, 8980, 11, 6548, 3807, 3122, 1825, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13969181323873586, "compression_ratio": 1.568, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442644972640256e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 259208, "start": 2597.7599999999998, "end": 2604.4, "text": " So, a stagnant, impossible-to-navigate DMV bureaucracy where you wait four hours to get a stamp,", "tokens": [50649, 407, 11, 257, 32853, 394, 11, 6243, 12, 1353, 12, 629, 85, 328, 473, 15322, 53, 44671, 689, 291, 1699, 1451, 2496, 281, 483, 257, 9921, 11, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13969181323873586, "compression_ratio": 1.568, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442644972640256e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 259208, "start": 2604.4, "end": 2609.92, "text": " a profoundly depressed human mind completely lacking the agency to get out of bed, and the literal", "tokens": [50981, 257, 39954, 18713, 1952, 1575, 2584, 20889, 264, 7934, 281, 483, 484, 295, 2901, 11, 293, 264, 20411, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13969181323873586, "compression_ratio": 1.568, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442644972640256e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 259208, "start": 2610.48, "end": 2616.7999999999997, "text": " eventual heat death of the cosmos are literally the exact same mathematical equation solving to zero.", "tokens": [51285, 33160, 3738, 2966, 295, 264, 41794, 366, 3736, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 5367, 12606, 281, 4018, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13969181323873586, "compression_ratio": 1.568, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442644972640256e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 261680, "start": 2616.8, "end": 2624.0, "text": " Yes. They are identically the same. It is the profound structural alignment of the failure of the RSVP", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 814, 366, 2473, 984, 264, 912, 13, 467, 307, 264, 14382, 15067, 18515, 295, 264, 7763, 295, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08650888005892436, "compression_ratio": 1.5775193798449612, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610497257848246e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 261680, "start": 2624.0, "end": 2629.36, "text": " plenum. When the gradients vanish, reality stops flowing. Whether that reality is made of curved", "tokens": [50725, 499, 268, 449, 13, 1133, 264, 2771, 2448, 43584, 11, 4103, 10094, 13974, 13, 8503, 300, 4103, 307, 1027, 295, 24991, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08650888005892436, "compression_ratio": 1.5775193798449612, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610497257848246e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 261680, "start": 2629.36, "end": 2634.4, "text": " space-time, biological synapses, or social contracts, the apocalypse looks mathematically exactly the", "tokens": [50993, 1901, 12, 3766, 11, 13910, 5451, 2382, 279, 11, 420, 2093, 13952, 11, 264, 42600, 1542, 44003, 2293, 264, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08650888005892436, "compression_ratio": 1.5775193798449612, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610497257848246e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 261680, "start": 2634.4, "end": 2640.0, "text": " same. The engine stalls. Let's pull all of this together. We started with a tiny, incredibly faint cosmic", "tokens": [51245, 912, 13, 440, 2848, 50248, 13, 961, 311, 2235, 439, 295, 341, 1214, 13, 492, 1409, 365, 257, 5870, 11, 6252, 21104, 27614, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08650888005892436, "compression_ratio": 1.5775193798449612, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610497257848246e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 264000, "start": 2640.0, "end": 2646.08, "text": " fossil, LAP1B, a primordial galaxy so isolated it hasn't been chemically overwritten by the turbulent", "tokens": [50365, 18737, 11, 441, 4715, 16, 33, 11, 257, 2886, 765, 831, 17639, 370, 14621, 309, 6132, 380, 668, 4771, 984, 670, 26859, 538, 264, 41697, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677263633492067, "compression_ratio": 1.5617977528089888, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355340676903033e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 264000, "start": 2646.08, "end": 2651.84, "text": " history of the universe. Acting as an undisrupted event log in matter. Right. Showing us how specific", "tokens": [50669, 2503, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 42413, 382, 364, 674, 271, 5428, 292, 2280, 3565, 294, 1871, 13, 1779, 13, 6895, 278, 505, 577, 2685, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677263633492067, "compression_ratio": 1.5617977528089888, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355340676903033e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 264000, "start": 2651.84, "end": 2657.04, "text": " elements were refused the right to propagate into the future. And we learned we could only even perceive", "tokens": [50957, 4959, 645, 14654, 264, 558, 281, 48256, 666, 264, 2027, 13, 400, 321, 3264, 321, 727, 787, 754, 20281, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677263633492067, "compression_ratio": 1.5617977528089888, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355340676903033e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 264000, "start": 2657.04, "end": 2664.56, "text": " it because of mediated extraction. A massive gravitational lens acting as a mandatory amplifier for the most", "tokens": [51217, 309, 570, 295, 17269, 770, 30197, 13, 316, 5994, 28538, 6765, 6577, 382, 257, 22173, 27439, 337, 264, 881, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09677263633492067, "compression_ratio": 1.5617977528089888, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355340676903033e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 266456, "start": 2664.56, "end": 2670.64, "text": " primitive, invisible truths. Which led us to uncover the RSVP plenum, the universal master engine where", "tokens": [50365, 28540, 11, 14603, 30079, 13, 3013, 4684, 505, 281, 21694, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 11, 264, 11455, 4505, 2848, 689, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056742098139620376, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 2.076444268264699e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 266456, "start": 2670.64, "end": 2676.08, "text": " entropy gradients mathematically drive vector flows to accumulate scalar mass. A singular engine that", "tokens": [50669, 30867, 2771, 2448, 44003, 3332, 8062, 12867, 281, 33384, 39684, 2758, 13, 316, 20010, 2848, 300, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.056742098139620376, "compression_ratio": 1.553030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 2.076444268264699e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek