start": 2966.6800000000003, "end": 2968.1000000000004, "text": " is that they do not transform", "tokens": [51334, 307, 300, 436, 360, 406, 4088, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22621084686018464, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.405012716414189e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 294730, "start": 2968.1000000000004, "end": 2969.26, "text": " under Weill rescalings.", "tokens": [51405, 833, 492, 373, 9610, 304, 1109, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22621084686018464, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.405012716414189e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 294730, "start": 2969.5800000000004, "end": 2970.6800000000003, "text": " They are perfectly immune", "tokens": [51479, 814, 366, 6239, 11992, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22621084686018464, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.405012716414189e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 294730, "start": 2970.6800000000003, "end": 2972.44, "text": " to the stretching of space-time geometry.", "tokens": [51534, 281, 264, 19632, 295, 1901, 12, 3766, 18426, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22621084686018464, "compression_ratio": 1.6347517730496455, "no_speech_prob": 1.405012716414189e-12}, {"id": 935, "seek": 297244, "start": 2972.44, "end": 2973.96, "text": " And because they are higher derivative,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 436, 366, 2946, 13760, 11, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17607158025105793, "compression_ratio": 1.1630434782608696, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420382828596374e-12}, {"id": 936, "seek": 297244, "start": 2974.18, "end": 2975.78, "text": " I assume they also come with a ledger", "tokens": [50452, 286, 6552, 436, 611, 808, 365, 257, 4684, 1321, 50532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17607158025105793, "compression_ratio": 1.1630434782608696, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420382828596374e-12}, {"id": 937, "seek": 297244, "start": 2975.78, "end": 2977.44, "text": " full of negative norm ghosts.", "tokens": [50532, 1577, 295, 3671, 2026, 21744, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17607158025105793, "compression_ratio": 1.1630434782608696, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420382828596374e-12}, {"id": 938, "seek": 297744, "start": 2977.44, "end": 2978.68, "text": " They absolutely do.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 3122, 360, 13, 50427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 939, "seek": 297744, "start": 2978.78, "end": 2980.48, "text": " They are plagued by coordinate ghosts.", "tokens": [50432, 814, 366, 33756, 5827, 538, 15670, 21744, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 940, "seek": 297744, "start": 2981.04, "end": 2982.08, "text": " But they also possess", "tokens": [50545, 583, 436, 611, 17490, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 941, "seek": 297744, "start": 2982.08, "end": 2984.86, "text": " a massive, infinite-dimensional gauge symmetry", "tokens": [50597, 257, 5994, 11, 13785, 12, 18759, 17924, 25440, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 942, "seek": 297744, "start": 2984.86, "end": 2987.58, "text": " that allows you to mathematically shift the field", "tokens": [50736, 300, 4045, 291, 281, 44003, 5513, 264, 2519, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 943, "seek": 297744, "start": 2987.58, "end": 2989.28, "text": " by any harmonic function.", "tokens": [50872, 538, 604, 32270, 2445, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 944, "seek": 297744, "start": 2989.9, "end": 2992.12, "text": " When you rigorously account for this symmetry,", "tokens": [50988, 1133, 291, 42191, 5098, 2696, 337, 341, 25440, 11, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 945, "seek": 297744, "start": 2992.54, "end": 2993.5, "text": " you find that the theory", "tokens": [51120, 291, 915, 300, 264, 5261, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 946, "seek": 297744, "start": 2993.5, "end": 2995.7200000000003, "text": " has no local degrees of freedom at all.", "tokens": [51168, 575, 572, 2654, 5310, 295, 5645, 412, 439, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 947, "seek": 297744, "start": 2996.46, "end": 2998.04, "text": " The projection operator pi", "tokens": [51316, 440, 22743, 12973, 3895, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 948, "seek": 297744, "start": 2998.04, "end": 3000.76, "text": " maps the entire complex admissibility manifold", "tokens": [51395, 11317, 264, 2302, 3997, 5910, 891, 2841, 47138, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 949, "seek": 297744, "start": 3000.76, "end": 3003.64, "text": " down to a single, unique physical state", "tokens": [51531, 760, 281, 257, 2167, 11, 3845, 4001, 1785, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 950, "seek": 297744, "start": 3003.64, "end": 3005.14, "text": " in the observable manifold,", "tokens": [51675, 294, 264, 9951, 712, 47138, 11, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20373613792553283, "compression_ratio": 1.6321428571428571, "no_speech_prob": 2.676847458971121e-12}, {"id": 951, "seek": 300514, "start": 3005.14, "end": 3006.2599999999998, "text": " the vacuum.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 14224, 13, 50421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 952, "seek": 300514, "start": 3006.7799999999997, "end": 3008.98, "text": " So the entire chaotic internal field of ghosts", "tokens": [50447, 407, 264, 2302, 27013, 6920, 2519, 295, 21744, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 953, "seek": 300514, "start": 3008.98, "end": 3010.6, "text": " perfectly cancels itself out", "tokens": [50557, 6239, 393, 66, 1625, 2564, 484, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 954, "seek": 300514, "start": 3010.6, "end": 3012.3599999999997, "text": " to leave behind absolute nothingness,", "tokens": [50638, 281, 1856, 2261, 8236, 1825, 1287, 11, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 955, "seek": 300514, "start": 3012.48, "end": 3013.72, "text": " a perfectly stable vacuum.", "tokens": [50732, 257, 6239, 8351, 14224, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 956, "seek": 300514, "start": 3014.3599999999997, "end": 3015.66, "text": " Why introduce them at all", "tokens": [50826, 1545, 5366, 552, 412, 439, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 957, "seek": 300514, "start": 3015.66, "end": 3016.42, "text": " if they just vanish?", "tokens": [50891, 498, 436, 445, 43584, 30, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 958, "seek": 300514, "start": 3016.52, "end": 3017.9, "text": " What problem do they actually solve", "tokens": [50934, 708, 1154, 360, 436, 767, 5039, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 959, "seek": 300514, "start": 3017.9, "end": 3018.42, "text": " in the background?", "tokens": [51003, 294, 264, 3678, 30, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 960, "seek": 300514, "start": 3018.64, "end": 3020.02, "text": " They solve the Weill anomaly.", "tokens": [51040, 814, 5039, 264, 492, 373, 42737, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 961, "seek": 300514, "start": 3020.66, "end": 3021.96, "text": " When you take the standard model", "tokens": [51141, 1133, 291, 747, 264, 3832, 2316, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 962, "seek": 300514, "start": 3021.96, "end": 3022.98, "text": " of particle physics,", "tokens": [51206, 295, 12359, 10649, 11, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 963, "seek": 300514, "start": 3023.22, "end": 3024.68, "text": " quarks, electrons, photons,", "tokens": [51269, 421, 20851, 11, 14265, 11, 40209, 11, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 964, "seek": 300514, "start": 3024.94, "end": 3026.06, "text": " and you put them in a", "tokens": [51355, 293, 291, 829, 552, 294, 257, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 965, "seek": 300514, "start": 3026.06, "end": 3027.5, "text": " curved space-time background,", "tokens": [51411, 24991, 1901, 12, 3766, 3678, 11, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 966, "seek": 300514, "start": 3027.7799999999997, "end": 3029.56, "text": " like a galaxy or the expanding universe,", "tokens": [51497, 411, 257, 17639, 420, 264, 14702, 6445, 11, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 967, "seek": 300514, "start": 3029.96, "end": 3031.8199999999997, "text": " the quantum fluctuations of those particles", "tokens": [51606, 264, 13018, 45276, 295, 729, 10007, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 968, "seek": 300514, "start": 3031.8199999999997, "end": 3032.64, "text": " produce an anomaly.", "tokens": [51699, 5258, 364, 42737, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 969, "seek": 300514, "start": 3033.2799999999997, "end": 3034.92, "text": " Specifically, the trace of the stress", "tokens": [51772, 26058, 11, 264, 13508, 295, 264, 4244, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1916707229614258, "compression_ratio": 1.7314814814814814, "no_speech_prob": 1.9893140953963773e-12}, {"id": 970, "seek": 303492, "start": 3034.92, "end": 3036.6800000000003, "text": " energy tensor no longer equals zero.", "tokens": [50365, 2281, 40863, 572, 2854, 6915, 4018, 13, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 971, "seek": 303492, "start": 3037.2000000000003, "end": 3038.5, "text": " This breaks conformal symmetry,", "tokens": [50479, 639, 9857, 18975, 304, 25440, 11, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 972, "seek": 303492, "start": 3038.7200000000003, "end": 3040.0, "text": " which is a mathematical disaster", "tokens": [50555, 597, 307, 257, 18894, 11293, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 973, "seek": 303492, "start": 3040.0, "end": 3041.62, "text": " for theories that rely on scale", "tokens": [50619, 337, 13667, 300, 10687, 322, 4373, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 974, "seek": 303492, "start": 3041.62, "end": 3042.92, "text": " and variance at the Big Bang.", "tokens": [50700, 293, 21977, 412, 264, 5429, 11538, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 975, "seek": 303492, "start": 3043.34, "end": 3044.54, "text": " And how did physicists try", "tokens": [50786, 400, 577, 630, 48716, 853, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 976, "seek": 303492, "start": 3044.54, "end": 3045.84, "text": " to fix this anomaly before?", "tokens": [50846, 281, 3191, 341, 42737, 949, 30, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 977, "seek": 303492, "start": 3046.38, "end": 3047.92, "text": " Historically, physicists thought", "tokens": [50938, 25108, 984, 11, 48716, 1194, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 978, "seek": 303492, "start": 3047.92, "end": 3049.46, "text": " the only way to cancel this anomaly", "tokens": [51015, 264, 787, 636, 281, 10373, 341, 42737, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 979, "seek": 303492, "start": 3049.46, "end": 3051.32, "text": " was to invent supersymmetry.", "tokens": [51092, 390, 281, 7962, 37906, 32497, 9889, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 980, "seek": 303492, "start": 3052.0, "end": 3053.94, "text": " They theorized a whole suite", "tokens": [51219, 814, 27423, 1602, 257, 1379, 14205, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 981, "seek": 303492, "start": 3053.94, "end": 3055.9, "text": " of undiscovered mirror particles,", "tokens": [51316, 295, 674, 40080, 292, 8013, 10007, 11, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 982, "seek": 303492, "start": 3056.6, "end": 3058.6800000000003, "text": " selectrons, squarks, neutrolinos,", "tokens": [51449, 3048, 13270, 11, 2339, 20851, 11, 7989, 340, 5045, 329, 11, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 983, "seek": 303492, "start": 3059.08, "end": 3060.26, "text": " whose quantum fluctuations", "tokens": [51573, 6104, 13018, 45276, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 984, "seek": 303492, "start": 3060.26, "end": 3061.7200000000003, "text": " would perfectly cancel out", "tokens": [51632, 576, 6239, 10373, 484, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 985, "seek": 303492, "start": 3061.7200000000003, "end": 3063.38, "text": " the standard model fluctuations.", "tokens": [51705, 264, 3832, 2316, 45276, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21430561560710878, "compression_ratio": 1.6835016835016836, "no_speech_prob": 2.0243951914106217e-12}, {"id": 986, "seek": 306338, "start": 3063.38, "end": 3065.04, "text": " Which is very convenient,", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 588, 10851, 11, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 987, "seek": 306338, "start": 3065.2000000000003, "end": 3066.7200000000003, "text": " since the Large Hadron Collider", "tokens": [50456, 1670, 264, 33092, 12298, 2044, 4586, 1438, 50532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 988, "seek": 306338, "start": 3066.7200000000003, "end": 3067.98, "text": " has spent over a decade", "tokens": [50532, 575, 4418, 670, 257, 10378, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 989, "seek": 306338, "start": 3067.98, "end": 3069.2200000000003, "text": " and billions of dollars", "tokens": [50595, 293, 17375, 295, 3808, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 990, "seek": 306338, "start": 3069.2200000000003, "end": 3070.7000000000003, "text": " smashing protons together", "tokens": [50657, 43316, 40270, 1214, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 991, "seek": 306338, "start": 3070.7000000000003, "end": 3072.04, "text": " looking for supersymmetry", "tokens": [50731, 1237, 337, 37906, 32497, 9889, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 992, "seek": 306338, "start": 3072.04, "end": 3074.1, "text": " and hasn't found a single shred", "tokens": [50798, 293, 6132, 380, 1352, 257, 2167, 21567, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 993, "seek": 306338, "start": 3074.1, "end": 3075.32, "text": " of evidence that it actually", "tokens": [50901, 295, 4467, 300, 309, 767, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 994, "seek": 306338, "start": 3075.32, "end": 3076.1600000000003, "text": " exists in nature.", "tokens": [50962, 8198, 294, 3687, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compression_ratio": 1.6122448979591837, "no_speech_prob": 2.4945280216459587e-12}, {"id": 995, "seek": 306338, "start": 3076.58, "end": 3077.1400000000003, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51025, 48746, 736, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16187083019929774, "compre