, "seek": 5520, "start": 68.38, "end": 72.38, "text": " And we're going to translate them into a framework that you can actually visualize and understand.", "tokens": [51024, 400, 321, 434, 516, 281, 13799, 552, 666, 257, 8388, 300, 291, 393, 767, 23273, 293, 1223, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10962289624509558, "compression_ratio": 1.6588628762541806, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693893225589896e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 5520, "start": 72.72, "end": 77.06, "text": " I mean, we are going to completely redefine time, gravity, quantum mechanics,", "tokens": [51241, 286, 914, 11, 321, 366, 516, 281, 2584, 38818, 533, 565, 11, 12110, 11, 13018, 12939, 11, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10962289624509558, "compression_ratio": 1.6588628762541806, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693893225589896e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 5520, "start": 77.06, "end": 81.36, "text": " and how we actually observe the earliest galaxies in the cosmos.", "tokens": [51458, 293, 577, 321, 767, 11441, 264, 20573, 28755, 294, 264, 41794, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10962289624509558, "compression_ratio": 1.6588628762541806, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693893225589896e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 8136, "start": 81.36, "end": 84.84, "text": " And if you're listening to this right now and thinking, you know, this sounds completely", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 291, 434, 4764, 281, 341, 558, 586, 293, 1953, 11, 291, 458, 11, 341, 3263, 2584, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 8136, "start": 84.84, "end": 86.18, "text": " unprovable, this sounds insane.", "tokens": [50539, 517, 4318, 17915, 11, 341, 3263, 10838, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 8136, "start": 86.3, "end": 88.72, "text": " Well, you are exactly where the scientific community was.", "tokens": [50612, 1042, 11, 291, 366, 2293, 689, 264, 8134, 1768, 390, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 8136, "start": 88.98, "end": 91.7, "text": " Yeah, the initial reaction was highly skeptical.", "tokens": [50746, 865, 11, 264, 5883, 5480, 390, 5405, 28601, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 8136, "start": 92.03999999999999, "end": 94.82, "text": " Because, I mean, how do you prove a mathematical ghost?", "tokens": [50899, 1436, 11, 286, 914, 11, 577, 360, 291, 7081, 257, 18894, 8359, 30, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 8136, "start": 95.0, "end": 97.03999999999999, "text": " How do you observe a universe that moves backward?", "tokens": [51047, 1012, 360, 291, 11441, 257, 6445, 300, 6067, 23897, 30, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 8136, "start": 97.7, "end": 103.62, "text": " But if you've ever felt overwhelmed by how physics, your own cognition, and the society you live in", "tokens": [51182, 583, 498, 291, 600, 1562, 2762, 19042, 538, 577, 10649, 11, 428, 1065, 46905, 11, 293, 264, 4086, 291, 1621, 294, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 8136, "start": 103.62, "end": 106.7, "text": " seem to operate on totally different contradictory rules,", "tokens": [51478, 1643, 281, 9651, 322, 3879, 819, 49555, 4474, 11, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14040960002149272, "compression_ratio": 1.6237623762376239, "no_speech_prob": 1.361797393600872e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 10670, "start": 106.7, "end": 111.04, "text": " this deep dive is going to show you a hidden architecture connecting them all.", "tokens": [50365, 341, 2452, 9192, 307, 516, 281, 855, 291, 257, 7633, 9482, 11015, 552, 439, 13, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 10670, "start": 111.3, "end": 112.8, "text": " It really is a unifying framework.", "tokens": [50595, 467, 534, 307, 257, 517, 5489, 8388, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 10670, "start": 113.08, "end": 114.48, "text": " So we have a ton of ground to cover.", "tokens": [50684, 407, 321, 362, 257, 2952, 295, 2727, 281, 2060, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 10670, "start": 114.76, "end": 120.10000000000001, "text": " We are going to start at the absolute foundation, a concept Flixion calls the RSVP framework.", "tokens": [50768, 492, 366, 516, 281, 722, 412, 264, 8236, 7030, 11, 257, 3410, 3235, 970, 313, 5498, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 10670, "start": 120.7, "end": 122.54, "text": " This is proposed as the substrate of everything.", "tokens": [51065, 639, 307, 10348, 382, 264, 27585, 295, 1203, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 10670, "start": 122.94, "end": 127.64, "text": " So what exactly is the relativistic scalar vector plenum?", "tokens": [51177, 407, 437, 2293, 307, 264, 21960, 3142, 39684, 8062, 499, 268, 449, 30, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 10670, "start": 127.64, "end": 131.92000000000002, "text": " Let's break that down because it really is the stage upon which this entire theory plays out.", "tokens": [51412, 961, 311, 1821, 300, 760, 570, 309, 534, 307, 264, 3233, 3564, 597, 341, 2302, 5261, 5749, 484, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18371815340859549, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.443967558370507e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 13192, "start": 131.92, "end": 136.72, "text": " So the RSVP plenum is proposed as a continuous medium.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 307, 10348, 382, 257, 10957, 6399, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 13192, "start": 137.76, "end": 142.04, "text": " And in physics, to define a medium, you first need a space to put it in.", "tokens": [50657, 400, 294, 10649, 11, 281, 6964, 257, 6399, 11, 291, 700, 643, 257, 1901, 281, 829, 309, 294, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 13192, "start": 142.57999999999998, "end": 143.85999999999999, "text": " Right, a container of some sort.", "tokens": [50898, 1779, 11, 257, 10129, 295, 512, 1333, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 13192, "start": 143.95999999999998, "end": 144.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50967, 7587, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 13192, "start": 144.98, "end": 150.79999999999998, "text": " Flixion defines this on what is known mathematically as a preferred 3 plus 1 foliation.", "tokens": [51018, 3235, 970, 313, 23122, 341, 322, 437, 307, 2570, 44003, 382, 257, 16494, 805, 1804, 502, 3339, 6642, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 13192, "start": 151.14, "end": 152.22, "text": " Wait, let me stop you right there.", "tokens": [51326, 3802, 11, 718, 385, 1590, 291, 558, 456, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 13192, "start": 152.27999999999997, "end": 155.5, "text": " A 3 plus 1 foliation, like slicing space and time.", "tokens": [51383, 316, 805, 1804, 502, 3339, 6642, 11, 411, 46586, 1901, 293, 565, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1593788260280496, "compression_ratio": 1.5381165919282511, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 15550, "start": 155.5, "end": 163.08, "text": " I'm picturing a loaf of bread where the whole loaf is the universe and each slice is just a single moment in time.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 478, 2317, 1345, 257, 40743, 295, 5961, 689, 264, 1379, 40743, 307, 264, 6445, 293, 1184, 13153, 307, 445, 257, 2167, 1623, 294, 565, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 15550, "start": 163.42, "end": 165.7, "text": " That is actually a very helpful starting point.", "tokens": [50761, 663, 307, 767, 257, 588, 4961, 2891, 935, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 15550, "start": 165.7, "end": 170.76, "text": " Because in Einstein's relativity, the universe is a four-dimensional block, you know, space-time.", "tokens": [50875, 1436, 294, 23486, 311, 45675, 11, 264, 6445, 307, 257, 1451, 12, 18759, 3461, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1901, 12, 3766, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 15550, "start": 171.44, "end": 175.24, "text": " Normally, relativity tells us there is no preferred way to slice that loaf.", "tokens": [51162, 17424, 11, 45675, 5112, 505, 456, 307, 572, 16494, 636, 281, 13153, 300, 40743, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 15550, "start": 175.38, "end": 177.34, "text": " Because time is relative to the observer.", "tokens": [51359, 1436, 565, 307, 4972, 281, 264, 27878, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 15550, "start": 177.56, "end": 177.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51468, 7587, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 15550, "start": 178.48, "end": 182.52, "text": " Depending on how fast you're moving, your slices will cut through the loaf at totally different angles.", "tokens": [51514, 22539, 322, 577, 2370, 291, 434, 2684, 11, 428, 19793, 486, 1723, 807, 264, 40743, 412, 3879, 819, 14708, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12307169477818376, "compression_ratio": 1.664406779661017, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554011629700161e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 18252, "start": 182.52, "end": 185.44, "text": " But Flixion's math requires a preferred foliation.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 5221, 7029, 257, 16494, 3339, 6642, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 18252, "start": 186.02, "end": 192.10000000000002, "text": " It establishes a specific, universal background slicing of three spatial dimensions evolving over one dimension of time.", "tokens": [50540, 467, 8327, 279, 257, 2685, 11, 11455, 3678, 46586, 295, 1045, 23598, 12819, 21085, 670, 472, 10139, 295, 565, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 18252, "start": 192.34, "end": 193.76000000000002, "text": " Okay, so we have our slices of bread.", "tokens": [50856, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 362, 527, 19793, 295, 5961, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 18252, "start": 194.08, "end": 194.32000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50943, 1779, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 18252, "start": 194.52, "end": 198.68, "text": " And the plenum, the actual substance of reality, exists within those slices.", "tokens": [50965, 400, 264, 499, 268, 449, 11, 264, 3539, 12961, 295, 4103, 11, 8198, 1951, 729, 19793, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 18252, "start": 199.32000000000002, "end": 203.9, "text": " But instead of just viewing it as empty space curving under the weight of stars and planets,", "tokens": [51205, 583, 2602, 295, 445, 17480, 309, 382, 6707, 1901, 1262, 798, 833, 264, 3364, 295, 6105, 293, 15126, 11, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 18252, "start": 204.4, "end": 210.52, "text": " the plenum consists of three tightly coupled fields that exist everywhere at all times.", "tokens": [51459, 264, 499, 268, 449, 14689, 295, 1045, 21952, 29482, 7909, 300, 2514, 5315, 412, 439, 1413, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325779214369512, "compression_ratio": 1.6458333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271414995950527e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 21052, "start": 210.52, "end": 214.02, "text": " Okay, so reality is literally filled with three fields.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 4103, 307, 3736, 6412, 365, 1045, 7909, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 21052, "start": 214.28, "end": 214.94, "text": " What are they?", "tokens": [50553, 708, 366, 436, 30, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 21052, "start": 215.06, "end": 216.36, "text": " First, you have the Greek letter phi.", "tokens": [50592, 2386, 11, 291, 362, 264, 10281, 5063, 13107, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 21052, "start": 217.04000000000002, "end": 219.10000000000002, "text": " This represents the scalar potential.", "tokens": [50691, 639, 8855, 264, 39684, 3995, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 21052, "start": 219.88, "end": 221.88, "text": " In physical terms, think of it as mass density.", "tokens": [50833, 682, 4001, 2115, 11, 519, 295, 309, 382, 2758, 10305, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 21052, "start": 222.24, "end": 225.02, "text": " Just how much stuff is at a specific point.", "tokens": [50951, 1449, 577, 709, 1507, 307, 412, 257, 2685, 935, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 21052, "start": 225.16000000000003, "end": 229.60000000000002, "text": " And I noticed in my notes, in cognitive terms, the paper actually refers to this as meaning density.", "tokens": [51097, 400, 286, 5694, 294, 452, 5570, 11, 294, 15605, 2115, 11, 264, 3035, 767, 14942, 281, 341, 382, 3620, 10305, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 21052, "start": 229.94, "end": 232.44, "text": " Yes, we will definitely get to the cognitive mapping later.", "tokens": [51336, 1079, 11, 321, 486, 2138, 483, 281, 264, 15605, 18350, 1780, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 21052, "start": 232.52, "end": 236.04000000000002, "text": " But yeah, it's the concentration of significance, or mass.", "tokens": [51465, 583, 1338, 11, 309, 311, 264, 9856, 295, 17687, 11, 420, 2758, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 21052, "start": 236.38, "end": 239.02, "text": " Now, the second field is the lowercase v, the vector flow.", "tokens": [51658, 823, 11, 264, 1150, 2519, 307, 264, 3126, 9765, 371, 11, 264, 8062, 3095, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14048861033880888, "compression_ratio": 1.6360759493670887, "no_speech_prob": 1.55520984545382e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 23902, "start": 239.02, "end": 241.56, "text": " A vector has both a magnitude and a direction.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 8062, 575, 1293, 257, 15668, 293, 257, 3513, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 23902, "start": 242.0, "end": 242.38000000000002, "text": " Like an arrow.", "tokens": [50514, 1743, 364, 11610, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 23902, "start": 242.66, "end": 243.60000000000002, "text": " Exactly like an arrow.", "tokens": [50547, 7587, 411, 364, 11610, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 23902, "start": 243.70000000000002, "end": 245.18, "text": " So this represents directional velocity.", "tokens": [50599, 407, 341, 8855, 42242, 9269, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 23902, "start": 245.86, "end": 248.02, "text": " It is the literal directed movement of the system.", "tokens": [50707, 467, 307, 264, 20411, 12898, 3963, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 23902, "start": 248.14000000000001, "end": 250.98000000000002, "text": " It's not just that stuff exists, it's that the stuff has a trajectory.", "tokens": [50821, 467, 311, 406, 445, 300, 1507, 8198, 11, 309, 311, 300, 264, 1507, 575, 257, 21512, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 23902, "start": 251.32000000000002, "end": 253.98000000000002, "text": " And finally, you have S, the entropy field.", "tokens": [50980, 400, 2721, 11, 291, 362, 318, 11, 264, 30867, 2519, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 23902, "start": 254.10000000000002, "end": 258.34000000000003, "text": " Now, entropy is usually described as like chaos or disorder, right?", "tokens": [51119, 823, 11, 30867, 307, 2673, 7619, 382, 411, 14158, 420, 13399, 11, 558, 30, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 23902, "start": 258.38, "end": 260.06, "text": " Like a bedroom getting messy over time.", "tokens": [51333, 1743, 257, 11211, 1242, 16191, 670, 565, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 23902, "start": 260.3, "end": 263.14, "text": " In the simplest terms, yes, thermodynamic disorder.", "tokens": [51429, 682, 264, 22811, 2115, 11, 2086, 11, 8810, 34988, 13399, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13483028896784377, "compression_ratio": 1.6580882352941178, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903511568579834e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 26314, "start": 263.14, "end": 268.96, "text": " But in the context of the RSVP framework, it's more precise to think of it in an informational sense.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 11, 309, 311, 544, 13600, 281, 519, 295, 309, 294, 364, 49391, 2020, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 26314, "start": 269.12, "end": 272.4, "text": " It represents the representational budget of a system.", "tokens": [50664, 467, 8855, 264, 2906, 1478, 4706, 295, 257, 1185, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 26314, "start": 272.91999999999996, "end": 273.65999999999997, "text": " Representational budget.", "tokens": [50854, 19945, 1478, 4706, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 26314, "start": 273.84, "end": 278.44, "text": " Yeah, it's a measure of the constraints, the heat, the lost information in the field.", "tokens": [50900, 865, 11, 309, 311, 257, 3481, 295, 264, 18491, 11, 264, 3738, 11, 264, 2731, 1589, 294, 264, 2519, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 26314, "start": 278.64, "end": 287.88, "text": " Okay, I need a better visual here because scalar, vector, and entropy fields intercepting on a 3 plus 1 foliation is a bit tough to hold in my head.", "tokens": [51140, 1033, 11, 286, 643, 257, 1101, 5056, 510, 570, 39684, 11, 8062, 11, 293, 30867, 7909, 24700, 278, 322, 257, 805, 1804, 502, 3339, 6642, 307, 257, 857, 4930, 281, 1797, 294, 452, 1378, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 26314, "start": 287.96, "end": 289.15999999999997, "text": " It is abstract for sure.", "tokens": [51606, 467, 307, 12649, 337, 988, 13, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0921916624086093, "compression_ratio": 1.683206106870229, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671675112141625e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 28916, "start": 289.16, "end": 297.98, "text": " Is it kind of like looking at a really complex weather map on the news where the scalar field, the phi, is the air pressure, like the high and low pressure zone?", "tokens": [50365, 1119, 309, 733, 295, 411, 1237, 412, 257, 534, 3997, 5503, 4471, 322, 264, 2583, 689, 264, 39684, 2519, 11, 264, 13107, 11, 307, 264, 1988, 3321, 11, 411, 264, 1090, 293, 2295, 3321, 6668, 30, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 28916, "start": 298.02000000000004, "end": 298.88000000000005, "text": " Okay, I see where you're going.", "tokens": [50808, 1033, 11, 286, 536, 689, 291, 434, 516, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 28916, "start": 299.06, "end": 304.84000000000003, "text": " And the vector field, the V, is the wind blowing, the actual arrows showing the directional flow of the air.", "tokens": [50860, 400, 264, 8062, 2519, 11, 264, 691, 11, 307, 264, 2468, 15068, 11, 264, 3539, 19669, 4099, 264, 42242, 3095, 295, 264, 1988, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 28916, "start": 304.92, "end": 308.38, "text": " And then the entropy field, the S, is the temperature, right?", "tokens": [51153, 400, 550, 264, 30867, 2519, 11, 264, 318, 11, 307, 264, 4292, 11, 558, 30, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 28916, "start": 308.68, "end": 312.22, "text": " Chaotic thermal energy swirling around inside those pressure systems.", "tokens": [51341, 12374, 9411, 15070, 2281, 30310, 278, 926, 1854, 729, 3321, 3652, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 28916, "start": 312.34000000000003, "end": 316.22, "text": " The weather map gets us halfway there, and it's a brilliant conceptual hook.", "tokens": [51524, 440, 5503, 4471, 2170, 505, 15461, 456, 11, 293, 309, 311, 257, 10248, 24106, 6328, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 28916, "start": 316.66, "end": 318.54, "text": " But we do have to be careful with it.", "tokens": [51740, 583, 321, 360, 362, 281, 312, 5026, 365, 309, 13, 51834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09081582746643951, "compression_ratio": 1.7539936102236422, "no_speech_prob": 1.443744646403844e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 31854, "start": 318.54, "end": 321.96000000000004, "text": " The problem with the weather analogy is that wind is made of atoms.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1154, 365, 264, 5503, 21663, 307, 300, 2468, 307, 1027, 295, 16871, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 31854, "start": 322.26000000000005, "end": 323.22, "text": " Right, it's physical stuff.", "tokens": [50551, 1779, 11, 309, 311, 4001, 1507, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 31854, "start": 323.5, "end": 323.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50613, 7587, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 31854, "start": 324.26000000000005, "end": 328.5, "text": " Air pressure is just billions of nitrogen and oxygen molecules bumping into each other.", "tokens": [50651, 5774, 3321, 307, 445, 17375, 295, 17903, 293, 9169, 13093, 9961, 278, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 31854, "start": 328.84000000000003, "end": 332.90000000000003, "text": " In the RSVP plenum, the vector flow isn't made of anything smaller.", "tokens": [50880, 682, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 11, 264, 8062, 3095, 1943, 380, 1027, 295, 1340, 4356, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 31854, "start": 333.32000000000005, "end": 335.58000000000004, "text": " It is the fundamental geometry of reality.", "tokens": [51104, 467, 307, 264, 8088, 18426, 295, 4103, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 31854, "start": 335.72, "end": 336.32000000000005, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51224, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209708502126295, "compression_ratio": 1.4311926605504588, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169077795419318e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 33632, "start": 336.32, "end": 338.78, "text": " But conceptually, yes.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3410, 671, 11, 2086, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1663254201412201, "compression_ratio": 1.4840425531914894, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671232115125553e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 33632, "start": 338.78, "end": 342.59999999999997, "text": " Think of it as pressure, wind, and heat interacting continuously.", "tokens": [50488, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 3321, 11, 2468, 11, 293, 3738, 18017, 15684, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1663254201412201, "compression_ratio": 1.4840425531914894, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671232115125553e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 33632, "start": 343.0, "end": 350.02, "text": " And that interaction leads us to the most critical mechanism in this first section, which the texts call the divergence constraint engine.", "tokens": [50699, 400, 300, 9285, 6689, 505, 281, 264, 881, 4924, 7513, 294, 341, 700, 3541, 11, 597, 264, 15765, 818, 264, 47387, 25534, 2848, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1663254201412201, "compression_ratio": 1.4840425531914894, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671232115125553e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 33632, "start": 350.44, "end": 353.28, "text": " This is where Flixion completely redefines gravity.", "tokens": [51071, 639, 307, 689, 3235, 970, 313, 2584, 38818, 1652, 12110, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1663254201412201, "compression_ratio": 1.4840425531914894, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671232115125553e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 35328, "start": 353.28, "end": 357.44, "text": " Because in this framework, gravity is not a fundamental force, is it?", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 294, 341, 8388, 11, 12110, 307, 406, 257, 8088, 3464, 11, 307, 309, 30, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926951342615588, "compression_ratio": 1.4876543209876543, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546343509406646e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 35328, "start": 357.61999999999995, "end": 359.23999999999995, "text": " It is not a primary force at all.", "tokens": [50582, 467, 307, 406, 257, 6194, 3464, 412, 439, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926951342615588, "compression_ratio": 1.4876543209876543, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546343509406646e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 35328, "start": 359.46, "end": 367.47999999999996, "text": " In the RSVP framework, gravitational attraction is constitutively identified with the entropic descent of those vector flow trajectories.", "tokens": [50674, 682, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 11, 28538, 17672, 307, 23079, 325, 3413, 9234, 365, 264, 948, 39173, 23475, 295, 729, 8062, 3095, 18257, 2083, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926951342615588, "compression_ratio": 1.4876543209876543, "no_speech_prob": 1.5546343509406646e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 36748, "start": 367.48, "end": 372.64000000000004, "text": " Okay, I'm going to need you to unpack entropic descent, because I learned in school that gravity is a pull.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 516, 281, 643, 291, 281, 26699, 948, 39173, 23475, 11, 570, 286, 3264, 294, 1395, 300, 12110, 307, 257, 2235, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 36748, "start": 373.22, "end": 377.32, "text": " You know, a mass sits in space, warps it, and just pulls things toward it.", "tokens": [50652, 509, 458, 11, 257, 2758, 12696, 294, 1901, 11, 1516, 1878, 309, 11, 293, 445, 16982, 721, 7361, 309, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 36748, "start": 377.36, "end": 378.52000000000004, "text": " Well, think about your weather map again.", "tokens": [50859, 1042, 11, 519, 466, 428, 5503, 4471, 797, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 36748, "start": 379.18, "end": 381.48, "text": " Wind doesn't blow because a magical force pulls it.", "tokens": [50950, 6320, 1177, 380, 6327, 570, 257, 12066, 3464, 16982, 309, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 36748, "start": 381.92, "end": 386.38, "text": " Wind blows because air moves from an area of high pressure to an area of low pressure.", "tokens": [51087, 6320, 18458, 570, 1988, 6067, 490, 364, 1859, 295, 1090, 3321, 281, 364, 1859, 295, 2295, 3321, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 36748, "start": 386.42, "end": 387.16, "text": " Oh, it's equalizing.", "tokens": [51312, 876, 11, 309, 311, 2681, 3319, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10697639905489408, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073595583531274e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 38716, "start": 387.16, "end": 389.20000000000005, "text": " Yes, it is resolving a gradient.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 309, 307, 49940, 257, 16235, 13, 50467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 38716, "start": 390.22, "end": 399.58000000000004, "text": " In Flixion's math, the force acting on a test particle, say a planet or just a marble, is directly proportional to the entropy gradient along the flow.", "tokens": [50518, 682, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 5221, 11, 264, 3464, 6577, 322, 257, 1500, 12359, 11, 584, 257, 5054, 420, 445, 257, 26844, 11, 307, 3838, 24969, 281, 264, 30867, 16235, 2051, 264, 3095, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 38716, "start": 400.38000000000005, "end": 402.94000000000005, "text": " Things fall because they're moving down an entropy gradient.", "tokens": [51026, 9514, 2100, 570, 436, 434, 2684, 760, 364, 30867, 16235, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 38716, "start": 403.1, "end": 403.98, "text": " That's wild.", "tokens": [51162, 663, 311, 4868, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 38716, "start": 404.20000000000005, "end": 407.32000000000005, "text": " The medium of the plenum acts like a compressible fluid.", "tokens": [51217, 440, 6399, 295, 264, 499, 268, 449, 10672, 411, 257, 14778, 964, 9113, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 38716, "start": 407.84000000000003, "end": 412.66, "text": " The scalar density, the mass, and the entropy act as physical sinks within that fluid.", "tokens": [51399, 440, 39684, 10305, 11, 264, 2758, 11, 293, 264, 30867, 605, 382, 4001, 43162, 1951, 300, 9113, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 38716, "start": 412.78000000000003, "end": 416.6, "text": " They literally force the vector flow to converge to dive down into them.", "tokens": [51646, 814, 3736, 3464, 264, 8062, 3095, 281, 41881, 281, 9192, 760, 666, 552, 13, 51837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09571023347998868, "compression_ratio": 1.7210144927536233, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671165978793032e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 41660, "start": 416.6, "end": 423.90000000000003, "text": " So it's less like a heavy bowling ball sitting on a rubber trampoline pulling marbles toward it, and more like a fluid flowing down a drain.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 1570, 411, 257, 4676, 35537, 2594, 3798, 322, 257, 11593, 38605, 18773, 8407, 1849, 8806, 7361, 309, 11, 293, 544, 411, 257, 9113, 13974, 760, 257, 12339, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 41660, "start": 424.28000000000003, "end": 426.08000000000004, "text": " And the drain itself is made of entropy.", "tokens": [50749, 400, 264, 12339, 2564, 307, 1027, 295, 30867, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 41660, "start": 426.34000000000003, "end": 426.56, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50852, 1079, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 41660, "start": 426.70000000000005, "end": 429.46000000000004, "text": " We are literally falling down a thermodynamic sinkhole.", "tokens": [50870, 492, 366, 3736, 7440, 760, 257, 8810, 34988, 9500, 14094, 13, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 41660, "start": 429.68, "end": 431.36, "text": " That captures the dynamic perfectly.", "tokens": [51019, 663, 27986, 264, 8546, 6239, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 41660, "start": 431.36, "end": 436.22, "text": " And what gives this theory such immense weight is the mathematical proof backing it up.", "tokens": [51103, 400, 437, 2709, 341, 5261, 1270, 22920, 3364, 307, 264, 18894, 8177, 19373, 309, 493, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 41660, "start": 436.88, "end": 443.5, "text": " The texts demonstrate that if you take this RSVP fluid and push it to what physicists call the stiff limit.", "tokens": [51379, 440, 15765, 11698, 300, 498, 291, 747, 341, 25855, 53, 47, 9113, 293, 2944, 309, 281, 437, 48716, 818, 264, 15451, 4948, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 41660, "start": 443.72, "end": 444.74, "text": " What does the stiff limit mean?", "tokens": [51721, 708, 775, 264, 15451, 4948, 914, 30, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12363029883159854, "compression_ratio": 1.6732673267326732, "no_speech_prob": 1.1877773070656517e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 44474, "start": 444.74, "end": 447.94, "text": " It means you assume the viscosity of the fluid goes to infinity.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 291, 6552, 264, 39744, 295, 264, 9113, 1709, 281, 13202, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 44474, "start": 448.40000000000003, "end": 453.64, "text": " If you do that, the mathematical equations perfectly derive Einstein's equations of general relativity.", "tokens": [50548, 759, 291, 360, 300, 11, 264, 18894, 11787, 6239, 28446, 23486, 311, 11787, 295, 2674, 45675, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 44474, "start": 453.82, "end": 454.34000000000003, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50819, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 44474, "start": 454.7, "end": 455.04, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50863, 1079, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 44474, "start": 455.82, "end": 461.38, "text": " General relativity simply emerges as the extreme limit of this fluid dynamics problem.", "tokens": [50919, 6996, 45675, 2935, 38965, 382, 264, 8084, 4948, 295, 341, 9113, 15679, 1154, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 44474, "start": 461.94, "end": 467.74, "text": " The cosmic expansion, the curvature of space, it's all forced by this divergence constraint.", "tokens": [51225, 440, 27614, 11260, 11, 264, 37638, 295, 1901, 11, 309, 311, 439, 7579, 538, 341, 47387, 25534, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 44474, "start": 468.08, "end": 470.46000000000004, "text": " Okay, that's if the viscosity goes to infinity.", "tokens": [51532, 1033, 11, 300, 311, 498, 264, 39744, 1709, 281, 13202, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 44474, "start": 470.68, "end": 471.46000000000004, "text": " What if it doesn't?", "tokens": [51662, 708, 498, 309, 1177, 380, 30, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 44474, "start": 471.54, "end": 473.56, "text": " What if it's, I don't know, a looser fluid?", "tokens": [51705, 708, 498, 309, 311, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 257, 450, 22150, 9113, 30, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183854738871256, "compression_ratio": 1.7292418772563176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9579734968772078e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 47356, "start": 473.56, "end": 482.92, "text": " Well, if you take the quasi-static limit, where the flow velocity changes very, very slowly, the math derives Eric Verlin's theory of entropic gravity perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 498, 291, 747, 264, 20954, 12, 34632, 4948, 11, 689, 264, 3095, 9269, 2962, 588, 11, 588, 5692, 11, 264, 5221, 1163, 1539, 9336, 4281, 5045, 311, 5261, 295, 948, 39173, 12110, 6239, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10434130259922572, "compression_ratio": 1.5589519650655022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383327428396653e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 47356, "start": 483.12, "end": 484.38, "text": " I vaguely remember that.", "tokens": [50843, 286, 13501, 48863, 1604, 300, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10434130259922572, "compression_ratio": 1.5589519650655022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383327428396653e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 47356, "start": 484.58, "end": 492.18, "text": " Verlin proposed years ago that gravity was an emergent thermodynamic phenomenon, but he really struggled to provide the underlying substrate for it.", "tokens": [50916, 4281, 5045, 10348, 924, 2057, 300, 12110, 390, 364, 4345, 6930, 8810, 34988, 14029, 11, 457, 415, 534, 19023, 281, 2893, 264, 14217, 27585, 337, 309, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10434130259922572, "compression_ratio": 1.5589519650655022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383327428396653e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 47356, "start": 492.44, "end": 493.32, "text": " Fliction provides it.", "tokens": [51309, 3235, 4105, 6417, 309, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10434130259922572, "compression_ratio": 1.5589519650655022, "no_speech_prob": 1.4383327428396653e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 49332, "start": 493.32, "end": 499.84, "text": " Okay, that is already a massive paradigm shift for physics alone, but here's where it gets really wild for me.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 300, 307, 1217, 257, 5994, 24709, 5513, 337, 10649, 3312, 11, 457, 510, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 4868, 337, 385, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.114353211199651, "compression_ratio": 1.3978494623655915, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251370447063824e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 49332, "start": 499.84, "end": 507.64, "text": " As I was going through the notes, the slides we're looking at show that this exact same RSVP math applies across multiple, totally different domains.", "tokens": [50691, 1018, 286, 390, 516, 807, 264, 5570, 11, 264, 9788, 321, 434, 1237, 412, 855, 300, 341, 1900, 912, 25855, 53, 47, 5221, 13165, 2108, 3866, 11, 3879, 819, 25514, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.114353211199651, "compression_ratio": 1.3978494623655915, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251370447063824e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 50764, "start": 507.64, "end": 509.08, "text": " Yes, it's extremely versatile.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 309, 311, 4664, 25057, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15272919149959788, "compression_ratio": 1.5347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250379506257186e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 50764, "start": 509.3, "end": 512.18, "text": " Fliction calls it the ontological translation matrix.", "tokens": [50448, 3235, 4105, 5498, 309, 264, 6592, 4383, 12853, 8141, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15272919149959788, "compression_ratio": 1.5347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250379506257186e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 50764, "start": 512.9, "end": 517.0, "text": " In cosmology, the pressure, wind, and heat yield space-time and gravity.", "tokens": [50628, 682, 22207, 1793, 11, 264, 3321, 11, 2468, 11, 293, 3738, 11257, 1901, 12, 3766, 293, 12110, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15272919149959788, "compression_ratio": 1.5347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250379506257186e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 50764, "start": 517.48, "end": 522.36, "text": " But in cognitive science, the exact same mathematical projection yields the free energy principle.", "tokens": [50857, 583, 294, 15605, 3497, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 18894, 22743, 32168, 264, 1737, 2281, 8665, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15272919149959788, "compression_ratio": 1.5347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250379506257186e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 50764, "start": 522.78, "end": 528.06, "text": " Which is the prevailing unifying theory of the brain, championed by neuroscientist Carl Fristen.", "tokens": [51122, 3013, 307, 264, 12642, 23315, 517, 5489, 5261, 295, 264, 3567, 11, 10971, 292, 538, 28813, 5412, 468, 14256, 1526, 4821, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15272919149959788, "compression_ratio": 1.5347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250379506257186e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 52806, "start": 528.06, "end": 533.28, "text": " Right. Fristen's whole thing is that the brain is basically an inference engine trying to minimize surprise.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 1526, 4821, 311, 1379, 551, 307, 300, 264, 3567, 307, 1936, 364, 38253, 2848, 1382, 281, 17522, 6365, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 52806, "start": 533.78, "end": 536.78, "text": " It wants to predict the world so it doesn't get eaten by a tiger.", "tokens": [50651, 467, 2738, 281, 6069, 264, 1002, 370, 309, 1177, 380, 483, 12158, 538, 257, 21432, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 52806, "start": 537.3599999999999, "end": 544.9399999999999, "text": " And Fliction is saying that the brain minimizing surprise is mathematically identical to a planet falling down an entropy gradient in space.", "tokens": [50830, 400, 3235, 4105, 307, 1566, 300, 264, 3567, 46608, 6365, 307, 44003, 14800, 281, 257, 5054, 7440, 760, 364, 30867, 16235, 294, 1901, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 52806, "start": 545.16, "end": 547.02, "text": " It is an exact mathematical mapping.", "tokens": [51220, 467, 307, 364, 1900, 18894, 18350, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 52806, "start": 547.9399999999999, "end": 551.8599999999999, "text": " In cognition, the scalar field is the density of meaning, or belief.", "tokens": [51359, 682, 46905, 11, 264, 39684, 2519, 307, 264, 10305, 295, 3620, 11, 420, 7107, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 52806, "start": 552.3, "end": 555.42, "text": " The vector flow is directed cognitive action, or inference.", "tokens": [51577, 440, 8062, 3095, 307, 12898, 15605, 3069, 11, 420, 38253, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15176483436867041, "compression_ratio": 1.736462093862816, "no_speech_prob": 1.6299856429868864e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 55542, "start": 555.42, "end": 558.24, "text": " And the entropy is the sensory surprise.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 30867, 307, 264, 27233, 6365, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 55542, "start": 558.62, "end": 559.4399999999999, "text": " That's incredible.", "tokens": [50525, 663, 311, 4651, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 55542, "start": 559.6999999999999, "end": 565.2199999999999, "text": " The brain-resolving cognitive dissonance follows the exact same fluid dynamics as a planet orbiting a star.", "tokens": [50579, 440, 3567, 12, 495, 401, 798, 15605, 717, 3015, 719, 10002, 264, 1900, 912, 9113, 15679, 382, 257, 5054, 48985, 257, 3543, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 55542, "start": 566.0, "end": 567.28, "text": " And Fliction doesn't stop there.", "tokens": [50894, 400, 3235, 4105, 1177, 380, 1590, 456, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 55542, "start": 567.64, "end": 571.42, "text": " The texts extend this to sociology with something called sphere-pop mechanics.", "tokens": [50976, 440, 15765, 10101, 341, 281, 41744, 365, 746, 1219, 16687, 12, 13872, 12939, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 55542, "start": 571.5999999999999, "end": 574.36, "text": " Right, the mechanics of institutions. I remember reading that part.", "tokens": [51174, 1779, 11, 264, 12939, 295, 8142, 13, 286, 1604, 3760, 300, 644, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 55542, "start": 574.7199999999999, "end": 575.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51330, 1079, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 55542, "start": 575.88, "end": 579.42, "text": " Human social institutions are modeled as bounding spheres in this fluid.", "tokens": [51388, 10294, 2093, 8142, 366, 37140, 382, 5472, 278, 41225, 294, 341, 9113, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 55542, "start": 580.42, "end": 584.76, "text": " The scalar potential is the institution's core meaning or ideological mass.", "tokens": [51615, 440, 39684, 3995, 307, 264, 7818, 311, 4965, 3620, 420, 35341, 2758, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15277618472859011, "compression_ratio": 1.6812080536912752, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204061084410196e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 58476, "start": 584.76, "end": 588.7, "text": " The vector flow is its institutional drive or trajectory.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8062, 3095, 307, 1080, 18391, 3332, 420, 21512, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 58476, "start": 589.8, "end": 594.0, "text": " And the entropy is the institutional friction, like the bureaucratic ritual cost.", "tokens": [50617, 400, 264, 30867, 307, 264, 18391, 17710, 11, 411, 264, 26360, 25198, 13792, 2063, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 58476, "start": 594.46, "end": 597.92, "text": " So dealing with red tape is literally societal entropy.", "tokens": [50850, 407, 6260, 365, 2182, 7314, 307, 3736, 33472, 30867, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 58476, "start": 598.36, "end": 598.64, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51045, 7587, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 58476, "start": 598.98, "end": 606.7, "text": " Two institutions, say, two corporations or two governments, only merge if the thermodynamic pressure between them overcomes their boundary resistance.", "tokens": [51076, 4453, 8142, 11, 584, 11, 732, 17676, 420, 732, 11280, 11, 787, 22183, 498, 264, 8810, 34988, 3321, 1296, 552, 670, 9055, 641, 12866, 7335, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 58476, "start": 606.96, "end": 608.52, "text": " It is unification by substrate.", "tokens": [51475, 467, 307, 517, 3774, 538, 27585, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 58476, "start": 608.92, "end": 610.4399999999999, "text": " Not just analogy, but substrate.", "tokens": [51573, 1726, 445, 21663, 11, 457, 27585, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16287787242602275, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674099388199303e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 61044, "start": 610.44, "end": 617.44, "text": " Which leads to what might be the most terrifyingly beautiful concept in this whole first section, the unified failure modes.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 6689, 281, 437, 1062, 312, 264, 881, 18106, 356, 2238, 3410, 294, 341, 1379, 700, 3541, 11, 264, 26787, 7763, 14068, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331047058105468, "compression_ratio": 1.5936073059360731, "no_speech_prob": 1.734686396262508e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 61044, "start": 617.7600000000001, "end": 623.5200000000001, "text": " Because if the math is identical across all these systems, the way these systems die must also be identical, right?", "tokens": [50731, 1436, 498, 264, 5221, 307, 14800, 2108, 439, 613, 3652, 11, 264, 636, 613, 3652, 978, 1633, 611, 312, 14800, 11, 558, 30, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331047058105468, "compression_ratio": 1.5936073059360731, "no_speech_prob": 1.734686396262508e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 61044, "start": 623.6, "end": 625.3000000000001, "text": " That is the inescapable conclusion.", "tokens": [51023, 663, 307, 264, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 10063, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331047058105468, "compression_ratio": 1.5936073059360731, "no_speech_prob": 1.734686396262508e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 61044, "start": 625.84, "end": 629.2800000000001, "text": " The theorem states that in what Fliction terms the Lamford dying regime.", "tokens": [51135, 440, 20904, 4368, 300, 294, 437, 3235, 4105, 2115, 264, 18825, 7404, 8639, 13120, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331047058105468, "compression_ratio": 1.5936073059360731, "no_speech_prob": 1.734686396262508e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 62928, "start": 629.28, "end": 630.3399999999999, "text": " Which is what, exactly?", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 437, 11, 2293, 30, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 62928, "start": 630.48, "end": 635.1999999999999, "text": " It's essentially the state where the injection of order or nigentropy into the system completely stops.", "tokens": [50425, 467, 311, 4476, 264, 1785, 689, 264, 22873, 295, 1668, 420, 26996, 317, 27514, 666, 264, 1185, 2584, 10094, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 62928, "start": 635.56, "end": 639.48, "text": " When that happens, both the scalar and vector gradients decay exponentially to zero.", "tokens": [50679, 1133, 300, 2314, 11, 1293, 264, 39684, 293, 8062, 2771, 2448, 21039, 37330, 281, 4018, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 62928, "start": 639.8199999999999, "end": 641.28, "text": " The gradients flatten out entirely.", "tokens": [50892, 440, 2771, 2448, 24183, 484, 7696, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 62928, "start": 641.66, "end": 644.8399999999999, "text": " So going back to the weather map, that means the map goes totally blank.", "tokens": [50984, 407, 516, 646, 281, 264, 5503, 4471, 11, 300, 1355, 264, 4471, 1709, 3879, 8247, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 62928, "start": 645.3, "end": 646.98, "text": " There are no high or low pressure zones.", "tokens": [51166, 821, 366, 572, 1090, 420, 2295, 3321, 16025, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 62928, "start": 647.14, "end": 648.38, "text": " There are no temperature differences.", "tokens": [51258, 821, 366, 572, 4292, 7300, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 62928, "start": 648.62, "end": 651.62, "text": " And because of that, there is absolutely zero wind.", "tokens": [51332, 400, 570, 295, 300, 11, 456, 307, 3122, 4018, 2468, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 62928, "start": 652.02, "end": 652.72, "text": " Nothing moves.", "tokens": [51502, 6693, 6067, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14529843915972793, "compression_ratio": 1.632867132867133, "no_speech_prob": 1.69450488796824e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 65272, "start": 652.72, "end": 653.0400000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 65272, "start": 653.44, "end": 657.22, "text": " And what does a flat gradient look like in the real world?", "tokens": [50401, 400, 437, 775, 257, 4962, 16235, 574, 411, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 30, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 65272, "start": 657.74, "end": 660.94, "text": " In cosmology, physicists call it the cosmic heat death.", "tokens": [50616, 682, 22207, 1793, 11, 48716, 818, 309, 264, 27614, 3738, 2966, 13, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 65272, "start": 661.26, "end": 663.0400000000001, "text": " Just a cold, dark universe.", "tokens": [50792, 1449, 257, 3554, 11, 2877, 6445, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 65272, "start": 663.4, "end": 667.22, "text": " The universe expands and cools until everything is the exact same temperature.", "tokens": [50899, 440, 6445, 33706, 293, 42883, 1826, 1203, 307, 264, 1900, 912, 4292, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 65272, "start": 667.48, "end": 670.0400000000001, "text": " And no thermodynamic work can ever be done again.", "tokens": [51103, 400, 572, 8810, 34988, 589, 393, 1562, 312, 1096, 797, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 65272, "start": 670.5, "end": 671.58, "text": " Everything just stops.", "tokens": [51254, 5471, 445, 10094, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 65272, "start": 672.08, "end": 679.26, "text": " Now in human cognition, the text maps this flat gradient to agency collapse or functional brain deadness.", "tokens": [51333, 823, 294, 1952, 46905, 11, 264, 2487, 11317, 341, 4962, 16235, 281, 7934, 15584, 420, 11745, 3567, 3116, 1287, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 65272, "start": 679.26, "end": 681.94, "text": " Because there's no gradient for the thoughts to flow down.", "tokens": [51692, 1436, 456, 311, 572, 16235, 337, 264, 4598, 281, 3095, 760, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19763073168302836, "compression_ratio": 1.6055363321799307, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 68194, "start": 681.94, "end": 682.5200000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 68194, "start": 682.82, "end": 687.2800000000001, "text": " Without a scalar gradient, without a concentration of meaning, the cognitive vector flow halts.", "tokens": [50409, 9129, 257, 39684, 16235, 11, 1553, 257, 9856, 295, 3620, 11, 264, 15605, 8062, 3095, 7523, 1373, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 68194, "start": 687.72, "end": 690.74, "text": " You have no directed action, no inference, no ability to make a choice.", "tokens": [50654, 509, 362, 572, 12898, 3069, 11, 572, 38253, 11, 572, 3485, 281, 652, 257, 3922, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 68194, "start": 690.82, "end": 691.46, "text": " And society.", "tokens": [50809, 400, 4086, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 68194, "start": 691.6, "end": 695.44, "text": " And society, a slack gradient manifests as institutional rigidity.", "tokens": [50848, 400, 4086, 11, 257, 29767, 16235, 50252, 382, 18391, 8329, 17711, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 68194, "start": 695.9000000000001, "end": 700.1400000000001, "text": " The societal vorticity decays, the circulation of ideas and resources halts,", "tokens": [51063, 440, 33472, 371, 477, 44198, 979, 3772, 11, 264, 23168, 295, 3487, 293, 3593, 7523, 1373, 11, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 68194, "start": 700.4200000000001, "end": 705.84, "text": " and you are left with massive, unmergable, totally rigid bureaucracies that cannot adapt or act.", "tokens": [51289, 293, 291, 366, 1411, 365, 5994, 11, 517, 936, 70, 712, 11, 3879, 22195, 26360, 12080, 530, 300, 2644, 6231, 420, 605, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 68194, "start": 706.12, "end": 707.5600000000001, "text": " It's just incredible.", "tokens": [51574, 467, 311, 445, 4651, 13, 51646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1612338522206182, "compression_ratio": 1.6569343065693432, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112782324344878e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 70756, "start": 707.56, "end": 711.38, "text": " The heat death of the universe, a person losing their cognitive agency,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3738, 2966, 295, 264, 6445, 11, 257, 954, 7027, 641, 15605, 7934, 11, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 70756, "start": 712.0799999999999, "end": 718.14, "text": " and a stalled, bloated government bureaucracy are mathematically the exact same phenomena.", "tokens": [50591, 293, 257, 342, 8907, 11, 1749, 770, 2463, 44671, 366, 44003, 264, 1900, 912, 22004, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 70756, "start": 718.2199999999999, "end": 719.3399999999999, "text": " Under this framework, yes.", "tokens": [50898, 6974, 341, 8388, 11, 2086, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 70756, "start": 719.78, "end": 722.1999999999999, "text": " They are all just a flattened RSVP field.", "tokens": [50976, 814, 366, 439, 445, 257, 24183, 292, 25855, 53, 47, 2519, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 70756, "start": 722.3, "end": 724.64, "text": " But you know, as I was reading this, I kept hitting a wall.", "tokens": [51102, 583, 291, 458, 11, 382, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 11, 286, 4305, 8850, 257, 2929, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 70756, "start": 725.04, "end": 729.2199999999999, "text": " If reality is just this continuous fluid of scalar and vector fields,", "tokens": [51239, 759, 4103, 307, 445, 341, 10957, 9113, 295, 39684, 293, 8062, 7909, 11, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 70756, "start": 729.4, "end": 731.3599999999999, "text": " well, fluids can slosh backward.", "tokens": [51457, 731, 11, 33033, 393, 1061, 3019, 23897, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1268189779602655, "compression_ratio": 1.5390625, "no_speech_prob": 1.825333937818807e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 73136, "start": 731.36, "end": 735.12, "text": " If it's just pressure and wind, wind can change direction.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 309, 311, 445, 3321, 293, 2468, 11, 2468, 393, 1319, 3513, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 73136, "start": 735.52, "end": 736.58, "text": " Real life doesn't.", "tokens": [50573, 8467, 993, 1177, 380, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 73136, "start": 736.94, "end": 739.14, "text": " That's the core paradox of thermodynamics.", "tokens": [50644, 663, 311, 264, 4965, 26221, 295, 8810, 35483, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 73136, "start": 739.46, "end": 739.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50770, 1779, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 73136, "start": 739.92, "end": 745.0600000000001, "text": " If this theory is the substrate of everything, it has to explain why time only flows one way.", "tokens": [50793, 759, 341, 5261, 307, 264, 27585, 295, 1203, 11, 309, 575, 281, 2903, 983, 565, 787, 12867, 472, 636, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 73136, "start": 745.62, "end": 749.28, "text": " If it can't explain why I can't unburn a piece of toast, the whole theory falls apart.", "tokens": [51078, 759, 309, 393, 380, 2903, 983, 286, 393, 380, 517, 21763, 257, 2522, 295, 15354, 11, 264, 1379, 5261, 8804, 4936, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 73136, "start": 749.74, "end": 752.24, "text": " So how does fliction actually solve the problem of time?", "tokens": [51284, 407, 577, 775, 932, 4105, 767, 5039, 264, 1154, 295, 565, 30, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15882947709825304, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349564710236742e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 75224, "start": 752.24, "end": 758.26, "text": " You've identified the crucial missing piece, which is the sole focus of the second monograph in our stack,", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 9234, 264, 11462, 5361, 2522, 11, 597, 307, 264, 12321, 1879, 295, 264, 1150, 1108, 3108, 294, 527, 8630, 11, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 75224, "start": 758.72, "end": 760.34, "text": " adjunction and irreversibility.", "tokens": [50689, 614, 10010, 882, 293, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 75224, "start": 760.84, "end": 764.42, "text": " The problem of the arrow of time has plagued physics for over a century.", "tokens": [50795, 440, 1154, 295, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 575, 33756, 5827, 10649, 337, 670, 257, 4901, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 75224, "start": 764.94, "end": 767.48, "text": " Because the basic equations work backward and forward.", "tokens": [51000, 1436, 264, 3875, 11787, 589, 23897, 293, 2128, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 75224, "start": 767.9, "end": 768.4, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51148, 7587, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 75224, "start": 769.22, "end": 774.0, "text": " Classical thermodynamics tells us that entropy always increases in a closed system.", "tokens": [51214, 9471, 804, 8810, 35483, 5112, 505, 300, 30867, 1009, 8637, 294, 257, 5395, 1185, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 75224, "start": 774.88, "end": 776.78, "text": " The burned toast cannot unburn.", "tokens": [51497, 440, 13490, 15354, 2644, 517, 21763, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 75224, "start": 777.62, "end": 781.22, "text": " But as Flixion points out, that is merely a phenomenological gloss.", "tokens": [51634, 583, 382, 3235, 970, 313, 2793, 484, 11, 300, 307, 17003, 257, 9388, 4383, 19574, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17998205876983372, "compression_ratio": 1.571917808219178, "no_speech_prob": 1.3886480940833446e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 78122, "start": 781.22, "end": 782.9200000000001, "text": " Meaning it's just an observation.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 309, 311, 445, 364, 14816, 13, 50450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 78122, "start": 783.12, "end": 786.6, "text": " We see it happening, so we write it down as a rule, but we don't know why.", "tokens": [50460, 492, 536, 309, 2737, 11, 370, 321, 2464, 309, 760, 382, 257, 4978, 11, 457, 321, 500, 380, 458, 983, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 78122, "start": 786.78, "end": 787.22, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50643, 48746, 736, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 78122, "start": 787.36, "end": 789.7, "text": " It's an observation, not a structural cause.", "tokens": [50672, 467, 311, 364, 14816, 11, 406, 257, 15067, 3082, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 78122, "start": 790.72, "end": 795.14, "text": " Thermodynamics doesn't tell us why the asymmetry exists at a fundamental geometric level.", "tokens": [50840, 38957, 35483, 1177, 380, 980, 505, 983, 264, 37277, 9889, 8198, 412, 257, 8088, 33246, 1496, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 78122, "start": 795.6, "end": 799.36, "text": " Especially when you try to apply this to cognitive or semantic systems.", "tokens": [51084, 8545, 562, 291, 853, 281, 3079, 341, 281, 15605, 420, 47982, 3652, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 78122, "start": 799.6600000000001, "end": 799.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51287, 1779, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 78122, "start": 800.02, "end": 802.64, "text": " Because in a brain, heat isn't thermal agitation.", "tokens": [51305, 1436, 294, 257, 3567, 11, 3738, 1943, 380, 15070, 623, 4614, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 78122, "start": 802.94, "end": 803.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51451, 7587, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 78122, "start": 803.52, "end": 806.0400000000001, "text": " It's a structured incompatibility between ideas.", "tokens": [51480, 467, 311, 257, 18519, 40393, 267, 2841, 1296, 3487, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 78122, "start": 806.48, "end": 810.14, "text": " So why does a thought process or a universe only move forward?", "tokens": [51628, 407, 983, 775, 257, 1194, 1399, 420, 257, 6445, 787, 1286, 2128, 30, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1703544018873528, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 2.4372702207148267e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 81014, "start": 810.14, "end": 820.04, "text": " Flixion proposes a structural theorem for irreversibility based on the transition from a continuous field space, or RSVP plenum, to a discrete history space.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 970, 313, 2365, 4201, 257, 15067, 20904, 337, 16014, 840, 2841, 2361, 322, 264, 6034, 490, 257, 10957, 2519, 1901, 11, 420, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 11, 281, 257, 27706, 2503, 1901, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1243486215572546, "compression_ratio": 1.6133828996282529, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549591779115413e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 81014, "start": 820.16, "end": 822.98, "text": " Okay, what does that transition look like, continuous to discrete?", "tokens": [50866, 1033, 11, 437, 775, 300, 6034, 574, 411, 11, 10957, 281, 27706, 30, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1243486215572546, "compression_ratio": 1.6133828996282529, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549591779115413e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 81014, "start": 823.28, "end": 831.86, "text": " Think about taking a perfectly continuous, unbroken line drawn on a piece of paper and trying to represent that line by placing a series of discrete, separate dots over it.", "tokens": [51022, 6557, 466, 1940, 257, 6239, 10957, 11, 517, 37947, 1622, 10117, 322, 257, 2522, 295, 3035, 293, 1382, 281, 2906, 300, 1622, 538, 17221, 257, 2638, 295, 27706, 11, 4994, 15026, 670, 309, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1243486215572546, "compression_ratio": 1.6133828996282529, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549591779115413e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 81014, "start": 831.92, "end": 833.72, "text": " Like digitizing an old vinyl record.", "tokens": [51454, 1743, 14293, 3319, 364, 1331, 25226, 2136, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1243486215572546, "compression_ratio": 1.6133828996282529, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549591779115413e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 83372, "start": 833.72, "end": 834.58, "text": " Great analogy.", "tokens": [50365, 3769, 21663, 13, 50408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 83372, "start": 835.1800000000001, "end": 840.58, "text": " When you digitize or discretize something continuous, information is fundamentally lost.", "tokens": [50438, 1133, 291, 14293, 1125, 420, 25656, 1125, 746, 10957, 11, 1589, 307, 17879, 2731, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 83372, "start": 841.02, "end": 843.9200000000001, "text": " Unless the mathematical mapping is perfectly injective.", "tokens": [50730, 16581, 264, 18894, 18350, 307, 6239, 10711, 488, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 83372, "start": 844.0600000000001, "end": 844.78, "text": " Injective.", "tokens": [50882, 682, 1020, 488, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 83372, "start": 844.94, "end": 850.1800000000001, "text": " In mathematics, an injective function means there is a perfect, flawless one-to-one match.", "tokens": [50926, 682, 18666, 11, 364, 10711, 488, 2445, 1355, 456, 307, 257, 2176, 11, 45693, 472, 12, 1353, 12, 546, 2995, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 83372, "start": 851.0, "end": 855.74, "text": " No two distinct points in the continuous field map to the exact same discrete dot.", "tokens": [51229, 883, 732, 10644, 2793, 294, 264, 10957, 2519, 4471, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 27706, 5893, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18905655930681928, "compression_ratio": 1.6618357487922706, "no_speech_prob": 1.668483602147719e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 85574, "start": 855.74, "end": 858.76, "text": " But the universe is not perfectly injective.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 6445, 307, 406, 6239, 10711, 488, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 85574, "start": 859.38, "end": 863.0600000000001, "text": " I'm trying to think of a real-world example of this discretization process.", "tokens": [50547, 286, 478, 1382, 281, 519, 295, 257, 957, 12, 13217, 1365, 295, 341, 25656, 2144, 1399, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 85574, "start": 863.42, "end": 866.26, "text": " Because dots on a line is still a bit abstract for me.", "tokens": [50749, 1436, 15026, 322, 257, 1622, 307, 920, 257, 857, 12649, 337, 385, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 85574, "start": 866.52, "end": 870.14, "text": " Think about a complex physical process that breaks down a hole into parts.", "tokens": [50904, 6557, 466, 257, 3997, 4001, 1399, 300, 9857, 760, 257, 5458, 666, 3166, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 85574, "start": 870.24, "end": 872.58, "text": " Okay, like a meat grinder.", "tokens": [51090, 1033, 11, 411, 257, 4615, 41424, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 85574, "start": 872.76, "end": 873.26, "text": " Let's follow that.", "tokens": [51216, 961, 311, 1524, 300, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 85574, "start": 873.58, "end": 879.04, "text": " If I have a cow, which is a continuous, highly complex, structured biological system,", "tokens": [51257, 759, 286, 362, 257, 8408, 11, 597, 307, 257, 10957, 11, 5405, 3997, 11, 18519, 13910, 1185, 11, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469490070535679, "compression_ratio": 1.5098814229249011, "no_speech_prob": 1.5980811509178072e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 87904, "start": 879.04, "end": 883.66, "text": " and I put that cow through an industrial meat grinder, I get a hamburger patty out the other side.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 286, 829, 300, 8408, 807, 364, 9987, 4615, 41424, 11, 286, 483, 257, 34575, 1947, 874, 484, 264, 661, 1252, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 87904, "start": 883.8399999999999, "end": 885.18, "text": " A very grim picture, but yes.", "tokens": [50605, 316, 588, 36010, 3036, 11, 457, 2086, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 87904, "start": 885.26, "end": 887.0, "text": " The patty is a discrete event.", "tokens": [50676, 440, 1947, 874, 307, 257, 27706, 2280, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 87904, "start": 887.16, "end": 893.76, "text": " Now, mathematically, I suppose you could map the journey of every single cut of beef, every cell, as it goes through the blades and ends up in the patty.", "tokens": [50771, 823, 11, 44003, 11, 286, 7297, 291, 727, 4471, 264, 4671, 295, 633, 2167, 1723, 295, 9256, 11, 633, 2815, 11, 382, 309, 1709, 807, 264, 20066, 293, 5314, 493, 294, 264, 1947, 874, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 87904, "start": 893.8399999999999, "end": 894.24, "text": " You could.", "tokens": [51105, 509, 727, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 87904, "start": 894.5, "end": 897.04, "text": " The forward equation is theoretically calculable.", "tokens": [51138, 440, 2128, 5367, 307, 29400, 4322, 712, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 87904, "start": 897.06, "end": 898.3199999999999, "text": " But the irreversibility.", "tokens": [51266, 583, 264, 16014, 840, 2841, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 87904, "start": 898.54, "end": 901.78, "text": " I could never run the hamburger backward through the grinder and get the cow.", "tokens": [51340, 286, 727, 1128, 1190, 264, 34575, 23897, 807, 264, 41424, 293, 483, 264, 8408, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10750724048149295, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.832638207854842e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 90178, "start": 901.78, "end": 907.74, "text": " The information about the cow's original cellular structure, the way the muscles connected to the bones,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1589, 466, 264, 8408, 311, 3380, 29267, 3877, 11, 264, 636, 264, 9530, 4582, 281, 264, 10491, 11, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 90178, "start": 907.92, "end": 911.48, "text": " it's all obliterated by the process of turning it into a discrete patty.", "tokens": [50672, 309, 311, 439, 23740, 1681, 770, 538, 264, 1399, 295, 6246, 309, 666, 257, 27706, 1947, 874, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 90178, "start": 911.66, "end": 914.14, "text": " You just can't reconstruct the cow from the burger.", "tokens": [50859, 509, 445, 393, 380, 31499, 264, 8408, 490, 264, 16393, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 90178, "start": 914.3399999999999, "end": 916.52, "text": " That's a brilliantly visceral analogy.", "tokens": [50993, 663, 311, 257, 8695, 42580, 1452, 47879, 21663, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 90178, "start": 916.66, "end": 918.86, "text": " And it perfectly encapsulates the math.", "tokens": [51109, 400, 309, 6239, 38745, 26192, 264, 5221, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 90178, "start": 919.0799999999999, "end": 923.56, "text": " Fliction defines irreversibility precisely as this reconstruction defect.", "tokens": [51230, 3235, 4105, 23122, 16014, 840, 2841, 13402, 382, 341, 31565, 16445, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 90178, "start": 923.8399999999999, "end": 924.04, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51468, 865, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 90178, "start": 924.3399999999999, "end": 930.8399999999999, "text": " The universe operates as a continuous field, but events, the things that actually happen to get recorded, are discrete.", "tokens": [51493, 440, 6445, 22577, 382, 257, 10957, 2519, 11, 457, 3931, 11, 264, 721, 300, 767, 1051, 281, 483, 8287, 11, 366, 27706, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14218759536743164, "compression_ratio": 1.6933333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.3617889368239267e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 93084, "start": 930.84, "end": 932.34, "text": " They're the hamburger patties.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 434, 264, 34575, 49916, 530, 13, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 93084, "start": 932.5, "end": 932.6600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50448, 1079, 13, 50456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 93084, "start": 932.96, "end": 937.7, "text": " When the continuous RSVP field is discretized into events, you generate a history.", "tokens": [50471, 1133, 264, 10957, 25855, 53, 47, 2519, 307, 25656, 1602, 666, 3931, 11, 291, 8460, 257, 2503, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 93084, "start": 938.4, "end": 945.38, "text": " And because the mapping is not perfectly injective, you cannot perfectly invert the map from that discrete history back to the continuous state.", "tokens": [50743, 400, 570, 264, 18350, 307, 406, 6239, 10711, 488, 11, 291, 2644, 6239, 33966, 264, 4471, 490, 300, 27706, 2503, 646, 281, 264, 10957, 1785, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 93084, "start": 945.74, "end": 946.5, "text": " The cow is gone.", "tokens": [51110, 440, 8408, 307, 2780, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 93084, "start": 946.72, "end": 949.96, "text": " So the arrow of time isn't like a force pushing us forward.", "tokens": [51159, 407, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 1943, 380, 411, 257, 3464, 7380, 505, 2128, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 93084, "start": 950.1, "end": 953.5, "text": " Time is just the impossibility of going backward because the data has been destroyed.", "tokens": [51328, 6161, 307, 445, 264, 38802, 2841, 295, 516, 23897, 570, 264, 1412, 575, 668, 8937, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 93084, "start": 953.82, "end": 954.26, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51514, 7587, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 93084, "start": 954.7, "end": 958.2800000000001, "text": " The text states that the entropy defect isn't thermal heat.", "tokens": [51558, 440, 2487, 4368, 300, 264, 30867, 16445, 1943, 380, 15070, 3738, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276222135199875, "compression_ratio": 1.7307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609825935846255e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 95828, "start": 958.28, "end": 961.9399999999999, "text": " It is the measure-theoretic shadow of that lost information.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 3481, 12, 3322, 26262, 299, 8576, 295, 300, 2731, 1589, 13, 50548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 95828, "start": 963.1, "end": 969.66, "text": " To prove this, Fliction utilizes a highly complex mathematical tool called the Jensen-Shannon divergence.", "tokens": [50606, 1407, 7081, 341, 11, 3235, 4105, 4976, 5660, 257, 5405, 3997, 18894, 2290, 1219, 264, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 47387, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 95828, "start": 970.1, "end": 972.28, "text": " I saw that term in the papers and immediately glazed over.", "tokens": [50956, 286, 1866, 300, 1433, 294, 264, 10577, 293, 4258, 8771, 11312, 670, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 95828, "start": 972.4399999999999, "end": 974.04, "text": " What is a Jensen-Shannon divergence?", "tokens": [51073, 708, 307, 257, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 47387, 30, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 95828, "start": 974.62, "end": 978.6999999999999, "text": " It is a way of measuring the similarity between two probability distributions.", "tokens": [51182, 467, 307, 257, 636, 295, 13389, 264, 32194, 1296, 732, 8482, 37870, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 95828, "start": 979.5799999999999, "end": 984.8199999999999, "text": " Imagine two slightly different paths the system could take that end up at the exact same final state.", "tokens": [51430, 11739, 732, 4748, 819, 14518, 264, 1185, 727, 747, 300, 917, 493, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 2572, 1785, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 95828, "start": 984.92, "end": 985.16, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51697, 1033, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13421865340766556, "compression_ratio": 1.6151079136690647, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622698005731463e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 98516, "start": 985.16, "end": 995.42, "text": " The Jensen-Shannon divergence measures exactly how much distinct information is destroyed when the universe blurs the distinction between those two paths and just records the final destination.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 47387, 8000, 2293, 577, 709, 10644, 1589, 307, 8937, 562, 264, 6445, 888, 2156, 264, 16844, 1296, 729, 732, 14518, 293, 445, 7724, 264, 2572, 12236, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06527455260113972, "compression_ratio": 1.7196652719665273, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 98516, "start": 995.8199999999999, "end": 1001.48, "text": " The higher the divergence, the more information is lost and the more violently irreversible the process is.", "tokens": [50898, 440, 2946, 264, 47387, 11, 264, 544, 1589, 307, 2731, 293, 264, 544, 46728, 16014, 840, 964, 264, 1399, 307, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06527455260113972, "compression_ratio": 1.7196652719665273, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 98516, "start": 1001.76, "end": 1006.98, "text": " The arrow of time is literally generated by the universe failing to keep track of its own continuous nuances.", "tokens": [51195, 440, 11610, 295, 565, 307, 3736, 10833, 538, 264, 6445, 18223, 281, 1066, 2837, 295, 1080, 1065, 10957, 38775, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06527455260113972, "compression_ratio": 1.7196652719665273, "no_speech_prob": 1.890336194868003e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 100698, "start": 1006.98, "end": 1016.86, "text": " And the mechanism doing the grinding, the thing that is actually chopping the continuous reality into a discrete history, is a mathematical operator Fliction calls refuse.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 7513, 884, 264, 25300, 11, 264, 551, 300, 307, 767, 35205, 264, 10957, 4103, 666, 257, 27706, 2503, 11, 307, 257, 18894, 12973, 3235, 4105, 5498, 16791, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20901159003928857, "compression_ratio": 1.4606741573033708, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499339209277933e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 100698, "start": 1017.58, "end": 1017.88, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50895, 1079, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20901159003928857, "compression_ratio": 1.4606741573033708, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499339209277933e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 100698, "start": 1018.44, "end": 1022.4200000000001, "text": " This comes from the SpherePop calculus we mentioned earlier regarding institutions.", "tokens": [50938, 639, 1487, 490, 264, 318, 6605, 38677, 33400, 321, 2835, 3071, 8595, 8142, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20901159003928857, "compression_ratio": 1.4606741573033708, "no_speech_prob": 1.9499339209277933e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 102242, "start": 1022.42, "end": 1027.98, "text": " The SpherePop calculus has several event operators that govern how systems interact.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 318, 6605, 38677, 33400, 575, 2940, 2280, 19077, 300, 1980, 577, 3652, 4648, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 102242, "start": 1028.74, "end": 1033.5, "text": " There's POP for creation, bind for connection, collapse for destruction.", "tokens": [50681, 821, 311, 430, 12059, 337, 8016, 11, 14786, 337, 4984, 11, 15584, 337, 13563, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 102242, "start": 1033.98, "end": 1037.22, "text": " But the refuse operator is the critical engine for time.", "tokens": [50943, 583, 264, 16791, 12973, 307, 264, 4924, 2848, 337, 565, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 102242, "start": 1037.58, "end": 1038.1599999999999, "text": " Oh, so.", "tokens": [51123, 876, 11, 370, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 102242, "start": 1038.58, "end": 1043.3, "text": " The refuse operator structurally restricts admissible future continuations.", "tokens": [51173, 440, 16791, 12973, 6594, 6512, 7694, 82, 5910, 41073, 2027, 2993, 763, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 102242, "start": 1043.72, "end": 1048.28, "text": " It acts as a physical filter that permanently blocks certain pathways from happening.", "tokens": [51430, 467, 10672, 382, 257, 4001, 6608, 300, 24042, 8474, 1629, 22988, 490, 2737, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692606460216435, "compression_ratio": 1.6134453781512605, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682351030097853e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 104828, "start": 1048.28, "end": 1054.6, "text": " So it's making a choice, obviously not a conscious choice, but the universe is physically excluding futures.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 1455, 257, 3922, 11, 2745, 406, 257, 6648, 3922, 11, 457, 264, 6445, 307, 9762, 49999, 26071, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 104828, "start": 1054.8999999999999, "end": 1056.54, "text": " That is exactly what it is doing.", "tokens": [50696, 663, 307, 2293, 437, 309, 307, 884, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 104828, "start": 1056.84, "end": 1060.66, "text": " And this leads to a profound philosophical implication that Fliction highlights.", "tokens": [50793, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 257, 14382, 25066, 37814, 300, 3235, 4105, 14254, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 104828, "start": 1061.28, "end": 1062.34, "text": " Identity is history.", "tokens": [51015, 25905, 507, 307, 2503, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 104828, "start": 1062.7, "end": 1063.6399999999999, "text": " Identity is history.", "tokens": [51086, 25905, 507, 307, 2503, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 104828, "start": 1063.8, "end": 1064.42, "text": " Explain that one.", "tokens": [51141, 39574, 300, 472, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 104828, "start": 1064.5, "end": 1067.52, "text": " Let's imagine you have two physical systems that appear totally identical.", "tokens": [51176, 961, 311, 3811, 291, 362, 732, 4001, 3652, 300, 4204, 3879, 14800, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 104828, "start": 1067.86, "end": 1069.22, "text": " Say, two hotel rooms.", "tokens": [51344, 6463, 11, 732, 7622, 9396, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 104828, "start": 1069.52, "end": 1071.78, "text": " You walk into room A and you walk into room B.", "tokens": [51427, 509, 1792, 666, 1808, 316, 293, 291, 1792, 666, 1808, 363, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 104828, "start": 1071.86, "end": 1072.68, "text": " Okay, I'm with you.", "tokens": [51544, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466370122186069, "compression_ratio": 1.6679104477611941, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279319894011104e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 107268, "start": 1072.68, "end": 1079.48, "text": " They have the exact same temperature, the exact same air pressure, the exact same arrangement of furniture down to the atomic level of this exact instant.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 362, 264, 1900, 912, 4292, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 1988, 3321, 11, 264, 1900, 912, 17620, 295, 15671, 760, 281, 264, 22275, 1496, 295, 341, 1900, 9836, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12111469507217407, "compression_ratio": 1.7445887445887447, "no_speech_prob": 2.125341786243795e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 107268, "start": 1080.1000000000001, "end": 1083.52, "text": " Standard classical physics would say those two rooms exist in identical states.", "tokens": [50736, 21298, 13735, 10649, 576, 584, 729, 732, 9396, 2514, 294, 14800, 4368, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12111469507217407, "compression_ratio": 1.7445887445887447, "no_speech_prob": 2.125341786243795e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 107268, "start": 1083.8200000000002, "end": 1084.3400000000001, "text": " They are the same.", "tokens": [50922, 814, 366, 264, 912, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12111469507217407, "compression_ratio": 1.7445887445887447, "no_speech_prob": 2.125341786243795e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 107268, "start": 1084.5, "end": 1091.8400000000001, "text": " But Fliction argues they are fundamentally physically distinct if they arrived at that identical state through different refuse admissible histories.", "tokens": [50956, 583, 3235, 4105, 38218, 436, 366, 17879, 9762, 10644, 498, 436, 6678, 412, 300, 14800, 1785, 807, 819, 16791, 5910, 41073, 30631, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12111469507217407, "compression_ratio": 1.7445887445887447, "no_speech_prob": 2.125341786243795e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 109184, "start": 1091.84, "end": 1105.28, "text": " So if room A was carefully arranged by a maid over an hour and room B was just completely rebuilt from scratch after a fire 10 minutes ago, their instantaneous state right now might match perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 1808, 316, 390, 7500, 18721, 538, 257, 30410, 670, 364, 1773, 293, 1808, 363, 390, 445, 2584, 38532, 490, 8459, 934, 257, 2610, 1266, 2077, 2057, 11, 641, 45596, 1785, 558, 586, 1062, 2995, 6239, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12154343984659435, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519417328473954e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 109184, "start": 1105.52, "end": 1108.06, "text": " But you're saying the universe treats them as different.", "tokens": [51049, 583, 291, 434, 1566, 264, 6445, 19566, 552, 382, 819, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12154343984659435, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519417328473954e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 109184, "start": 1108.52, "end": 1117.32, "text": " Yes, because their history sensitive state space, what the math refers to as the path groupoid, retains the distinction of those lost trajectories.", "tokens": [51199, 1079, 11, 570, 641, 2503, 9477, 1785, 1901, 11, 437, 264, 5221, 14942, 281, 382, 264, 3100, 1594, 17079, 11, 1533, 2315, 264, 16844, 295, 729, 2731, 18257, 2083, 13, 51639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12154343984659435, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519417328473954e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 109184, "start": 1117.8799999999999, "end": 1120.5, "text": " Identity isn't just a snapshot of what you are right now.", "tokens": [51667, 25905, 507, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 30163, 295, 437, 291, 366, 558, 586, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12154343984659435, "compression_ratio": 1.6006944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 2.0519417328473954e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 112050, "start": 1120.5, "end": 1125.66, "text": " Identity is the sum total of the irreversible path of constraints you resolved to get here.", "tokens": [50365, 25905, 507, 307, 264, 2408, 3217, 295, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 3100, 295, 18491, 291, 20772, 281, 483, 510, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 112050, "start": 1125.8, "end": 1126.2, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50630, 3153, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 112050, "start": 1126.7, "end": 1130.42, "text": " The refuse operators that shaped room A are different from the ones that shaped room B.", "tokens": [50675, 440, 16791, 19077, 300, 13475, 1808, 316, 366, 819, 490, 264, 2306, 300, 13475, 1808, 363, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 112050, "start": 1130.66, "end": 1132.8, "text": " The mathematical space holds that history.", "tokens": [50873, 440, 18894, 1901, 9190, 300, 2503, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 112050, "start": 1132.94, "end": 1134.28, "text": " Okay, I love the poetry of that.", "tokens": [50987, 1033, 11, 286, 959, 264, 15155, 295, 300, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 112050, "start": 1134.38, "end": 1137.02, "text": " Identity is the irreversible path of constraints you resolved.", "tokens": [51059, 25905, 507, 307, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 3100, 295, 18491, 291, 20772, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 112050, "start": 1137.76, "end": 1138.92, "text": " But I have to push back here.", "tokens": [51228, 583, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 510, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 112050, "start": 1138.94, "end": 1139.32, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51287, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 112050, "start": 1139.46, "end": 1141.38, "text": " As a layman, I'm getting a little skeptical.", "tokens": [51313, 1018, 257, 2360, 1601, 11, 286, 478, 1242, 257, 707, 28601, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 112050, "start": 1141.72, "end": 1149.66, "text": " We are talking about all these hidden histories, these lost trajectories, these path groupoids that we can't physically see in the room.", "tokens": [51426, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 439, 613, 7633, 30631, 11, 613, 2731, 18257, 2083, 11, 613, 3100, 1594, 78, 3742, 300, 321, 393, 380, 9762, 536, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17035149527596427, "compression_ratio": 1.8445945945945945, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040682879874592e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 114966, "start": 1149.66, "end": 1152.0600000000002, "text": " But the math insists are there.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 5221, 50137, 366, 456, 13, 50485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12198912067177856, "compression_ratio": 1.5643564356435644, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594552137312753e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 114966, "start": 1152.68, "end": 1160.42, "text": " If our mathematical models hold on to history or data that we can never actually observe with our instruments, isn't that just a flaw in the math?", "tokens": [50516, 759, 527, 18894, 5245, 1797, 322, 281, 2503, 420, 1412, 300, 321, 393, 1128, 767, 11441, 365, 527, 12190, 11, 1943, 380, 300, 445, 257, 13717, 294, 264, 5221, 30, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12198912067177856, "compression_ratio": 1.5643564356435644, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594552137312753e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 114966, "start": 1160.78, "end": 1161.94, "text": " That's a very fair question.", "tokens": [50921, 663, 311, 257, 588, 3143, 1168, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12198912067177856, "compression_ratio": 1.5643564356435644, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594552137312753e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 114966, "start": 1162.18, "end": 1162.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50991, 1779, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12198912067177856, "compression_ratio": 1.5643564356435644, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594552137312753e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 114966, "start": 1162.5600000000002, "end": 1166.8000000000002, "text": " I mean, how do we know what's real and what's just a mathematical artifact that we should throw away?", "tokens": [51010, 286, 914, 11, 577, 360, 321, 458, 437, 311, 957, 293, 437, 311, 445, 257, 18894, 34806, 300, 321, 820, 3507, 1314, 30, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12198912067177856, "compression_ratio": 1.5643564356435644, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594552137312753e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 116680, "start": 1166.8, "end": 1173.36, "text": " You've just hit on the exact existential crisis that has paralyzed the field of quantum gravity for over 50 years.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 445, 2045, 322, 264, 1900, 37133, 5869, 300, 575, 41919, 264, 2519, 295, 13018, 12110, 337, 670, 2625, 924, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 116680, "start": 1173.68, "end": 1180.4199999999998, "text": " And it provides the perfect transition into the third major paper in our stack, Admissibility Interface Extended.", "tokens": [50709, 400, 309, 6417, 264, 2176, 6034, 666, 264, 2636, 2563, 3035, 294, 527, 8630, 11, 46292, 891, 2841, 5751, 2868, 9881, 3502, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 116680, "start": 1180.68, "end": 1181.1599999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51059, 1079, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 116680, "start": 1181.36, "end": 1186.86, "text": " This paper takes that exact skepticism you just voiced and tackles the infamous problem of ghosts.", "tokens": [51093, 639, 3035, 2516, 300, 1900, 19128, 26356, 291, 445, 42246, 293, 9426, 904, 264, 30769, 1154, 295, 21744, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 116680, "start": 1187.1599999999999, "end": 1187.6399999999999, "text": " Ghosts.", "tokens": [51383, 16323, 82, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 116680, "start": 1187.74, "end": 1188.34, "text": " Okay, yes.", "tokens": [51412, 1033, 11, 2086, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 116680, "start": 1188.44, "end": 1189.96, "text": " I've been waiting to unpack the ghosts.", "tokens": [51447, 286, 600, 668, 3806, 281, 26699, 264, 21744, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 116680, "start": 1190.28, "end": 1191.6, "text": " Let's set the stage for the listener.", "tokens": [51539, 961, 311, 992, 264, 3233, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12089290093938145, "compression_ratio": 1.5431654676258992, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906209063584978e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 119160, "start": 1191.6, "end": 1194.48, "text": " The holy grail of modern physics is quantum gravity.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10622, 1295, 388, 295, 4363, 10649, 307, 13018, 12110, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689142623505035, "compression_ratio": 1.5858585858585859, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722194817406997e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 119160, "start": 1194.8999999999999, "end": 1202.52, "text": " We have Einstein's equations of general relativity, which brilliantly describe the macro world, you know, planets, gravity, galaxies.", "tokens": [50530, 492, 362, 23486, 311, 11787, 295, 2674, 45675, 11, 597, 8695, 42580, 6786, 264, 18887, 1002, 11, 291, 458, 11, 15126, 11, 12110, 11, 28755, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689142623505035, "compression_ratio": 1.5858585858585859, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722194817406997e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 119160, "start": 1202.54, "end": 1203.5, "text": " Like it's a large scale.", "tokens": [50912, 1743, 309, 311, 257, 2416, 4373, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689142623505035, "compression_ratio": 1.5858585858585859, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722194817406997e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 119160, "start": 1203.8, "end": 1208.1799999999998, "text": " And we have quantum mechanics, which brilliantly describes the micro world.", "tokens": [50975, 400, 321, 362, 13018, 12939, 11, 597, 8695, 42580, 15626, 264, 4532, 1002, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689142623505035, "compression_ratio": 1.5858585858585859, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722194817406997e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 119160, "start": 1208.4599999999998, "end": 1210.3, "text": " Atoms, electrons, photons.", "tokens": [51208, 1711, 4785, 11, 14265, 11, 40209, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1689142623505035, "compression_ratio": 1.5858585858585859, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722194817406997e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 121030, "start": 1210.3, "end": 1216.98, "text": " But when physicists try to smash them together to understand something like the center of a black hole, the math breaks.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 48716, 853, 281, 17960, 552, 1214, 281, 1223, 746, 411, 264, 3056, 295, 257, 2211, 5458, 11, 264, 5221, 9857, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 121030, "start": 1217.2, "end": 1217.8999999999999, "text": " It doesn't just break.", "tokens": [50710, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 1821, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 121030, "start": 1218.02, "end": 1219.04, "text": " It completely shatters.", "tokens": [50751, 467, 2584, 402, 37690, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 121030, "start": 1219.7, "end": 1225.22, "text": " When you try to quantize general relativity using standard techniques, the equations spit out infinities.", "tokens": [50835, 1133, 291, 853, 281, 4426, 1125, 2674, 45675, 1228, 3832, 7512, 11, 264, 11787, 22127, 484, 7193, 1088, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 121030, "start": 1225.74, "end": 1228.44, "text": " It produces infinite probabilities, infinite energies.", "tokens": [51137, 467, 14725, 13785, 33783, 11, 13785, 25737, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 121030, "start": 1229.04, "end": 1232.36, "text": " In physics terminology, the theory is not renormalizable.", "tokens": [51302, 682, 10649, 27575, 11, 264, 5261, 307, 406, 8124, 24440, 22395, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 121030, "start": 1232.44, "end": 1234.0, "text": " It can't be fixed by smoothing it out.", "tokens": [51472, 467, 393, 380, 312, 6806, 538, 899, 6259, 571, 309, 484, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 121030, "start": 1234.06, "end": 1234.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51553, 7587, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 121030, "start": 1234.6, "end": 1236.94, "text": " It cannot be fixed by standard mathematical smoothing.", "tokens": [51580, 467, 2644, 312, 6806, 538, 3832, 18894, 899, 6259, 571, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1300250069569733, "compression_ratio": 1.7402135231316727, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995407480496547e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 123694, "start": 1236.94, "end": 1242.7, "text": " But in the 1970s, a physicist named K.S. Stel found a mathematical hack right.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 264, 14577, 82, 11, 257, 42466, 4926, 591, 13, 50, 13, 745, 338, 1352, 257, 18894, 10339, 558, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 123694, "start": 1243.3400000000001, "end": 1251.94, "text": " He showed that if you add extra, highly complex terms to Einstein's equations, specifically quadratic curvature terms, the infinities disappear.", "tokens": [50685, 634, 4712, 300, 498, 291, 909, 2857, 11, 5405, 3997, 2115, 281, 23486, 311, 11787, 11, 4682, 37262, 37638, 2115, 11, 264, 7193, 1088, 11596, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 123694, "start": 1252.5, "end": 1253.54, "text": " The math suddenly works.", "tokens": [51143, 440, 5221, 5800, 1985, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 123694, "start": 1253.6200000000001, "end": 1255.0800000000002, "text": " The theory becomes renormalizable.", "tokens": [51199, 440, 5261, 3643, 8124, 24440, 22395, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 123694, "start": 1255.0800000000002, "end": 1257.76, "text": " But there's a massive, seemingly fatal catch.", "tokens": [51272, 583, 456, 311, 257, 5994, 11, 18709, 24069, 3745, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 123694, "start": 1258.3400000000001, "end": 1260.72, "text": " Adding those quadratic terms cures the infinities, sure.", "tokens": [51435, 31204, 729, 37262, 2115, 269, 1303, 264, 7193, 1088, 11, 988, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 123694, "start": 1260.98, "end": 1263.7, "text": " But it introduces a new particle into the fundamental equations.", "tokens": [51567, 583, 309, 31472, 257, 777, 12359, 666, 264, 8088, 11787, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 123694, "start": 1264.04, "end": 1265.66, "text": " A massive spin-2 graviton.", "tokens": [51720, 316, 5994, 6060, 12, 17, 26048, 266, 13, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1531619863995051, "compression_ratio": 1.5827814569536425, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368506163862539e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 126566, "start": 1265.66, "end": 1267.94, "text": " And this particle has negative kinetic energy.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 12359, 575, 3671, 27135, 2281, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 126566, "start": 1268.0800000000002, "end": 1269.66, "text": " This is what physicists call a ghost.", "tokens": [50486, 639, 307, 437, 48716, 818, 257, 8359, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 126566, "start": 1270.3400000000001, "end": 1276.1000000000001, "text": " And a particle with negative kinetic energy essentially means a particle with a negative probability of existing.", "tokens": [50599, 400, 257, 12359, 365, 3671, 27135, 2281, 4476, 1355, 257, 12359, 365, 257, 3671, 8482, 295, 6741, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 126566, "start": 1276.98, "end": 1278.26, "text": " Which just breaks my brain.", "tokens": [50931, 3013, 445, 9857, 452, 3567, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 126566, "start": 1278.3200000000002, "end": 1280.22, "text": " I'm stuck on this negative probability thing.", "tokens": [50998, 286, 478, 5541, 322, 341, 3671, 8482, 551, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 126566, "start": 1280.28, "end": 1280.66, "text": " It's very counterintuitive.", "tokens": [51096, 467, 311, 588, 5682, 686, 48314, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 126566, "start": 1281.4, "end": 1288.6200000000001, "text": " If a weatherman goes on TV and says, tomorrow there is a minus 20% chance of rain, he is going to be fired.", "tokens": [51152, 759, 257, 5503, 1601, 1709, 322, 3558, 293, 1619, 11, 4153, 456, 307, 257, 3175, 945, 4, 2931, 295, 4830, 11, 415, 307, 516, 281, 312, 11777, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 126566, "start": 1289.0400000000002, "end": 1290.38, "text": " It's a nonsensical statement.", "tokens": [51534, 467, 311, 257, 297, 892, 694, 804, 5629, 13, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 126566, "start": 1290.5, "end": 1294.0600000000002, "text": " You can have a 0% chance, but you can't have less than 0.", "tokens": [51607, 509, 393, 362, 257, 1958, 4, 2931, 11, 457, 291, 393, 380, 362, 1570, 813, 1958, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11916196529681866, "compression_ratio": 1.7342657342657342, "no_speech_prob": 2.0044066233182445e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 129406, "start": 1294.06, "end": 1300.6799999999998, "text": " So how can physicists tolerate math that outputs impossible numbers in the first place?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 577, 393, 48716, 25773, 5221, 300, 23930, 6243, 3547, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 30, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20944742722944779, "compression_ratio": 1.4416243654822336, "no_speech_prob": 1.585888538546687e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 129406, "start": 1300.94, "end": 1302.46, "text": " Well, historically they haven't.", "tokens": [50709, 1042, 11, 16180, 436, 2378, 380, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20944742722944779, "compression_ratio": 1.4416243654822336, "no_speech_prob": 1.585888538546687e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 129406, "start": 1302.6, "end": 1302.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50792, 1779, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20944742722944779, "compression_ratio": 1.4416243654822336, "no_speech_prob": 1.585888538546687e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 129406, "start": 1302.94, "end": 1310.06, "text": " The standard reaction for 50 years has been, negative probability is impossible, therefore, Stel's quadratic gravity is garbage.", "tokens": [50809, 440, 3832, 5480, 337, 2625, 924, 575, 668, 11, 3671, 8482, 307, 6243, 11, 4412, 11, 745, 338, 311, 37262, 12110, 307, 14150, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20944742722944779, "compression_ratio": 1.4416243654822336, "no_speech_prob": 1.585888538546687e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 129406, "start": 1310.56, "end": 1311.72, "text": " Throw the whole theory out.", "tokens": [51190, 22228, 264, 1379, 5261, 484, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20944742722944779, "compression_ratio": 1.4416243654822336, "no_speech_prob": 1.585888538546687e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 131172, "start": 1311.72, "end": 1312.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16347391264779226, "compression_ratio": 1.3505747126436782, "no_speech_prob": 2.1409692595175667e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 131172, "start": 1312.5, "end": 1314.78, "text": " The physics community overwhelmingly abandoned it.", "tokens": [50404, 440, 10649, 1768, 42926, 13732, 309, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16347391264779226, "compression_ratio": 1.3505747126436782, "no_speech_prob": 2.1409692595175667e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 131172, "start": 1315.14, "end": 1326.06, "text": " But Flickshinen, building on some highly controversial recent work by physicists Neil Turok and Sam Bateman, argues that this rejection is based on a massive, unexamined bias.", "tokens": [50536, 583, 3235, 618, 2716, 5636, 11, 2390, 322, 512, 5405, 17323, 5162, 589, 538, 48716, 18615, 314, 7052, 74, 293, 4832, 10066, 15023, 11, 38218, 300, 341, 26044, 307, 2361, 322, 257, 5994, 11, 11572, 335, 2001, 12577, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16347391264779226, "compression_ratio": 1.3505747126436782, "no_speech_prob": 2.1409692595175667e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 132606, "start": 1326.06, "end": 1329.58, "text": " A philosophical prejudice masquerading as a physical law.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 25066, 34260, 2300, 8035, 8166, 382, 257, 4001, 2101, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 132606, "start": 1329.8, "end": 1330.46, "text": " Oh, I guess.", "tokens": [50552, 876, 11, 286, 2041, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 132606, "start": 1330.58, "end": 1331.8999999999999, "text": " They call it the Hilbert assumption.", "tokens": [50591, 814, 818, 309, 264, 19914, 4290, 15302, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 132606, "start": 1332.24, "end": 1333.4199999999998, "text": " What is the Hilbert assumption?", "tokens": [50674, 708, 307, 264, 19914, 4290, 15302, 30, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 132606, "start": 1333.8, "end": 1342.8999999999999, "text": " It is the deeply ingrained assumption that the internal mathematical state space of a physical theory must be identical to the observable physical world.", "tokens": [50752, 467, 307, 264, 8760, 3957, 31774, 15302, 300, 264, 6920, 18894, 1785, 1901, 295, 257, 4001, 5261, 1633, 312, 14800, 281, 264, 9951, 712, 4001, 1002, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 132606, "start": 1343.6799999999998, "end": 1351.1, "text": " The assumption demands that if something exists in the math, if it's in the equations, it must be capable of showing up on our measuring devices.", "tokens": [51246, 440, 15302, 15107, 300, 498, 746, 8198, 294, 264, 5221, 11, 498, 309, 311, 294, 264, 11787, 11, 309, 1633, 312, 8189, 295, 4099, 493, 322, 527, 13389, 5759, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14756405587289848, "compression_ratio": 1.756, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042215941746487e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 135110, "start": 1351.1, "end": 1355.24, "text": " So if the math has a ghost, the universe must have a ghost.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 264, 5221, 575, 257, 8359, 11, 264, 6445, 1633, 362, 257, 8359, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 135110, "start": 1355.3999999999999, "end": 1355.76, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50580, 7587, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 135110, "start": 1355.98, "end": 1356.58, "text": " But hold on.", "tokens": [50609, 583, 1797, 322, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 135110, "start": 1357.04, "end": 1368.3, "text": " If a theory predicts a particle with negative probability, or worse, if it predicts a universe with unbounded negative energy, which I think the text referred to as the Ostrogradsky instability.", "tokens": [50662, 759, 257, 5261, 6069, 82, 257, 12359, 365, 3671, 8482, 11, 420, 5324, 11, 498, 309, 6069, 82, 257, 6445, 365, 517, 18767, 292, 3671, 2281, 11, 597, 286, 519, 264, 2487, 10839, 281, 382, 264, 34140, 6675, 81, 5834, 4133, 34379, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 135110, "start": 1368.5, "end": 1370.1799999999998, "text": " Yes, the Ostrogradsky instability.", "tokens": [51235, 1079, 11, 264, 34140, 6675, 81, 5834, 4133, 34379, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 135110, "start": 1370.3999999999999, "end": 1372.36, "text": " Doesn't that mean the universe literally explodes?", "tokens": [51330, 12955, 380, 300, 914, 264, 6445, 3736, 42610, 30, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13113633381951714, "compression_ratio": 1.6759259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.17628801264802e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 137236, "start": 1372.36, "end": 1381.6399999999999, "text": " From what I read, if a system can drop into infinite negative energy, it will simultaneously produce an infinite amount of positive energy particles to balance it out.", "tokens": [50365, 3358, 437, 286, 1401, 11, 498, 257, 1185, 393, 3270, 666, 13785, 3671, 2281, 11, 309, 486, 16561, 5258, 364, 13785, 2372, 295, 3353, 2281, 10007, 281, 4772, 309, 484, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 137236, "start": 1382.32, "end": 1383.86, "text": " The universe should just detonate.", "tokens": [50863, 440, 6445, 820, 445, 39920, 473, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 137236, "start": 1384.26, "end": 1388.74, "text": " If the math says that happens, how can Fliction just say, ignore the math?", "tokens": [50960, 759, 264, 5221, 1619, 300, 2314, 11, 577, 393, 3235, 4105, 445, 584, 11, 11200, 264, 5221, 30, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 137236, "start": 1389.2199999999998, "end": 1390.86, "text": " Fliction isn't saying to ignore the math.", "tokens": [51208, 3235, 4105, 1943, 380, 1566, 281, 11200, 264, 5221, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 137236, "start": 1391.28, "end": 1394.74, "text": " Fliction is saying we are misinterpreting what the math is actually describing.", "tokens": [51311, 3235, 4105, 307, 1566, 321, 366, 3346, 5106, 3712, 783, 437, 264, 5221, 307, 767, 16141, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 137236, "start": 1394.9399999999998, "end": 1401.02, "text": " And to understand this, we need to look at a vital concept in the paper called the projection pathology separation theorem.", "tokens": [51494, 400, 281, 1223, 341, 11, 321, 643, 281, 574, 412, 257, 11707, 3410, 294, 264, 3035, 1219, 264, 22743, 3100, 1793, 14634, 20904, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12276566718235489, "compression_ratio": 1.7375415282392026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5252625551465115e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 140102, "start": 1401.02, "end": 1403.74, "text": " This requires a radical perspective shift.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 7029, 257, 12001, 4585, 5513, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 140102, "start": 1404.48, "end": 1411.3799999999999, "text": " Fliction asks us to rigorously distinguish between a coordinate pathology and an observable pathology.", "tokens": [50538, 3235, 4105, 8962, 505, 281, 42191, 5098, 20206, 1296, 257, 15670, 3100, 1793, 293, 364, 9951, 712, 3100, 1793, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 140102, "start": 1411.46, "end": 1414.36, "text": " Okay, let's bring back the medical x-ray metaphor from the beginning of the show.", "tokens": [50887, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1565, 646, 264, 4625, 2031, 12, 3458, 19157, 490, 264, 2863, 295, 264, 855, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 140102, "start": 1414.44, "end": 1414.72, "text": " Perfect.", "tokens": [51036, 10246, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 140102, "start": 1415.3, "end": 1417.08, "text": " Imagine the doctor is looking at your x-ray.", "tokens": [51079, 11739, 264, 4631, 307, 1237, 412, 428, 2031, 12, 3458, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 140102, "start": 1417.66, "end": 1421.28, "text": " A coordinate pathology is a smudge on the x-ray film itself.", "tokens": [51197, 316, 15670, 3100, 1793, 307, 257, 899, 16032, 322, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 2007, 2564, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 140102, "start": 1422.04, "end": 1424.74, "text": " It is a defect in the representational machinery.", "tokens": [51416, 467, 307, 257, 16445, 294, 264, 2906, 1478, 27302, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 140102, "start": 1425.3799999999999, "end": 1428.94, "text": " Maybe some chemical developer spilled or the lens was scratched.", "tokens": [51583, 2704, 512, 7313, 10754, 37833, 420, 264, 6765, 390, 40513, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12929144240262216, "compression_ratio": 1.6148409893992932, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760842709740876e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 142894, "start": 1428.94, "end": 1433.98, "text": " An observable pathology, on the other hand, is a tumor in the actual patient's body.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 9951, 712, 3100, 1793, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 307, 257, 22512, 294, 264, 3539, 4537, 311, 1772, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 142894, "start": 1434.48, "end": 1440.28, "text": " Okay, so the Hilbert assumption is the doctor assuming that every single smudge on the film is a deadly tumor in the patient.", "tokens": [50642, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 19914, 4290, 15302, 307, 264, 4631, 11926, 300, 633, 2167, 899, 16032, 322, 264, 2007, 307, 257, 18232, 22512, 294, 264, 4537, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 142894, "start": 1440.5, "end": 1440.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50943, 7587, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 142894, "start": 1441.46, "end": 1443.94, "text": " The Hilbert assumption demands that the map is the territory.", "tokens": [50991, 440, 19914, 4290, 15302, 15107, 300, 264, 4471, 307, 264, 11360, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 142894, "start": 1444.9, "end": 1451.0800000000002, "text": " But the separation theorem proves mathematically that a coordinate pathology in the underlying manifold,", "tokens": [51163, 583, 264, 14634, 20904, 25019, 44003, 300, 257, 15670, 3100, 1793, 294, 264, 14217, 47138, 11, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 142894, "start": 1451.5, "end": 1457.14, "text": " the mathematical space, does not necessarily imply an observable pathology in the real physical world.", "tokens": [51493, 264, 18894, 1901, 11, 775, 406, 4725, 33616, 364, 9951, 712, 3100, 1793, 294, 264, 957, 4001, 1002, 13, 51775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10881721221648895, "compression_ratio": 1.8452830188679246, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147414130974648e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 145714, "start": 1457.14, "end": 1459.5800000000002, "text": " The smudge on the film doesn't mean you have cancer.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 899, 16032, 322, 264, 2007, 1177, 380, 914, 291, 362, 5592, 13, 50487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 145714, "start": 1459.8000000000002, "end": 1459.96, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50498, 1079, 13, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 145714, "start": 1460.0400000000002, "end": 1461.92, "text": " Because there's a filter, a projection.", "tokens": [50510, 1436, 456, 311, 257, 6608, 11, 257, 22743, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 145714, "start": 1462.5400000000002, "end": 1462.8200000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50635, 1079, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 145714, "start": 1463.3600000000001, "end": 1468.72, "text": " To prove this, the text explores a famous mathematical model known as the Pace-Ulinbeck oscillator.", "tokens": [50676, 1407, 7081, 341, 11, 264, 2487, 45473, 257, 4618, 18894, 2316, 2570, 382, 264, 430, 617, 12, 52, 5045, 650, 547, 43859, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 145714, "start": 1469.3600000000001, "end": 1472.44, "text": " This is a mathematical toy model, a system of equations,", "tokens": [50976, 639, 307, 257, 18894, 12058, 2316, 11, 257, 1185, 295, 11787, 11, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 145714, "start": 1472.8400000000001, "end": 1477.98, "text": " where the Hamiltonian, the calculation of the total energy of the system, is completely unbounded.", "tokens": [51150, 689, 264, 18484, 952, 11, 264, 17108, 295, 264, 3217, 2281, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 307, 2584, 517, 18767, 292, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 145714, "start": 1478.3400000000001, "end": 1480.1000000000001, "text": " It runs away to negative infinity.", "tokens": [51425, 467, 6676, 1314, 281, 3671, 13202, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 145714, "start": 1480.46, "end": 1483.5400000000002, "text": " It's the exact definition of a total Ostrogrodsky instability.", "tokens": [51531, 467, 311, 264, 1900, 7123, 295, 257, 3217, 34140, 6675, 11452, 25810, 34379, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19285896735462715, "compression_ratio": 1.6521739130434783, "no_speech_prob": 1.610998552441234e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 148354, "start": 1483.54, "end": 1487.06, "text": " Exactly. The math screams that the system will explode.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 5221, 22832, 300, 264, 1185, 486, 21411, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 148354, "start": 1487.26, "end": 1487.98, "text": " But it doesn't.", "tokens": [50551, 583, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 148354, "start": 1488.08, "end": 1488.7, "text": " It doesn't.", "tokens": [50592, 467, 1177, 380, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 148354, "start": 1488.8, "end": 1496.28, "text": " If you stop looking at the raw energy calculations and instead trace the actual physically admissible trajectories of the system,", "tokens": [50628, 759, 291, 1590, 1237, 412, 264, 8936, 2281, 20448, 293, 2602, 13508, 264, 3539, 9762, 5910, 41073, 18257, 2083, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 148354, "start": 1496.7, "end": 1498.3999999999999, "text": " the paths it is actually allowed to take,", "tokens": [51023, 264, 14518, 309, 307, 767, 4350, 281, 747, 11, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 148354, "start": 1498.8, "end": 1503.3999999999999, "text": " the entire system violently reduces down to two coupled harmonic oscillators.", "tokens": [51128, 264, 2302, 1185, 46728, 18081, 760, 281, 732, 29482, 32270, 18225, 3391, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 148354, "start": 1503.52, "end": 1505.3, "text": " Wait, what does that mean in plain English?", "tokens": [51364, 3802, 11, 437, 775, 300, 914, 294, 11121, 3669, 30, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 148354, "start": 1505.5, "end": 1510.3799999999999, "text": " It means the actual physical trajectory is a bounded, perfectly stable, endlessly repeating orbit.", "tokens": [51463, 467, 1355, 264, 3539, 4001, 21512, 307, 257, 37498, 11, 6239, 8351, 11, 44920, 18617, 13991, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15472776239568536, "compression_ratio": 1.676056338028169, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881465843276988e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 151038, "start": 1510.38, "end": 1514.24, "text": " The mathematical state space contained an exploding direction,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18894, 1785, 1901, 16212, 364, 35175, 3513, 11, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 151038, "start": 1514.5600000000002, "end": 1517.46, "text": " but the physical system never, ever travels down it.", "tokens": [50574, 457, 264, 4001, 1185, 1128, 11, 1562, 19863, 760, 309, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 151038, "start": 1517.5600000000002, "end": 1520.96, "text": " So the ghost particle, the spin-2 graviton with negative energy,", "tokens": [50724, 407, 264, 8359, 12359, 11, 264, 6060, 12, 17, 26048, 266, 365, 3671, 2281, 11, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 151038, "start": 1521.5800000000002, "end": 1523.7, "text": " it exists in the deep mathematical substrate,", "tokens": [50925, 309, 8198, 294, 264, 2452, 18894, 27585, 11, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 151038, "start": 1524.0800000000002, "end": 1527.3600000000001, "text": " but the universe physically refuses to let it reach our detectors.", "tokens": [51050, 457, 264, 6445, 9762, 33222, 281, 718, 309, 2524, 527, 46866, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 151038, "start": 1527.92, "end": 1528.44, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51242, 48746, 736, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 151038, "start": 1528.98, "end": 1531.64, "text": " And this is where Turok and Bateman's work comes in.", "tokens": [51295, 400, 341, 307, 689, 314, 7052, 74, 293, 10066, 15023, 311, 589, 1487, 294, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 151038, "start": 1532.3600000000001, "end": 1536.74, "text": " They use a specific, highly exotic mathematical structure called a Kreen space.", "tokens": [51464, 814, 764, 257, 2685, 11, 5405, 27063, 18894, 3877, 1219, 257, 591, 1492, 1901, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20564626297860775, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 2.7289281945286348e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 153674, "start": 1536.74, "end": 1542.36, "text": " Unlike a standard Hilbert space, which only allows positive distances and positive probabilities,", "tokens": [50365, 17657, 257, 3832, 19914, 4290, 1901, 11, 597, 787, 4045, 3353, 22182, 293, 3353, 33783, 11, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 153674, "start": 1542.9, "end": 1546.44, "text": " a Kreen space allows for an indefinite inner product.", "tokens": [50673, 257, 591, 1492, 1901, 4045, 337, 364, 24162, 5194, 642, 7284, 1674, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 153674, "start": 1546.92, "end": 1548.3, "text": " It allows for the negative numbers.", "tokens": [50874, 467, 4045, 337, 264, 3671, 3547, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 153674, "start": 1548.6, "end": 1548.74, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50958, 1079, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 153674, "start": 1549.06, "end": 1550.42, "text": " It allows for negative norms.", "tokens": [50981, 467, 4045, 337, 3671, 24357, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 153674, "start": 1550.72, "end": 1553.02, "text": " It's a mathematical space that can handle the ghosts.", "tokens": [51064, 467, 311, 257, 18894, 1901, 300, 393, 4813, 264, 21744, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 153674, "start": 1553.78, "end": 1558.74, "text": " Turok and Bateman show that these ghosts are actually just hidden admissibility directions.", "tokens": [51217, 314, 7052, 74, 293, 10066, 15023, 855, 300, 613, 21744, 366, 767, 445, 7633, 5910, 891, 2841, 11095, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 153674, "start": 1559.42, "end": 1563.46, "text": " They're essentially rotational data, hidden phases in the quantum wave function.", "tokens": [51499, 814, 434, 4476, 45420, 1412, 11, 7633, 18764, 294, 264, 13018, 5772, 2445, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 153674, "start": 1564.1, "end": 1565.48, "text": " And here's the genius part.", "tokens": [51733, 400, 510, 311, 264, 14017, 644, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1581627721371858, "compression_ratio": 1.7158273381294964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830474510066585e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 156548, "start": 1565.48, "end": 1571.52, "text": " They perfectly cancel themselves out when you calculate the final observable probability.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 6239, 10373, 2969, 484, 562, 291, 8873, 264, 2572, 9951, 712, 8482, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 156548, "start": 1571.72, "end": 1573.42, "text": " They cancel themselves out? How?", "tokens": [50677, 814, 10373, 2969, 484, 30, 1012, 30, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 156548, "start": 1573.94, "end": 1577.44, "text": " Well, Fliction points out that the famous Born rule in quantum mechanics...", "tokens": [50788, 1042, 11, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 264, 4618, 29808, 4978, 294, 13018, 12939, 485, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 156548, "start": 1577.44, "end": 1580.58, "text": " This is the rule where you take the quantum amplitude and square it", "tokens": [50963, 639, 307, 264, 4978, 689, 291, 747, 264, 13018, 27433, 293, 3732, 309, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 156548, "start": 1580.58, "end": 1582.98, "text": " to get the actual probability of an event happening.", "tokens": [51120, 281, 483, 264, 3539, 8482, 295, 364, 2280, 2737, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 156548, "start": 1583.08, "end": 1583.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51245, 1079, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 156548, "start": 1583.76, "end": 1586.84, "text": " Fliction argues that the Born rule is not just a mathematical trick.", "tokens": [51279, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 264, 29808, 4978, 307, 406, 445, 257, 18894, 4282, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 156548, "start": 1586.94, "end": 1588.98, "text": " It is precisely a coarse-graining projection.", "tokens": [51438, 467, 307, 13402, 257, 39312, 12, 20735, 1760, 22743, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 156548, "start": 1589.48, "end": 1590.72, "text": " It is the universe's filter.", "tokens": [51565, 467, 307, 264, 6445, 311, 6608, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 156548, "start": 1591.04, "end": 1594.96, "text": " When you square the amplitude, you literally square away the negative signs.", "tokens": [51643, 1133, 291, 3732, 264, 27433, 11, 291, 3736, 3732, 1314, 264, 3671, 7880, 13, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1491195261478424, "compression_ratio": 1.7637540453074434, "no_speech_prob": 2.01225386180226e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 159496, "start": 1594.96, "end": 1598.16, "text": " Oh! Because a negative times a negative is a positive.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 0, 1436, 257, 3671, 1413, 257, 3671, 307, 257, 3353, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15555978465724635, "compression_ratio": 1.5922330097087378, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907991491956544e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 159496, "start": 1598.28, "end": 1602.92, "text": " Exactly. You square away the hidden rotational data, you discard the ghosts before they can", "tokens": [50531, 7587, 13, 509, 3732, 1314, 264, 7633, 45420, 1412, 11, 291, 31597, 264, 21744, 949, 436, 393, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15555978465724635, "compression_ratio": 1.5922330097087378, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907991491956544e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 159496, "start": 1602.92, "end": 1605.56, "text": " ever cross the threshold into our observable reality.", "tokens": [50763, 1562, 3278, 264, 14678, 666, 527, 9951, 712, 4103, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15555978465724635, "compression_ratio": 1.5922330097087378, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907991491956544e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 159496, "start": 1606.2, "end": 1610.44, "text": " The positive probability that we measure is what survives the projection.", "tokens": [50927, 440, 3353, 8482, 300, 321, 3481, 307, 437, 46231, 264, 22743, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15555978465724635, "compression_ratio": 1.5922330097087378, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907991491956544e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 159496, "start": 1610.96, "end": 1613.8, "text": " The ghost is what the universe structurally discards.", "tokens": [51165, 440, 8359, 307, 437, 264, 6445, 6594, 6512, 2983, 2287, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15555978465724635, "compression_ratio": 1.5922330097087378, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907991491956544e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 161380, "start": 1613.8, "end": 1615.8, "text": " Okay, my mind is completely blown.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 452, 1575, 307, 2584, 16479, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15351893296882288, "compression_ratio": 1.4467005076142132, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915004774116892e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 161380, "start": 1616.52, "end": 1622.06, "text": " We have been throwing away the potential cure for quantum gravity, Stell's quadratic gravity,", "tokens": [50501, 492, 362, 668, 10238, 1314, 264, 3995, 13698, 337, 13018, 12110, 11, 37364, 311, 37262, 12110, 11, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15351893296882288, "compression_ratio": 1.4467005076142132, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915004774116892e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 161380, "start": 1622.26, "end": 1628.08, "text": " for 50 years because we were terrified of a mathematical ghost that the universe's own geometry", "tokens": [50788, 337, 2625, 924, 570, 321, 645, 23051, 295, 257, 18894, 8359, 300, 264, 6445, 311, 1065, 18426, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15351893296882288, "compression_ratio": 1.4467005076142132, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915004774116892e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 161380, "start": 1628.08, "end": 1629.86, "text": " automatically filters out for us.", "tokens": [51079, 6772, 15995, 484, 337, 505, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15351893296882288, "compression_ratio": 1.4467005076142132, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915004774116892e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 161380, "start": 1629.94, "end": 1631.1, "text": " That is the argument, yes.", "tokens": [51172, 663, 307, 264, 6770, 11, 2086, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15351893296882288, "compression_ratio": 1.4467005076142132, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915004774116892e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 163110, "start": 1631.1, "end": 1634.6999999999998, "text": " But wait, if we change the foundational rules of quantum gravity,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 498, 321, 1319, 264, 32195, 4474, 295, 13018, 12110, 11, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 163110, "start": 1635.5, "end": 1640.4599999999998, "text": " if we accept that we don't need a perfectly positive, definite mathematical state space,", "tokens": [50585, 498, 321, 3241, 300, 321, 500, 380, 643, 257, 6239, 3353, 11, 25131, 18894, 1785, 1901, 11, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 163110, "start": 1640.7199999999998, "end": 1643.08, "text": " only a positive, definite observable projection,", "tokens": [50846, 787, 257, 3353, 11, 25131, 9951, 712, 22743, 11, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 163110, "start": 1643.5, "end": 1646.24, "text": " that totally changes our assumptions about string theory, doesn't it?", "tokens": [50985, 300, 3879, 2962, 527, 17695, 466, 6798, 5261, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 163110, "start": 1646.3, "end": 1650.2199999999998, "text": " It doesn't just change our assumptions, it potentially renders string theory obsolete.", "tokens": [51125, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 1319, 527, 17695, 11, 309, 7263, 6125, 433, 6798, 5261, 46333, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 163110, "start": 1650.76, "end": 1653.7199999999998, "text": " This is the focus of the fourth section of our deep dive,", "tokens": [51348, 639, 307, 264, 1879, 295, 264, 6409, 3541, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 11, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 163110, "start": 1654.26, "end": 1656.52, "text": " the architecture of the early universe.", "tokens": [51523, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 2440, 6445, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17778932131253755, "compression_ratio": 1.7751937984496124, "no_speech_prob": 1.6109995282231893e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 165652, "start": 1656.52, "end": 1659.04, "text": " Because, if I understand the history right,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 11, 498, 286, 1223, 264, 2503, 558, 11, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 165652, "start": 1659.48, "end": 1663.76, "text": " string theory was essentially invented to solve this exact ghost problem.", "tokens": [50513, 6798, 5261, 390, 4476, 14479, 281, 5039, 341, 1900, 8359, 1154, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 165652, "start": 1664.3, "end": 1668.28, "text": " Physicists realize that if you treat particles as tiny vibrating strings", "tokens": [50754, 15542, 299, 1751, 4325, 300, 498, 291, 2387, 10007, 382, 5870, 47748, 13985, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 165652, "start": 1668.28, "end": 1670.2, "text": " instead of zero-dimensional points,", "tokens": [50953, 2602, 295, 4018, 12, 18759, 2793, 11, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 165652, "start": 1670.4, "end": 1672.08, "text": " and if you give the universe ten dimensions,", "tokens": [51059, 293, 498, 291, 976, 264, 6445, 2064, 12819, 11, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 165652, "start": 1672.7, "end": 1675.26, "text": " the math miraculously smooths out.", "tokens": [51174, 264, 5221, 30686, 25038, 5508, 82, 484, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 165652, "start": 1675.4, "end": 1676.9, "text": " Yes, the anomalies disappear,", "tokens": [51309, 1079, 11, 264, 24769, 48872, 11596, 11, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 165652, "start": 1677.2, "end": 1679.74, "text": " and all the probabilities stay strictly positive.", "tokens": [51399, 293, 439, 264, 33783, 1754, 20792, 3353, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 165652, "start": 1679.92, "end": 1682.3799999999999, "text": " String theory was a life raft to escape the ghosts.", "tokens": [51535, 745, 2937, 5261, 390, 257, 993, 43863, 281, 7615, 264, 21744, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 165652, "start": 1683.1399999999999, "end": 1685.7, "text": " But Fliction's argument, relying on this new paradigm,", "tokens": [51696, 583, 3235, 4105, 311, 6770, 11, 24140, 322, 341, 777, 24709, 11, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18222627719911208, "compression_ratio": 1.6543624161073827, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552892311364696e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 168570, "start": 1685.7, "end": 1688.5800000000002, "text": " is that the life raft was totally unnecessary.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 300, 264, 993, 43863, 390, 3879, 19350, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 168570, "start": 1689.5800000000002, "end": 1694.06, "text": " If we don't need the probabilities to stay strictly positive in the hidden mathematical substrate,", "tokens": [50559, 759, 321, 500, 380, 643, 264, 33783, 281, 1754, 20792, 3353, 294, 264, 7633, 18894, 27585, 11, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 168570, "start": 1694.66, "end": 1696.94, "text": " if Kreen's space handles the negative norms,", "tokens": [50813, 498, 591, 1492, 311, 1901, 18722, 264, 3671, 24357, 11, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 168570, "start": 1697.16, "end": 1698.56, "text": " and the Born rule filters them out,", "tokens": [50938, 293, 264, 29808, 4978, 15995, 552, 484, 11, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 168570, "start": 1699.04, "end": 1701.5, "text": " then we don't need to invent ten dimensions to fix the math.", "tokens": [51032, 550, 321, 500, 380, 643, 281, 7962, 2064, 12819, 281, 3191, 264, 5221, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 168570, "start": 1701.6200000000001, "end": 1702.38, "text": " We don't need strings.", "tokens": [51161, 492, 500, 380, 643, 13985, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 168570, "start": 1702.6000000000001, "end": 1706.02, "text": " We can do quantum gravity in the standard four dimensions we actually see,", "tokens": [51210, 492, 393, 360, 13018, 12110, 294, 264, 3832, 1451, 12819, 321, 767, 536, 11, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 168570, "start": 1706.14, "end": 1708.24, "text": " up, down, left, right, forward, back in time.", "tokens": [51387, 493, 11, 760, 11, 1411, 11, 558, 11, 2128, 11, 646, 294, 565, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 168570, "start": 1708.38, "end": 1708.74, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51499, 1079, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 168570, "start": 1709.28, "end": 1710.88, "text": " We can work in a four-dimensional universe.", "tokens": [51544, 492, 393, 589, 294, 257, 1451, 12, 18759, 6445, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 168570, "start": 1711.48, "end": 1713.3600000000001, "text": " But to make this work without strings,", "tokens": [51654, 583, 281, 652, 341, 589, 1553, 13985, 11, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19179920589222627, "compression_ratio": 1.7533783783783783, "no_speech_prob": 1.755566395381103e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 171336, "start": 1713.36, "end": 1716.8999999999999, "text": " Fliction leans heavily into a different kind of fundamental symmetry.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 476, 599, 10950, 666, 257, 819, 733, 295, 8088, 25440, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 171336, "start": 1717.56, "end": 1721.34, "text": " The text details a staggering proposal from physicists Latham Boyle,", "tokens": [50575, 440, 2487, 4365, 257, 42974, 11494, 490, 48716, 441, 998, 335, 9486, 306, 11, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 171336, "start": 1721.4599999999998, "end": 1725.32, "text": " Karen Finn, and Neil Turok regarding a CPT-symmetric universe.", "tokens": [50770, 14834, 21066, 11, 293, 18615, 314, 7052, 74, 8595, 257, 22431, 51, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 6445, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 171336, "start": 1725.82, "end": 1729.1399999999999, "text": " CPT stands for charge, parity, and time, correct?", "tokens": [50988, 22431, 51, 7382, 337, 4602, 11, 44747, 11, 293, 565, 11, 3006, 30, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 171336, "start": 1729.4599999999998, "end": 1729.78, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51170, 12753, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 171336, "start": 1729.9199999999998, "end": 1731.8, "text": " It is a fundamental symmetry in physics,", "tokens": [51193, 467, 307, 257, 8088, 25440, 294, 10649, 11, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 171336, "start": 1732.2199999999998, "end": 1734.36, "text": " stating that if you swap all particles for antiparticles,", "tokens": [51308, 26688, 300, 498, 291, 18135, 439, 10007, 337, 2511, 647, 446, 5350, 11, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 171336, "start": 1735.24, "end": 1736.2199999999998, "text": " which is charge,", "tokens": [51459, 597, 307, 4602, 11, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18501824314154466, "compression_ratio": 1.5798319327731092, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906343504654366e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 173622, "start": 1736.22, "end": 1738.9, "text": " flip the spatial coordinates like a mirror,", "tokens": [50365, 7929, 264, 23598, 21056, 411, 257, 8013, 11, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 173622, "start": 1739.26, "end": 1739.98, "text": " which is parity,", "tokens": [50517, 597, 307, 44747, 11, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 173622, "start": 1740.38, "end": 1741.78, "text": " and reverse the flow of time,", "tokens": [50573, 293, 9943, 264, 3095, 295, 565, 11, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 173622, "start": 1742.06, "end": 1742.88, "text": " which is time.", "tokens": [50657, 597, 307, 565, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 173622, "start": 1743.68, "end": 1746.42, "text": " The laws of physics should remain exactly the same.", "tokens": [50738, 440, 6064, 295, 10649, 820, 6222, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 173622, "start": 1747.58, "end": 1752.24, "text": " Boyle, Finn, and Turok proposed that this symmetry applies to the entire universe itself.", "tokens": [50933, 9486, 306, 11, 21066, 11, 293, 314, 7052, 74, 10348, 300, 341, 25440, 13165, 281, 264, 2302, 6445, 2564, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 173622, "start": 1752.6000000000001, "end": 1755.8, "text": " They proposed that the universe didn't just start at the Big Bang and move forward.", "tokens": [51184, 814, 10348, 300, 264, 6445, 994, 380, 445, 722, 412, 264, 5429, 11538, 293, 1286, 2128, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 173622, "start": 1756.04, "end": 1757.92, "text": " The Big Bang is not an absolute beginning.", "tokens": [51356, 440, 5429, 11538, 307, 406, 364, 8236, 2863, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 173622, "start": 1758.26, "end": 1758.94, "text": " It is a mirror.", "tokens": [51467, 467, 307, 257, 8013, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 173622, "start": 1759.16, "end": 1759.52, "text": " A mirror.", "tokens": [51512, 316, 8013, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23167928643182878, "compression_ratio": 1.6736401673640167, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984659342688223e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 175952, "start": 1759.52, "end": 1762.6399999999999, "text": " So there is our universe expanding and moving forward in time.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 456, 307, 527, 6445, 14702, 293, 2684, 2128, 294, 565, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 175952, "start": 1762.98, "end": 1766.12, "text": " And on the other side of the Big Bang, there is an anti-universe.", "tokens": [50538, 400, 322, 264, 661, 1252, 295, 264, 5429, 11538, 11, 456, 307, 364, 6061, 12, 409, 5376, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 175952, "start": 1766.34, "end": 1766.74, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50706, 7587, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 175952, "start": 1767.04, "end": 1769.18, "text": " An anti-universe made of anti-matter,", "tokens": [50741, 1107, 6061, 12, 409, 5376, 1027, 295, 6061, 12, 76, 1161, 11, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 175952, "start": 1769.6399999999999, "end": 1772.82, "text": " expanding and moving backward in time away from the singularity.", "tokens": [50871, 14702, 293, 2684, 23897, 294, 565, 1314, 490, 264, 20010, 507, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 175952, "start": 1773.36, "end": 1775.3, "text": " The Big Bang didn't just create us.", "tokens": [51057, 440, 5429, 11538, 994, 380, 445, 1884, 505, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 175952, "start": 1775.56, "end": 1778.3799999999999, "text": " It created our exact reflection in the mirror of time.", "tokens": [51167, 467, 2942, 527, 1900, 12914, 294, 264, 8013, 295, 565, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 175952, "start": 1778.92, "end": 1783.5, "text": " This completely preserves the CPT-symmetry of the cosmos from the moment of inception.", "tokens": [51335, 639, 2584, 1183, 9054, 264, 22431, 51, 12, 3187, 2174, 9889, 295, 264, 41794, 490, 264, 1623, 295, 49834, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 175952, "start": 1783.78, "end": 1784.58, "text": " That is heavy.", "tokens": [51578, 663, 307, 4676, 13, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16793238321940104, "compression_ratio": 1.7745901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813152432793022e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 178458, "start": 1784.58, "end": 1790.02, "text": " But how does the CPT-symmetric universe solve the mathematical anomalies without resorting to string theory?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 577, 775, 264, 22431, 51, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 6445, 5039, 264, 18894, 24769, 48872, 1553, 19606, 278, 281, 6798, 5261, 30, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 178458, "start": 1790.36, "end": 1793.98, "text": " I know the paper spends a lot of time on something called dimension zero scalars.", "tokens": [50654, 286, 458, 264, 3035, 25620, 257, 688, 295, 565, 322, 746, 1219, 10139, 4018, 15664, 685, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 178458, "start": 1794.3799999999999, "end": 1794.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50855, 1079, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 178458, "start": 1794.96, "end": 1798.1599999999999, "text": " To make a 4D universe mathematically viable at the quantum level,", "tokens": [50884, 1407, 652, 257, 1017, 35, 6445, 44003, 22024, 412, 264, 13018, 1496, 11, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 178458, "start": 1798.98, "end": 1801.82, "text": " the model introduces these dimension zero scalars.", "tokens": [51085, 264, 2316, 31472, 613, 10139, 4018, 15664, 685, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 178458, "start": 1802.46, "end": 1806.1799999999998, "text": " They are highly unique scalar fields that do not transform or change", "tokens": [51259, 814, 366, 5405, 3845, 39684, 7909, 300, 360, 406, 4088, 420, 1319, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 178458, "start": 1806.1799999999998, "end": 1808.54, "text": " under certain mathematical rescalings of the universe.", "tokens": [51445, 833, 1629, 18894, 9610, 304, 1109, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 178458, "start": 1809.26, "end": 1813.34, "text": " Now, natively, these fields seem to have their own severe ghost problems.", "tokens": [51599, 823, 11, 8470, 356, 11, 613, 7909, 1643, 281, 362, 641, 1065, 8922, 8359, 2740, 13, 51803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 178458, "start": 1813.3999999999999, "end": 1814.22, "text": " Of course they do.", "tokens": [51806, 2720, 1164, 436, 360, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11955630685400775, "compression_ratio": 1.7119741100323624, "no_speech_prob": 1.432201254293608e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 181422, "start": 1814.22, "end": 1818.68, "text": " But again, fliction demonstrates that a massive inherent gauge symmetry in the framework", "tokens": [50365, 583, 797, 11, 932, 4105, 31034, 300, 257, 5994, 26387, 17924, 25440, 294, 264, 8388, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 181422, "start": 1818.68, "end": 1821.94, "text": " projects those ghosts entirely out of the observable sector.", "tokens": [50588, 4455, 729, 21744, 7696, 484, 295, 264, 9951, 712, 6977, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 181422, "start": 1822.68, "end": 1826.6200000000001, "text": " But the true mathematical triumph of these dimension zero scalars", "tokens": [50788, 583, 264, 2074, 18894, 29156, 295, 613, 10139, 4018, 15664, 685, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 181422, "start": 1826.6200000000001, "end": 1829.9, "text": " is what they do to the vacuum energy and the whale anomaly.", "tokens": [50985, 307, 437, 436, 360, 281, 264, 14224, 2281, 293, 264, 25370, 42737, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 181422, "start": 1830.22, "end": 1831.88, "text": " I need you to explain the whale anomaly.", "tokens": [51165, 286, 643, 291, 281, 2903, 264, 25370, 42737, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 181422, "start": 1832.3, "end": 1835.22, "text": " What is it and why is it so bad that we need to cancel it?", "tokens": [51269, 708, 307, 309, 293, 983, 307, 309, 370, 1578, 300, 321, 643, 281, 10373, 309, 30, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 181422, "start": 1835.32, "end": 1839.18, "text": " Well, in classical physics, certain equations have what is called conformal symmetry.", "tokens": [51420, 1042, 11, 294, 13735, 10649, 11, 1629, 11787, 362, 437, 307, 1219, 18975, 304, 25440, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 181422, "start": 1839.98, "end": 1841.06, "text": " They're scale invariant.", "tokens": [51653, 814, 434, 4373, 33270, 394, 13, 51707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12220871966818105, "compression_ratio": 1.658703071672355, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281831347915055e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 184106, "start": 1841.06, "end": 1844.8999999999999, "text": " It means the physics looks the same whether you zoom way in or zoom way out.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 264, 10649, 1542, 264, 912, 1968, 291, 8863, 636, 294, 420, 8863, 636, 484, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 184106, "start": 1845.52, "end": 1847.86, "text": " But when you apply quantum mechanics to these equations,", "tokens": [50588, 583, 562, 291, 3079, 13018, 12939, 281, 613, 11787, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 184106, "start": 1848.52, "end": 1850.78, "text": " the quantum fluctuations break that symmetry.", "tokens": [50738, 264, 13018, 45276, 1821, 300, 25440, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 184106, "start": 1851.28, "end": 1852.8999999999999, "text": " The math starts spitting out errors.", "tokens": [50876, 440, 5221, 3719, 637, 2414, 484, 13603, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 184106, "start": 1853.6799999999998, "end": 1855.94, "text": " That breaking of symmetry is the whale anomaly.", "tokens": [50996, 663, 7697, 295, 25440, 307, 264, 25370, 42737, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 184106, "start": 1856.52, "end": 1858.56, "text": " Imagine a perfectly balanced spinning top.", "tokens": [51138, 11739, 257, 6239, 13902, 15640, 1192, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 184106, "start": 1858.6599999999999, "end": 1859.6799999999998, "text": " It spins flawlessly.", "tokens": [51245, 467, 31587, 13717, 12048, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 184106, "start": 1860.26, "end": 1861.4199999999998, "text": " That's your classical symmetry.", "tokens": [51325, 663, 311, 428, 13735, 25440, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 184106, "start": 1862.0, "end": 1865.1799999999998, "text": " But quantum mechanics introduces tiny random vibrations.", "tokens": [51412, 583, 13018, 12939, 31472, 5870, 4974, 32339, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20426994009116262, "compression_ratio": 1.7231404958677685, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346918172733705e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 186518, "start": 1865.18, "end": 1868.8, "text": " Suddenly, the top starts wobbling violently out of control.", "tokens": [50365, 21194, 11, 264, 1192, 3719, 33775, 18262, 46728, 484, 295, 1969, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 186518, "start": 1869.3600000000001, "end": 1870.74, "text": " That wobble is the anomaly.", "tokens": [50574, 663, 33775, 638, 307, 264, 42737, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 186518, "start": 1871.1200000000001, "end": 1873.5800000000002, "text": " And if you don't cancel that wobble, the top crashes.", "tokens": [50662, 400, 498, 291, 500, 380, 10373, 300, 33775, 638, 11, 264, 1192, 28642, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 186518, "start": 1874.0, "end": 1874.78, "text": " The theory fails.", "tokens": [50806, 440, 5261, 18199, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 186518, "start": 1875.0600000000002, "end": 1875.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50859, 7587, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 186518, "start": 1876.0600000000002, "end": 1877.8400000000001, "text": " So how do you stabilize the spinning top?", "tokens": [50909, 407, 577, 360, 291, 31870, 264, 15640, 1192, 30, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 186518, "start": 1878.22, "end": 1882.7, "text": " To cancel the whale anomaly and balance the vacuum energy without inventing supersymmetry", "tokens": [51017, 1407, 10373, 264, 25370, 42737, 293, 4772, 264, 14224, 2281, 1553, 7962, 278, 37906, 32497, 9889, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 186518, "start": 1882.7, "end": 1888.46, "text": " or extra dimensions, the geometry of a 4D universe demands a very specific counterweight.", "tokens": [51241, 420, 2857, 12819, 11, 264, 18426, 295, 257, 1017, 35, 6445, 15107, 257, 588, 2685, 5682, 12329, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15899730682373048, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6945156215697477e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 188846, "start": 1888.46, "end": 1889.72, "text": " What kind of counterweight?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 733, 295, 5682, 12329, 30, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 188846, "start": 1890.0, "end": 1894.8400000000001, "text": " You take the equations, you set the anomalies to zero, and the math forces a strict requirement.", "tokens": [50442, 509, 747, 264, 11787, 11, 291, 992, 264, 24769, 48872, 281, 4018, 11, 293, 264, 5221, 5874, 257, 10910, 11695, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 188846, "start": 1895.26, "end": 1900.3400000000001, "text": " It demands the existence of exactly three generations of fermions, including right-handed neutrinos.", "tokens": [50705, 467, 15107, 264, 9123, 295, 2293, 1045, 10593, 295, 26558, 626, 11, 3009, 558, 12, 25407, 7989, 12629, 329, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 188846, "start": 1900.44, "end": 1904.56, "text": " And a fermion is a fundamental particle of matter, like an electron or a quark.", "tokens": [50964, 400, 257, 26558, 313, 307, 257, 8088, 12359, 295, 1871, 11, 411, 364, 6084, 420, 257, 421, 809, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 188846, "start": 1904.78, "end": 1905.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51181, 1079, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 188846, "start": 1905.46, "end": 1909.0, "text": " And what is staggering is that the standard model of particle physics,", "tokens": [51215, 400, 437, 307, 42974, 307, 300, 264, 3832, 2316, 295, 12359, 10649, 11, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 188846, "start": 1909.3, "end": 1913.48, "text": " the most tested theory in human history, has exactly three generations of fermions.", "tokens": [51407, 264, 881, 8246, 5261, 294, 1952, 2503, 11, 575, 2293, 1045, 10593, 295, 26558, 626, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 188846, "start": 1913.58, "end": 1915.8, "text": " The electron, the muon, and the tau.", "tokens": [51621, 440, 6084, 11, 264, 2992, 266, 11, 293, 264, 17842, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10843605465359157, "compression_ratio": 1.773851590106007, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414732850218329e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 191580, "start": 1915.8, "end": 1916.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 191580, "start": 1916.96, "end": 1919.5, "text": " For decades, physicists have asked, why three?", "tokens": [50423, 1171, 7878, 11, 48716, 362, 2351, 11, 983, 1045, 30, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 191580, "start": 1919.76, "end": 1921.52, "text": " Why not two or four or 17?", "tokens": [50563, 1545, 406, 732, 420, 1451, 420, 3282, 30, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 191580, "start": 1922.4199999999998, "end": 1925.82, "text": " It has always seemed like an arbitrary random number pulled out of a hat.", "tokens": [50696, 467, 575, 1009, 6576, 411, 364, 23211, 4974, 1230, 7373, 484, 295, 257, 2385, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 191580, "start": 1926.24, "end": 1929.18, "text": " But this framework suggests it's not a random number at all.", "tokens": [50887, 583, 341, 8388, 13409, 309, 311, 406, 257, 4974, 1230, 412, 439, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 191580, "start": 1929.9199999999998, "end": 1935.1399999999999, "text": " Three generations is a strict, inescapable, geometric requirement", "tokens": [51071, 6244, 10593, 307, 257, 10910, 11, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 11, 33246, 11695, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 191580, "start": 1935.1399999999999, "end": 1939.2, "text": " to cancel gravitational anomalies in a four-dimensional universe.", "tokens": [51332, 281, 10373, 28538, 24769, 48872, 294, 257, 1451, 12, 18759, 6445, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 191580, "start": 1939.26, "end": 1939.96, "text": " That's amazing.", "tokens": [51538, 663, 311, 2243, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 191580, "start": 1940.1599999999999, "end": 1944.3999999999999, "text": " The universe has to have three generations of matter, or it tears itself apart mathematically.", "tokens": [51583, 440, 6445, 575, 281, 362, 1045, 10593, 295, 1871, 11, 420, 309, 10462, 2564, 4936, 44003, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17373809479830557, "compression_ratio": 1.6056338028169015, "no_speech_prob": 2.0125541858040386e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 194440, "start": 1944.4, "end": 1947.7, "text": " That is the most satisfying answer to a physics question I've ever heard.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 881, 18348, 1867, 281, 257, 10649, 1168, 286, 600, 1562, 2198, 13, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 194440, "start": 1948.1200000000001, "end": 1952.7800000000002, "text": " But it gets even better, because this model also solves one of the biggest mysteries in astronomy,", "tokens": [50551, 583, 309, 2170, 754, 1101, 11, 570, 341, 2316, 611, 39890, 472, 295, 264, 3880, 30785, 294, 37844, 11, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 194440, "start": 1953.46, "end": 1954.0, "text": " dark matter.", "tokens": [50818, 2877, 1871, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 194440, "start": 1954.5600000000002, "end": 1957.4, "text": " And it does it without inventing any new magical particles.", "tokens": [50873, 400, 309, 775, 309, 1553, 7962, 278, 604, 777, 12066, 10007, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 194440, "start": 1958.18, "end": 1958.5600000000002, "text": " That's right.", "tokens": [51054, 663, 311, 558, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 194440, "start": 1958.96, "end": 1960.76, "text": " Explain how the model handles dark matter.", "tokens": [51093, 39574, 577, 264, 2316, 18722, 2877, 1871, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 194440, "start": 1961.1000000000001, "end": 1963.8600000000001, "text": " Well, standard physics has been searching for dark matter for decades,", "tokens": [51200, 1042, 11, 3832, 10649, 575, 668, 10808, 337, 2877, 1871, 337, 7878, 11, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 194440, "start": 1964.0600000000002, "end": 1969.7, "text": " inventing hypothetical particles like axions or WIMPs to explain all the extra gravity we see in galaxies.", "tokens": [51348, 7962, 278, 33053, 10007, 411, 6360, 626, 420, 343, 6324, 23043, 281, 2903, 439, 264, 2857, 12110, 321, 536, 294, 28755, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13715753220675284, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.741478163931609e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 196970, "start": 1969.7, "end": 1973.66, "text": " But if this CPT-symmetric mirror universe model is true,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 341, 22431, 51, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 8013, 6445, 2316, 307, 2074, 11, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13307055998384282, "compression_ratio": 1.5107296137339057, "no_speech_prob": 1.404806826421634e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 196970, "start": 1974.0, "end": 1975.9, "text": " it predicts that right at the Big Bang,", "tokens": [50580, 309, 6069, 82, 300, 558, 412, 264, 5429, 11538, 11, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13307055998384282, "compression_ratio": 1.5107296137339057, "no_speech_prob": 1.404806826421634e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 196970, "start": 1976.26, "end": 1980.1200000000001, "text": " a massive amount of incredibly heavy right-handed neutrinos are produced.", "tokens": [50693, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 6252, 4676, 558, 12, 25407, 7989, 12629, 329, 366, 7126, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13307055998384282, "compression_ratio": 1.5107296137339057, "no_speech_prob": 1.404806826421634e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 196970, "start": 1980.52, "end": 1984.96, "text": " The paper predicts their mass is roughly 5 times 10 to the 8 gig electron volts.", "tokens": [50906, 440, 3035, 6069, 82, 641, 2758, 307, 9810, 1025, 1413, 1266, 281, 264, 1649, 8741, 6084, 22322, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13307055998384282, "compression_ratio": 1.5107296137339057, "no_speech_prob": 1.404806826421634e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 196970, "start": 1985.42, "end": 1990.24, "text": " And they are produced by the exact same mechanism that produces Hawking radiation from a black hole.", "tokens": [51151, 400, 436, 366, 7126, 538, 264, 1900, 912, 7513, 300, 14725, 9325, 5092, 12420, 490, 257, 2211, 5458, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13307055998384282, "compression_ratio": 1.5107296137339057, "no_speech_prob": 1.404806826421634e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 199024, "start": 1990.24, "end": 1994.34, "text": " And when you calculate the density of these primordial heavy neutrinos,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 562, 291, 8873, 264, 10305, 295, 613, 2886, 765, 831, 4676, 7989, 12629, 329, 11, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 199024, "start": 1994.84, "end": 2000.6200000000001, "text": " it perfectly, flawlessly matches the exact amount of dark matter we observe in the universe today.", "tokens": [50595, 309, 6239, 11, 13717, 12048, 10676, 264, 1900, 2372, 295, 2877, 1871, 321, 11441, 294, 264, 6445, 965, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 199024, "start": 2000.72, "end": 2001.6200000000001, "text": " It's a perfect fit.", "tokens": [50889, 467, 311, 257, 2176, 3318, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 199024, "start": 2001.74, "end": 2004.4, "text": " No dark sector, no invisible axions,", "tokens": [50940, 883, 2877, 6977, 11, 572, 14603, 6360, 626, 11, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 199024, "start": 2004.9, "end": 2008.96, "text": " just heavy neutrinos required by the mirror symmetry of the Big Bang.", "tokens": [51098, 445, 4676, 7989, 12629, 329, 4739, 538, 264, 8013, 25440, 295, 264, 5429, 11538, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 199024, "start": 2009.1200000000001, "end": 2011.1200000000001, "text": " It is an incredibly elegant solution.", "tokens": [51309, 467, 307, 364, 6252, 21117, 3827, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16588737798291583, "compression_ratio": 1.5509259259259258, "no_speech_prob": 2.134002176357175e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 201112, "start": 2011.12, "end": 2015.3, "text": " And if we pull back and connect this to the macroscopic picture of the cosmos,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 321, 2235, 646, 293, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 3036, 295, 264, 41794, 11, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 201112, "start": 2015.9399999999998, "end": 2020.4199999999998, "text": " it fundamentally reframes our understanding of why the universe looks the way it does.", "tokens": [50606, 309, 17879, 13334, 1632, 527, 3701, 295, 983, 264, 6445, 1542, 264, 636, 309, 775, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 201112, "start": 2020.6, "end": 2022.4199999999998, "text": " We have to consider gravitational entropy.", "tokens": [50839, 492, 362, 281, 1949, 28538, 30867, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 201112, "start": 2022.9399999999998, "end": 2026.82, "text": " Right, because standard cosmology relies on this concept called cosmic inflation.", "tokens": [50956, 1779, 11, 570, 3832, 22207, 1793, 30910, 322, 341, 3410, 1219, 27614, 15860, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 201112, "start": 2027.1599999999999, "end": 2029.6799999999998, "text": " The idea that a fraction of a second after the Big Bang,", "tokens": [51167, 440, 1558, 300, 257, 14135, 295, 257, 1150, 934, 264, 5429, 11538, 11, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 201112, "start": 2029.82, "end": 2032.08, "text": " the universe expanded faster than the speed of light.", "tokens": [51300, 264, 6445, 14342, 4663, 813, 264, 3073, 295, 1442, 13, 51413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 201112, "start": 2032.4599999999998, "end": 2037.4799999999998, "text": " And inflation was invented to explain why the universe today is so perfectly flat and so uniform.", "tokens": [51432, 400, 15860, 390, 14479, 281, 2903, 983, 264, 6445, 965, 307, 370, 6239, 4962, 293, 370, 9452, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14067667722702026, "compression_ratio": 1.7030716723549488, "no_speech_prob": 3.5461371252626384e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 203748, "start": 2037.48, "end": 2041.76, "text": " Why the temperature of space is exactly the same everywhere we look.", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 264, 4292, 295, 1901, 307, 2293, 264, 912, 5315, 321, 574, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 203748, "start": 2042.1200000000001, "end": 2045.4, "text": " But Fliction's framework, and the Turok-Boyle model it rests upon,", "tokens": [50597, 583, 3235, 4105, 311, 8388, 11, 293, 264, 314, 7052, 74, 12, 31378, 306, 2316, 309, 39755, 3564, 11, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 203748, "start": 2045.8600000000001, "end": 2047.68, "text": " completely rejects cosmic inflation.", "tokens": [50784, 2584, 8248, 82, 27614, 15860, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 203748, "start": 2048.54, "end": 2050.16, "text": " In fact, it offers a testable prediction.", "tokens": [50918, 682, 1186, 11, 309, 7736, 257, 1500, 712, 17630, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 203748, "start": 2051.06, "end": 2054.02, "text": " It predicts a tensor-to-scalar ratio of exactly zero.", "tokens": [51044, 467, 6069, 82, 257, 40863, 12, 1353, 12, 4417, 12031, 8509, 295, 2293, 4018, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 203748, "start": 2054.2400000000002, "end": 2054.88, "text": " Which means what?", "tokens": [51203, 3013, 1355, 437, 30, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 203748, "start": 2055.52, "end": 2059.18, "text": " The tensor-to-scalar ratio is a measurement of primordial gravitational waves,", "tokens": [51267, 440, 40863, 12, 1353, 12, 4417, 12031, 8509, 307, 257, 13160, 295, 2886, 765, 831, 28538, 9417, 11, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 203748, "start": 2059.56, "end": 2062.48, "text": " ripples in space-time that would have been caused by the violent,", "tokens": [51469, 367, 37674, 294, 1901, 12, 3766, 300, 576, 362, 668, 7008, 538, 264, 11867, 11, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 203748, "start": 2062.88, "end": 2064.72, "text": " faster-than-light expansion of inflation.", "tokens": [51635, 4663, 12, 24852, 12, 2764, 11260, 295, 15860, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15358822844749273, "compression_ratio": 1.6310344827586207, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351744599133136e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 206472, "start": 2064.72, "end": 2069.24, "text": " If inflation happened, there should be a measurable ratio of these waves.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 15860, 2011, 11, 456, 820, 312, 257, 43615, 8509, 295, 613, 9417, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 206472, "start": 2070.14, "end": 2072.2999999999997, "text": " Fliction's model says there was no inflation,", "tokens": [50636, 3235, 4105, 311, 2316, 1619, 456, 390, 572, 15860, 11, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 206472, "start": 2072.68, "end": 2075.64, "text": " so there should be zero primordial gravitational waves.", "tokens": [50763, 370, 456, 820, 312, 4018, 2886, 765, 831, 28538, 9417, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 206472, "start": 2075.8799999999997, "end": 2077.22, "text": " Okay, but if there was no inflation,", "tokens": [50923, 1033, 11, 457, 498, 456, 390, 572, 15860, 11, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 206472, "start": 2077.3599999999997, "end": 2080.2, "text": " how do they explain why the universe is so flat and uniform?", "tokens": [50997, 577, 360, 436, 2903, 983, 264, 6445, 307, 370, 4962, 293, 9452, 30, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 206472, "start": 2080.9399999999996, "end": 2081.2999999999997, "text": " Thermodynamics.", "tokens": [51176, 38957, 35483, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 206472, "start": 2081.8199999999997, "end": 2085.9399999999996, "text": " When you calculate the gravitational entropy of the entire cosmological ensemble,", "tokens": [51220, 1133, 291, 8873, 264, 28538, 30867, 295, 264, 2302, 22207, 4383, 19492, 11, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 206472, "start": 2086.2799999999997, "end": 2088.16, "text": " all the possible shapes the universe could take,", "tokens": [51443, 439, 264, 1944, 10854, 264, 6445, 727, 747, 11, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1694761657714844, "compression_ratio": 1.7647058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524380806019593e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 208816, "start": 2088.16, "end": 2093.16, "text": " the total entropy is maximized when the universe is flat, homogenous, and isotropic,", "tokens": [50365, 264, 3217, 30867, 307, 5138, 1602, 562, 264, 6445, 307, 4962, 11, 3655, 45519, 11, 293, 38018, 39173, 11, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 208816, "start": 2093.54, "end": 2096.12, "text": " with a small, positive cosmological constant.", "tokens": [50634, 365, 257, 1359, 11, 3353, 22207, 4383, 5754, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 208816, "start": 2096.3599999999997, "end": 2101.08, "text": " So a flat, uniform universe is simply the most mathematically probable macro state.", "tokens": [50775, 407, 257, 4962, 11, 9452, 6445, 307, 2935, 264, 881, 44003, 21759, 18887, 1785, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 208816, "start": 2101.3399999999997, "end": 2101.8999999999996, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51024, 7587, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 208816, "start": 2102.3199999999997, "end": 2106.3199999999997, "text": " It's like asking why, when you release a canister of gas in a room,", "tokens": [51073, 467, 311, 411, 3365, 983, 11, 562, 291, 4374, 257, 393, 1964, 295, 4211, 294, 257, 1808, 11, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 208816, "start": 2106.7, "end": 2110.24, "text": " the gas fills the room evenly, instead of mysteriously huddling in one corner.", "tokens": [51292, 264, 4211, 22498, 264, 1808, 17658, 11, 2602, 295, 11010, 8994, 276, 26656, 1688, 294, 472, 4538, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14939014033267373, "compression_ratio": 1.5611814345991561, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735391505414253e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 211024, "start": 2110.24, "end": 2114.3799999999997, "text": " It's not because a magical, faster-than-light force pushed the gas everywhere.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 570, 257, 12066, 11, 4663, 12, 24852, 12, 2764, 3464, 9152, 264, 4211, 5315, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 211024, "start": 2114.6, "end": 2115.24, "text": " It's just thermodynamics.", "tokens": [50583, 467, 311, 445, 8810, 35483, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 211024, "start": 2116.08, "end": 2117.3999999999996, "text": " The gas naturally spreads out.", "tokens": [50657, 440, 4211, 8195, 25728, 484, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 211024, "start": 2117.54, "end": 2117.7599999999998, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50730, 1079, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 211024, "start": 2118.04, "end": 2121.24, "text": " An evenly distributed gas is statistically the most probable state.", "tokens": [50755, 1107, 17658, 12631, 4211, 307, 36478, 264, 881, 21759, 1785, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 211024, "start": 2121.8799999999997, "end": 2124.9799999999996, "text": " The universe is flat and uniform for the exact same reason.", "tokens": [50947, 440, 6445, 307, 4962, 293, 9452, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 1778, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 211024, "start": 2125.2799999999997, "end": 2128.3599999999997, "text": " It is the most thermodynamically stable outcome of the Big Bang.", "tokens": [51117, 467, 307, 264, 881, 8810, 21399, 984, 8351, 9700, 295, 264, 5429, 11538, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 211024, "start": 2128.4199999999996, "end": 2130.54, "text": " It is a stunning, cohesive paradigm.", "tokens": [51274, 467, 307, 257, 18550, 11, 43025, 24709, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 211024, "start": 2130.8199999999997, "end": 2136.3999999999996, "text": " It unites time, gravity, quantum ghosts, and the Big Bang under one mathematical umbrella.", "tokens": [51394, 467, 517, 3324, 565, 11, 12110, 11, 13018, 21744, 11, 293, 264, 5429, 11538, 833, 472, 18894, 21925, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15072687740983634, "compression_ratio": 1.6886446886446886, "no_speech_prob": 1.824662166152735e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 213640, "start": 2136.4, "end": 2140.82, "text": " But, you know, as any good empirical scientist will tell you,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 382, 604, 665, 31886, 12662, 486, 980, 291, 11, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 213640, "start": 2141.28, "end": 2144.86, "text": " it's one thing to have a grand, beautiful mathematical theory about the early universe.", "tokens": [50609, 309, 311, 472, 551, 281, 362, 257, 2697, 11, 2238, 18894, 5261, 466, 264, 2440, 6445, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 213640, "start": 2145.3, "end": 2147.58, "text": " It is another thing entirely to actually prove it.", "tokens": [50810, 467, 307, 1071, 551, 7696, 281, 767, 7081, 309, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 213640, "start": 2147.7000000000003, "end": 2148.58, "text": " Math needs data.", "tokens": [50930, 15776, 2203, 1412, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 213640, "start": 2148.82, "end": 2150.3, "text": " Math is great, but we need data.", "tokens": [50986, 15776, 307, 869, 11, 457, 321, 643, 1412, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 213640, "start": 2150.52, "end": 2153.48, "text": " We have to look at the physical fossils left behind by the Big Bang.", "tokens": [51071, 492, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 4001, 39159, 1411, 2261, 538, 264, 5429, 11538, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 213640, "start": 2153.7000000000003, "end": 2156.08, "text": " Which brings us to the fifth section of our deep dive,", "tokens": [51230, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 9266, 3541, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 11, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 213640, "start": 2156.32, "end": 2159.94, "text": " and a massive shift from theoretical physics to observational astronomy.", "tokens": [51361, 293, 257, 5994, 5513, 490, 20864, 10649, 281, 9951, 1478, 37844, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 213640, "start": 2160.42, "end": 2162.94, "text": " We need to talk about the fossil manifolds paper,", "tokens": [51566, 492, 643, 281, 751, 466, 264, 18737, 8173, 31518, 3035, 11, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12920358104090537, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524408995276078e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 216294, "start": 2162.94, "end": 2167.9, "text": " and the incredible discovery made by the James Webb Space Telescope in 2026.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 264, 4651, 12114, 1027, 538, 264, 5678, 49649, 8705, 48595, 13960, 294, 945, 10880, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 216294, "start": 2168.32, "end": 2171.7400000000002, "text": " This is where the abstract mathematics suddenly becomes very, very physical.", "tokens": [50634, 639, 307, 689, 264, 12649, 18666, 5800, 3643, 588, 11, 588, 4001, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 216294, "start": 2172.66, "end": 2179.04, "text": " In early 2026, the JWST detected an ultra-faint galaxy designated LAP-1b.", "tokens": [50851, 682, 2440, 945, 10880, 11, 264, 49885, 6840, 21896, 364, 14808, 12, 69, 5114, 17639, 21688, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 65, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 216294, "start": 2179.84, "end": 2182.5, "text": " They measured its redshift at approximately 6.6.", "tokens": [51210, 814, 12690, 1080, 2182, 47445, 412, 10447, 1386, 13, 21, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 216294, "start": 2182.62, "end": 2184.2000000000003, "text": " Which, for those who don't speak astronomy,", "tokens": [51349, 3013, 11, 337, 729, 567, 500, 380, 1710, 37844, 11, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 216294, "start": 2184.4, "end": 2189.0, "text": " means we are seeing this galaxy as it existed roughly 800 million years after the Big Bang.", "tokens": [51438, 1355, 321, 366, 2577, 341, 17639, 382, 309, 13135, 9810, 13083, 2459, 924, 934, 264, 5429, 11538, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 216294, "start": 2189.32, "end": 2191.58, "text": " That is incredibly early in the history of the universe.", "tokens": [51684, 663, 307, 6252, 2440, 294, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13096450740455562, "compression_ratio": 1.5326797385620916, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619814248788889e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 219158, "start": 2191.58, "end": 2192.54, "text": " It is early, yes.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 2440, 11, 2086, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 219158, "start": 2192.9, "end": 2194.7999999999997, "text": " But it's not just its age that makes it important.", "tokens": [50431, 583, 309, 311, 406, 445, 1080, 3205, 300, 1669, 309, 1021, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 219158, "start": 2195.12, "end": 2199.62, "text": " It is its bizarrely tiny size, and its unprecedented chemical purity.", "tokens": [50542, 467, 307, 1080, 18265, 356, 5870, 2744, 11, 293, 1080, 21555, 7313, 34382, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 219158, "start": 2200.3199999999997, "end": 2206.48, "text": " The text details that LAP-1b has an estimated stellar mass of under 3,300 solar masses.", "tokens": [50802, 440, 2487, 4365, 300, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 65, 575, 364, 14109, 42333, 2758, 295, 833, 805, 11, 12566, 7936, 23935, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 219158, "start": 2206.92, "end": 2210.36, "text": " To put that in perspective, our Milky Way galaxy has hundreds of billions of stars.", "tokens": [51132, 1407, 829, 300, 294, 4585, 11, 527, 38465, 9558, 17639, 575, 6779, 295, 17375, 295, 6105, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 219158, "start": 2211.02, "end": 2213.9, "text": " 3,300 solar masses is less than a rounding error.", "tokens": [51337, 805, 11, 12566, 7936, 23935, 307, 1570, 813, 257, 48237, 6713, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 219158, "start": 2214.08, "end": 2216.72, "text": " It's more like a tiny star cluster than a full-fledged galaxy.", "tokens": [51490, 467, 311, 544, 411, 257, 5870, 3543, 13630, 813, 257, 1577, 12, 69, 1493, 3004, 17639, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 219158, "start": 2216.92, "end": 2217.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51632, 7587, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 219158, "start": 2217.46, "end": 2220.42, "text": " And its chemistry is completely anomalous compared to standard galaxies.", "tokens": [51659, 400, 1080, 12558, 307, 2584, 24769, 11553, 5347, 281, 3832, 28755, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1228613924624315, "compression_ratio": 1.6185897435897436, "no_speech_prob": 1.4161653620614612e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 222042, "start": 2220.42, "end": 2224.32, "text": " It has an oxygen abundance that is essentially non-existent, just undetectable.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 575, 364, 9169, 23391, 300, 307, 4476, 2107, 12, 18217, 317, 11, 445, 674, 302, 557, 712, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 222042, "start": 2224.54, "end": 2228.26, "text": " But at the same time, it has a presumably elevated carbon-to-oxygen ratio.", "tokens": [50571, 583, 412, 264, 912, 565, 11, 309, 575, 257, 26742, 23457, 5954, 12, 1353, 12, 5230, 8647, 8509, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 222042, "start": 2228.66, "end": 2232.42, "text": " To understand why a lack of oxygen and a spike in carbon is a monumental discovery,", "tokens": [50777, 1407, 1223, 983, 257, 5011, 295, 9169, 293, 257, 21053, 294, 5954, 307, 257, 43105, 12114, 11, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 222042, "start": 2232.66, "end": 2236.46, "text": " we have to introduce the concept of what Fliction calls least overwritten systems.", "tokens": [50977, 321, 362, 281, 5366, 264, 3410, 295, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 1935, 670, 26859, 3652, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 222042, "start": 2236.8, "end": 2237.1, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51184, 1079, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 222042, "start": 2237.7200000000003, "end": 2241.44, "text": " In astronomy, there is a concept called galactic chemical evolution.", "tokens": [51230, 682, 37844, 11, 456, 307, 257, 3410, 1219, 7660, 19892, 7313, 9303, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 222042, "start": 2242.08, "end": 2246.92, "text": " The idea is that galaxies evolve by cooking heavier and heavier elements inside stars.", "tokens": [51448, 440, 1558, 307, 300, 28755, 16693, 538, 6361, 18279, 293, 18279, 4959, 1854, 6105, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16425838633480236, "compression_ratio": 1.6506849315068493, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842777152975e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 224692, "start": 2246.92, "end": 2253.42, "text": " But Fliction points out that what astronomers usually call chemical evolution is actually just chemical averaging.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 437, 43151, 2673, 818, 7313, 9303, 307, 767, 445, 7313, 47308, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1429245842827691, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719126906994296e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 224692, "start": 2253.62, "end": 2256.7000000000003, "text": " It's like mixing colors on a palette, right, but on a cosmic scale.", "tokens": [50700, 467, 311, 411, 11983, 4577, 322, 257, 15851, 11, 558, 11, 457, 322, 257, 27614, 4373, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1429245842827691, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719126906994296e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 224692, "start": 2256.8, "end": 2257.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50859, 7587, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1429245842827691, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719126906994296e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 224692, "start": 2257.64, "end": 2262.36, "text": " A massive star is born, it lives its life, and it dies in a massive supernova explosion.", "tokens": [50901, 316, 5994, 3543, 307, 4232, 11, 309, 2909, 1080, 993, 11, 293, 309, 2714, 294, 257, 5994, 1687, 39486, 15673, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1429245842827691, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719126906994296e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 224692, "start": 2262.88, "end": 2269.1, "text": " That explosion blasts heavy elements like metals, oxygen, iron, out into the surrounding gas cloud.", "tokens": [51163, 663, 15673, 12035, 82, 4676, 4959, 411, 22548, 11, 9169, 11, 6497, 11, 484, 666, 264, 11498, 4211, 4588, 13, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1429245842827691, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 2.7719126906994296e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 226910, "start": 2269.1, "end": 2274.4, "text": " Over millions of years, the next generation of stars forms from that newly enriched gas.", "tokens": [50365, 4886, 6803, 295, 924, 11, 264, 958, 5125, 295, 6105, 6422, 490, 300, 15109, 48624, 4211, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 226910, "start": 2274.58, "end": 2274.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50639, 1779, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 226910, "start": 2274.7799999999997, "end": 2277.66, "text": " They live, they die, and they blast more elements into the mix.", "tokens": [50649, 814, 1621, 11, 436, 978, 11, 293, 436, 12035, 544, 4959, 666, 264, 2890, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 226910, "start": 2278.12, "end": 2279.74, "text": " Every supernova stirs the pot.", "tokens": [50816, 2048, 1687, 39486, 8946, 82, 264, 1847, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 226910, "start": 2279.88, "end": 2282.88, "text": " Every generation overwrites the history of the last.", "tokens": [50904, 2048, 5125, 670, 86, 30931, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 1036, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 226910, "start": 2282.96, "end": 2287.58, "text": " So returning to the paint palette, you start with distinct drops of red and blue and yellow.", "tokens": [51058, 407, 12678, 281, 264, 4225, 15851, 11, 291, 722, 365, 10644, 11438, 295, 2182, 293, 3344, 293, 5566, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 226910, "start": 2288.14, "end": 2290.9, "text": " But if you keep mixing them together, stirring the pot over and over,", "tokens": [51317, 583, 498, 291, 1066, 11983, 552, 1214, 11, 28650, 264, 1847, 670, 293, 670, 11, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 226910, "start": 2290.98, "end": 2293.88, "text": " you eventually just get a muddy, indistinguishable brown.", "tokens": [51459, 291, 4728, 445, 483, 257, 38540, 11, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 6292, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13056817575663077, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 2.125685044651604e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 229388, "start": 2293.88, "end": 2298.02, "text": " You can't look at the brown paint and deduce exactly where the original drop of red was placed.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 380, 574, 412, 264, 6292, 4225, 293, 4172, 4176, 2293, 689, 264, 3380, 3270, 295, 2182, 390, 7074, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 229388, "start": 2298.32, "end": 2299.36, "text": " The history is lost.", "tokens": [50587, 440, 2503, 307, 2731, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 229388, "start": 2299.82, "end": 2300.1400000000003, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50662, 48746, 736, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 229388, "start": 2300.92, "end": 2309.56, "text": " The sequence and the specific geometry of individual stellar explosions in a massive galaxy like our Milky Way are completely irrecoverable.", "tokens": [50717, 440, 8310, 293, 264, 2685, 18426, 295, 2609, 42333, 36872, 294, 257, 5994, 17639, 411, 527, 38465, 9558, 366, 2584, 16014, 12516, 712, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 229388, "start": 2309.9, "end": 2312.04, "text": " They've been stirred and diluted so many times.", "tokens": [51166, 814, 600, 668, 49409, 293, 11504, 4866, 370, 867, 1413, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 229388, "start": 2312.7000000000003, "end": 2317.06, "text": " The interstellar medium of a mature galaxy encodes an integral over millions of events.", "tokens": [51306, 440, 728, 17816, 289, 6399, 295, 257, 14442, 17639, 2058, 4789, 364, 11573, 670, 6803, 295, 3931, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 229388, "start": 2317.6, "end": 2320.44, "text": " But the specific granular history is gone.", "tokens": [51551, 583, 264, 2685, 39962, 2503, 307, 2780, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 229388, "start": 2320.44, "end": 2323.76, "text": " But a least overwritten system like LAP-1B...", "tokens": [51693, 583, 257, 1935, 670, 26859, 1185, 411, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 33, 485, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16413159015750098, "compression_ratio": 1.6378737541528239, "no_speech_prob": 1.8686061812461796e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 232376, "start": 2323.76, "end": 2326.6200000000003, "text": " ...is one that has undergone very few of these averaging events.", "tokens": [50365, 1097, 271, 472, 300, 575, 833, 39743, 588, 1326, 295, 613, 47308, 3931, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352784446116244, "compression_ratio": 1.5659574468085107, "no_speech_prob": 2.0801960414623677e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 232376, "start": 2326.76, "end": 2330.48, "text": " Because it is so small and formed so early, the pot hasn't been stirred.", "tokens": [50515, 1436, 309, 307, 370, 1359, 293, 8693, 370, 2440, 11, 264, 1847, 6132, 380, 668, 49409, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352784446116244, "compression_ratio": 1.5659574468085107, "no_speech_prob": 2.0801960414623677e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 232376, "start": 2330.8, "end": 2332.38, "text": " It is a true physical fossil.", "tokens": [50717, 467, 307, 257, 2074, 4001, 18737, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352784446116244, "compression_ratio": 1.5659574468085107, "no_speech_prob": 2.0801960414623677e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 232376, "start": 2332.6600000000003, "end": 2339.0400000000004, "text": " This chemical state is very simple, but its historical legibility, its ability to tell us exactly what happened, is incredibly high.", "tokens": [50810, 639, 7313, 1785, 307, 588, 2199, 11, 457, 1080, 8584, 1676, 2841, 11, 1080, 3485, 281, 980, 505, 2293, 437, 2011, 11, 307, 6252, 1090, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352784446116244, "compression_ratio": 1.5659574468085107, "no_speech_prob": 2.0801960414623677e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 232376, "start": 2339.28, "end": 2343.4, "text": " And that elevated carbon to oxygen ratio is the cosmic smoking gun.", "tokens": [51141, 400, 300, 23457, 5954, 281, 9169, 8509, 307, 264, 27614, 14055, 3874, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1352784446116244, "compression_ratio": 1.5659574468085107, "no_speech_prob": 2.0801960414623677e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 234340, "start": 2343.4, "end": 2350.82, "text": " It perfectly matches the theoretical signature of what astrophysicists call faint Population III supernovae.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 6239, 10676, 264, 20864, 13397, 295, 437, 5357, 11741, 749, 299, 1751, 818, 21104, 10215, 2776, 16317, 1687, 39486, 68, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24732181674144307, "compression_ratio": 1.5149700598802396, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420395839022444e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 234340, "start": 2350.96, "end": 2351.14, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50743, 1079, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24732181674144307, "compression_ratio": 1.5149700598802396, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420395839022444e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 234340, "start": 2351.28, "end": 2354.52, "text": " Population III stars were the very first stars to ever ignite in the universe.", "tokens": [50759, 10215, 2776, 16317, 6105, 645, 264, 588, 700, 6105, 281, 1562, 49609, 294, 264, 6445, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24732181674144307, "compression_ratio": 1.5149700598802396, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420395839022444e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 234340, "start": 2354.6600000000003, "end": 2357.2000000000003, "text": " They were massive monsters made of pure hydrogen and helium.", "tokens": [50928, 814, 645, 5994, 15785, 1027, 295, 6075, 12697, 293, 40175, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24732181674144307, "compression_ratio": 1.5149700598802396, "no_speech_prob": 2.1420395839022444e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 235720, "start": 2357.2, "end": 2362.4399999999996, "text": " But when these specific stars in LAP-1B died, the explosion was incredibly weak.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 613, 2685, 6105, 294, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 33, 4539, 11, 264, 15673, 390, 6252, 5336, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14033667743206024, "compression_ratio": 1.0707070707070707, "no_speech_prob": 2.020450213385816e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 235720, "start": 2362.48, "end": 2363.9199999999996, "text": " It was a faint supernova.", "tokens": [50629, 467, 390, 257, 21104, 1687, 39486, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14033667743206024, "compression_ratio": 1.0707070707070707, "no_speech_prob": 2.020450213385816e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 236392, "start": 2363.92, "end": 2365.4, "text": " A very specific type of death.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 588, 2685, 2010, 295, 2966, 13, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1656849883323492, "compression_ratio": 1.5964125560538116, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056390580113325e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 236392, "start": 2365.58, "end": 2365.8, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50448, 1779, 13, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1656849883323492, "compression_ratio": 1.5964125560538116, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056390580113325e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 236392, "start": 2366.8, "end": 2373.0, "text": " The explosion was so weak that the heavy oxygen sitting deep in the core of the star couldn't achieve escape velocity.", "tokens": [50509, 440, 15673, 390, 370, 5336, 300, 264, 4676, 9169, 3798, 2452, 294, 264, 4965, 295, 264, 3543, 2809, 380, 4584, 7615, 9269, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1656849883323492, "compression_ratio": 1.5964125560538116, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056390580113325e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 236392, "start": 2373.64, "end": 2376.36, "text": " It fell back into the black hole that was forming at the center.", "tokens": [50851, 467, 5696, 646, 666, 264, 2211, 5458, 300, 390, 15745, 412, 264, 3056, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1656849883323492, "compression_ratio": 1.5964125560538116, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056390580113325e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 236392, "start": 2376.92, "end": 2384.12, "text": " But the lighter carbon, which was sitting in the outer layers of the star, managed to escape the gravity well and blow out into space.", "tokens": [51015, 583, 264, 11546, 5954, 11, 597, 390, 3798, 294, 264, 10847, 7914, 295, 264, 3543, 11, 6453, 281, 7615, 264, 12110, 731, 293, 6327, 484, 666, 1901, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1656849883323492, "compression_ratio": 1.5964125560538116, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056390580113325e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 238412, "start": 2384.12, "end": 2390.8399999999997, "text": " Now connect that physical astronomical fallback mechanism to the pure mathematics we discussed earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 1745, 300, 4001, 49035, 2100, 3207, 7513, 281, 264, 6075, 18666, 321, 7152, 3071, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 238412, "start": 2390.96, "end": 2391.14, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [50707, 3802, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 238412, "start": 2391.44, "end": 2393.54, "text": " The oxygen fell back into the black hole.", "tokens": [50731, 440, 9169, 5696, 646, 666, 264, 2211, 5458, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 238412, "start": 2394.04, "end": 2396.3399999999997, "text": " It was blocked from entering the future of the galaxy.", "tokens": [50861, 467, 390, 15470, 490, 11104, 264, 2027, 295, 264, 17639, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 238412, "start": 2396.72, "end": 2397.9, "text": " The refuse operator.", "tokens": [50995, 440, 16791, 12973, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 238412, "start": 2398.1, "end": 2398.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51064, 7587, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 238412, "start": 2398.88, "end": 2402.22, "text": " This galaxy literally acted out the refuse operator in real life.", "tokens": [51103, 639, 17639, 3736, 20359, 484, 264, 16791, 12973, 294, 957, 993, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 238412, "start": 2402.58, "end": 2404.16, "text": " The oxygen was physically blocked.", "tokens": [51288, 440, 9169, 390, 9762, 15470, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 238412, "start": 2404.38, "end": 2407.8399999999997, "text": " It was refused entry from entering the future history of the interstellar medium.", "tokens": [51378, 467, 390, 14654, 8729, 490, 11104, 264, 2027, 2503, 295, 264, 728, 17816, 289, 6399, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 238412, "start": 2408.3399999999997, "end": 2409.48, "text": " The carbon was admitted.", "tokens": [51576, 440, 5954, 390, 14920, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 238412, "start": 2410.04, "end": 2413.58, "text": " The chemical makeup of LAP-1B isn't just a random assortment of gases.", "tokens": [51661, 440, 7313, 6567, 295, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 33, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 4974, 1256, 477, 518, 295, 21452, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17235198734313484, "compression_ratio": 1.7697594501718212, "no_speech_prob": 1.5431013671712845e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 241358, "start": 2413.58, "end": 2416.2999999999997, "text": " It is literally an event log written in the stars.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 3736, 364, 2280, 3565, 3720, 294, 264, 6105, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 241358, "start": 2416.58, "end": 2420.62, "text": " It is a massive thermodynamic record of an irreversible pathway.", "tokens": [50515, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 8810, 34988, 2136, 295, 364, 16014, 840, 964, 18590, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 241358, "start": 2421.04, "end": 2422.7599999999998, "text": " It is a staggering realization.", "tokens": [50738, 467, 307, 257, 42974, 25138, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 241358, "start": 2423.58, "end": 2426.66, "text": " The galaxy's chemistry functions as an event log in matter.", "tokens": [50865, 440, 17639, 311, 12558, 6828, 382, 364, 2280, 3565, 294, 1871, 13, 51019], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 241358, "start": 2427.06, "end": 2430.52, "text": " It is the continuous plenum being discretized into history.", "tokens": [51039, 467, 307, 264, 10957, 499, 268, 449, 885, 25656, 1602, 666, 2503, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 241358, "start": 2431.36, "end": 2436.22, "text": " And furthermore, the reason LAP-1B exists at all, precisely at this tiny size,", "tokens": [51254, 400, 3052, 3138, 11, 264, 1778, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 33, 8198, 412, 439, 11, 13402, 412, 341, 5870, 2744, 11, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 241358, "start": 2436.46, "end": 2441.7599999999998, "text": " is explained by another mathematical concept from Fliction called the SIED formalism.", "tokens": [51509, 307, 8825, 538, 1071, 18894, 3410, 490, 3235, 4105, 1219, 264, 29083, 4731, 9860, 1434, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15557147384783543, "compression_ratio": 1.5709090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.996579550994637e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 244176, "start": 2441.76, "end": 2444.44, "text": " Scalar eruption via entropic differential.", "tokens": [50365, 2747, 12031, 42584, 5766, 948, 39173, 15756, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 244176, "start": 2444.98, "end": 2445.1600000000003, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50526, 1033, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 244176, "start": 2445.3, "end": 2446.82, "text": " I remember reading about SIED.", "tokens": [50542, 286, 1604, 3760, 466, 29083, 4731, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 244176, "start": 2446.98, "end": 2450.2400000000002, "text": " Standard cosmology says that galaxies form hierarchically, right?", "tokens": [50626, 21298, 22207, 1793, 1619, 300, 28755, 1254, 35250, 984, 11, 558, 30, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 244176, "start": 2450.42, "end": 2451.1000000000004, "text": " Like Legos.", "tokens": [50798, 1743, 7470, 329, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 244176, "start": 2451.5200000000004, "end": 2455.0, "text": " Small clumps of dark matter and gas merge together to make bigger clumps,", "tokens": [50853, 15287, 596, 16951, 295, 2877, 1871, 293, 4211, 22183, 1214, 281, 652, 3801, 596, 16951, 11, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 244176, "start": 2455.1600000000003, "end": 2456.6800000000003, "text": " which merge to make galaxies.", "tokens": [51035, 597, 22183, 281, 652, 28755, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20470722628311372, "compression_ratio": 1.4108108108108108, "no_speech_prob": 1.635968487415096e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 245668, "start": 2456.68, "end": 2458.94, "text": " Yes, the hierarchical bottom-up model.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 264, 35250, 804, 2767, 12, 1010, 2316, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 245668, "start": 2459.72, "end": 2463.58, "text": " But SIE math treats the formation of these early structures completely differently.", "tokens": [50517, 583, 318, 6550, 5221, 19566, 264, 11723, 295, 613, 2440, 9227, 2584, 7614, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 245668, "start": 2464.22, "end": 2468.3199999999997, "text": " It treats structure formation as a threshold instability in a conserved scalar field.", "tokens": [50742, 467, 19566, 3877, 11723, 382, 257, 14678, 34379, 294, 257, 1014, 6913, 39684, 2519, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 245668, "start": 2468.7999999999997, "end": 2473.1, "text": " The closest physical analogy is spinodal decomposition in condensed matter physics.", "tokens": [50971, 440, 13699, 4001, 21663, 307, 6060, 378, 304, 48356, 294, 36398, 1871, 10649, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 245668, "start": 2473.2799999999997, "end": 2474.46, "text": " Which means what, exactly?", "tokens": [51195, 3013, 1355, 437, 11, 2293, 30, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 245668, "start": 2474.72, "end": 2478.3599999999997, "text": " Spinodal decomposition is a mechanism where a uniform mixture of fluids", "tokens": [51267, 29185, 378, 304, 48356, 307, 257, 7513, 689, 257, 9452, 9925, 295, 33033, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 245668, "start": 2478.3599999999997, "end": 2480.9199999999996, "text": " suddenly rapidly separates into distinct regions.", "tokens": [51449, 5800, 12910, 34149, 666, 10644, 10682, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 245668, "start": 2481.18, "end": 2483.12, "text": " It doesn't build up slowly like Legos.", "tokens": [51590, 467, 1177, 380, 1322, 493, 5692, 411, 7470, 329, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16571770427382995, "compression_ratio": 1.6326530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552460357227572e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 248312, "start": 2483.12, "end": 2484.18, "text": " It precipitates.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 23354, 30035, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 248312, "start": 2484.62, "end": 2486.94, "text": " Think of a highly humid cloud suddenly hitting the dew point,", "tokens": [50440, 6557, 295, 257, 5405, 34649, 4588, 5800, 8850, 264, 48745, 935, 11, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 248312, "start": 2487.2, "end": 2490.2999999999997, "text": " and millions of discrete raindrops instantly condensing out of the vapor.", "tokens": [50569, 293, 6803, 295, 27706, 3342, 471, 49715, 13518, 2224, 22481, 484, 295, 264, 20358, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 248312, "start": 2490.7599999999998, "end": 2493.92, "text": " So the universe didn't build galaxies block by block.", "tokens": [50747, 407, 264, 6445, 994, 380, 1322, 28755, 3461, 538, 3461, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 248312, "start": 2494.02, "end": 2497.16, "text": " It precipitated them out of the RSVP plenum.", "tokens": [50910, 467, 23354, 18266, 552, 484, 295, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 248312, "start": 2497.2999999999997, "end": 2497.6, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51074, 1079, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 248312, "start": 2497.9, "end": 2502.2599999999998, "text": " And the mathematics of SID demand that this condensation happens", "tokens": [51104, 400, 264, 18666, 295, 318, 2777, 4733, 300, 341, 2224, 35292, 2314, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 248312, "start": 2502.2599999999998, "end": 2505.64, "text": " at a very specific, mathematically preferred scale.", "tokens": [51322, 412, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 44003, 16494, 4373, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 248312, "start": 2506.08, "end": 2509.08, "text": " It is determined by a regulator term in the equations", "tokens": [51513, 467, 307, 9540, 538, 257, 36250, 1433, 294, 264, 11787, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14168545084262113, "compression_ratio": 1.6174242424242424, "no_speech_prob": 1.825056382062651e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 250908, "start": 2509.08, "end": 2511.08, "text": " that suppresses runaway growth.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 26835, 279, 1190, 10318, 4599, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 250908, "start": 2512.02, "end": 2514.7599999999998, "text": " LAP1b isn't just a random small chunk of gas.", "tokens": [50512, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 4974, 1359, 16635, 295, 4211, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 250908, "start": 2515.02, "end": 2518.94, "text": " It erupted out of the background at its exact natural correlation length.", "tokens": [50662, 467, 20999, 25383, 484, 295, 264, 3678, 412, 1080, 1900, 3303, 20009, 4641, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 250908, "start": 2519.1, "end": 2519.54, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50866, 3153, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 250908, "start": 2519.72, "end": 2521.7999999999997, "text": " And here's the most crucial part for observability.", "tokens": [50897, 400, 510, 311, 264, 881, 11462, 644, 337, 9951, 2310, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 250908, "start": 2522.58, "end": 2525.88, "text": " Because its baryonic mass, the visible stars we can actually see,", "tokens": [51040, 1436, 1080, 272, 822, 11630, 2758, 11, 264, 8974, 6105, 321, 393, 767, 536, 11, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 250908, "start": 2526.18, "end": 2529.68, "text": " is so incredibly tiny compared to its invisible dark matter halo,", "tokens": [51220, 307, 370, 6252, 5870, 5347, 281, 1080, 14603, 2877, 1871, 46268, 11, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 250908, "start": 2530.48, "end": 2533.42, "text": " the baryons are essentially just sparse tracers.", "tokens": [51435, 264, 272, 822, 892, 366, 4476, 445, 637, 11668, 504, 326, 433, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 250908, "start": 2533.5, "end": 2534.38, "text": " Sparse tracers.", "tokens": [51586, 1738, 11668, 504, 326, 433, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19516284005683765, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810607147785486e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 253438, "start": 2534.38, "end": 2538.1, "text": " Imagine dropping a few tiny drops of fluorescent dye into a massive, rushing river.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 13601, 257, 1326, 5870, 11438, 295, 46735, 20179, 666, 257, 5994, 11, 25876, 6810, 13, 50551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 253438, "start": 2538.5, "end": 2540.32, "text": " The dye doesn't alter the flow of the river at all.", "tokens": [50571, 440, 20179, 1177, 380, 11337, 264, 3095, 295, 264, 6810, 412, 439, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 253438, "start": 2540.42, "end": 2541.0, "text": " It's too small.", "tokens": [50667, 467, 311, 886, 1359, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 253438, "start": 2541.36, "end": 2544.82, "text": " But the dye illuminates the currents, the eddies, the underlying structure of the water.", "tokens": [50714, 583, 264, 20179, 28593, 1024, 264, 30110, 11, 264, 1257, 22018, 11, 264, 14217, 3877, 295, 264, 1281, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 253438, "start": 2544.98, "end": 2545.38, "text": " I see.", "tokens": [50895, 286, 536, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 253438, "start": 2545.52, "end": 2547.42, "text": " The stars of LAP1b are the dye.", "tokens": [50922, 440, 6105, 295, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 366, 264, 20179, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 253438, "start": 2547.9, "end": 2551.94, "text": " There are sparse tracers revealing the massive, unseen constraint basin of the dark matter", "tokens": [51041, 821, 366, 637, 11668, 504, 326, 433, 23983, 264, 5994, 11, 40608, 25534, 34863, 295, 264, 2877, 1871, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 253438, "start": 2551.94, "end": 2555.6, "text": " without actually possessing enough mass to alter its gravitational flow.", "tokens": [51243, 1553, 767, 17490, 278, 1547, 2758, 281, 11337, 1080, 28538, 3095, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 253438, "start": 2555.86, "end": 2558.7000000000003, "text": " But this brings up a massive, glaring paradox.", "tokens": [51439, 583, 341, 5607, 493, 257, 5994, 11, 1563, 1921, 26221, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 253438, "start": 2558.9, "end": 2559.96, "text": " An epistemic paradox.", "tokens": [51591, 1107, 2388, 468, 3438, 26221, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13534906331230612, "compression_ratio": 1.735593220338983, "no_speech_prob": 1.9767778993567964e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 255996, "start": 2559.96, "end": 2566.52, "text": " If these tiny, least overwritten baby galaxies are the absolute most important objects in", "tokens": [50365, 759, 613, 5870, 11, 1935, 670, 26859, 3186, 28755, 366, 264, 8236, 881, 1021, 6565, 294, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 255996, "start": 2566.52, "end": 2569.12, "text": " the universe for understanding the fundamental laws of physics,", "tokens": [50693, 264, 6445, 337, 3701, 264, 8088, 6064, 295, 10649, 11, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 255996, "start": 2569.6, "end": 2573.14, "text": " why did it take until the year 2026 to finally find one?", "tokens": [50847, 983, 630, 309, 747, 1826, 264, 1064, 945, 10880, 281, 2721, 915, 472, 30, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 255996, "start": 2573.36, "end": 2577.64, "text": " That paradox is the core of the final paper in our stack, mediated extraction.", "tokens": [51035, 663, 26221, 307, 264, 4965, 295, 264, 2572, 3035, 294, 527, 8630, 11, 17269, 770, 30197, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 255996, "start": 2578.16, "end": 2581.16, "text": " And it addresses the fundamental observational problem of astronomy.", "tokens": [51275, 400, 309, 16862, 264, 8088, 9951, 1478, 1154, 295, 37844, 13, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 255996, "start": 2581.66, "end": 2584.8, "text": " The physical systems with the absolute highest informational value,", "tokens": [51450, 440, 4001, 3652, 365, 264, 8236, 6343, 49391, 2158, 11, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10292694879614789, "compression_ratio": 1.6075471698113208, "no_speech_prob": 2.6560173331524606e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 258480, "start": 2584.8, "end": 2589.86, "text": " the pristine, least overwritten fossils like LAP1b are inherently the smallest,", "tokens": [50365, 264, 582, 42745, 11, 1935, 670, 26859, 39159, 411, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 366, 27993, 264, 16998, 11, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 258480, "start": 2590.34, "end": 2592.6800000000003, "text": " the faintest, and the least luminous objects in existence.", "tokens": [50642, 264, 21104, 377, 11, 293, 264, 1935, 32476, 563, 6565, 294, 9123, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 258480, "start": 2592.88, "end": 2592.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50769, 1779, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 258480, "start": 2593.2200000000003, "end": 2597.8, "text": " A galaxy with under 3,300 solar masses sitting 13 billion light-years away", "tokens": [50786, 316, 17639, 365, 833, 805, 11, 12566, 7936, 23935, 3798, 3705, 5218, 1442, 12, 34569, 1314, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 258480, "start": 2597.8, "end": 2601.82, "text": " produces a surface brightness that is exponentially below the detection threshold", "tokens": [51015, 14725, 257, 3753, 21367, 300, 307, 37330, 2507, 264, 17784, 14678, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 258480, "start": 2601.82, "end": 2603.6800000000003, "text": " of any existing or planned human instrument.", "tokens": [51216, 295, 604, 6741, 420, 8589, 1952, 7198, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 258480, "start": 2603.96, "end": 2607.0, "text": " They are permanently inaccessible to direct observation.", "tokens": [51323, 814, 366, 24042, 33230, 780, 964, 281, 2047, 14816, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 258480, "start": 2607.48, "end": 2610.88, "text": " It's like trying to read a microscopic diary written at the dawn of time", "tokens": [51499, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 1401, 257, 47897, 26492, 3720, 412, 264, 18192, 295, 565, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 258480, "start": 2610.88, "end": 2612.6600000000003, "text": " before someone scribbled all over it.", "tokens": [51669, 949, 1580, 39435, 18320, 439, 670, 309, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12581630580681413, "compression_ratio": 1.5797546012269938, "no_speech_prob": 1.5614858581494695e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 261266, "start": 2612.66, "end": 2616.56, "text": " The diary contains the secrets of the universe, but you can't read it with your naked eye,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 26492, 8306, 264, 14093, 295, 264, 6445, 11, 457, 291, 393, 380, 1401, 309, 365, 428, 15791, 3313, 11, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 261266, "start": 2616.7599999999998, "end": 2619.46, "text": " and you literally cannot build a telescope big enough to see it.", "tokens": [50570, 293, 291, 3736, 2644, 1322, 257, 26114, 955, 1547, 281, 536, 309, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 261266, "start": 2620.02, "end": 2624.8599999999997, "text": " So how on Earth did the James Webb Space Telescope see LAP1b?", "tokens": [50733, 407, 577, 322, 4755, 630, 264, 5678, 49649, 8705, 48595, 13960, 536, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 30, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 261266, "start": 2625.04, "end": 2626.3199999999997, "text": " It could not have seen it alone.", "tokens": [50984, 467, 727, 406, 362, 1612, 309, 3312, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 261266, "start": 2626.68, "end": 2630.12, "text": " It required a process fliction calls, mediated extraction.", "tokens": [51066, 467, 4739, 257, 1399, 932, 4105, 5498, 11, 17269, 770, 30197, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 261266, "start": 2630.7799999999997, "end": 2635.06, "text": " The direct line of sight from the telescope's mirror to the tiny LAP1b galaxy", "tokens": [51271, 440, 2047, 1622, 295, 7860, 490, 264, 26114, 311, 8013, 281, 264, 5870, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 17639, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12727178311815449, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 2.0924145662654103e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 263506, "start": 2635.06, "end": 2639.2599999999998, "text": " happened to pass directly through a massive foreground galaxy cluster", "tokens": [50365, 2011, 281, 1320, 3838, 807, 257, 5994, 32058, 17639, 13630, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 263506, "start": 2639.2599999999998, "end": 2644.1, "text": " known as MACS J041c.12403.", "tokens": [50575, 2570, 382, 27716, 50, 508, 14565, 16, 66, 13, 4762, 5254, 18, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 263506, "start": 2644.16, "end": 2645.06, "text": " That's a mouthful.", "tokens": [50820, 663, 311, 257, 4525, 906, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 263506, "start": 2645.2999999999997, "end": 2645.68, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50877, 467, 307, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 263506, "start": 2645.92, "end": 2648.02, "text": " But this foreground cluster is incredibly dense,", "tokens": [50908, 583, 341, 32058, 13630, 307, 6252, 18011, 11, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 263506, "start": 2648.34, "end": 2651.34, "text": " filled with hundreds of mature galaxies and massive amounts of dark matter.", "tokens": [51029, 6412, 365, 6779, 295, 14442, 28755, 293, 5994, 11663, 295, 2877, 1871, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 263506, "start": 2651.52, "end": 2653.98, "text": " And because of all that mass, the cluster bends space.", "tokens": [51188, 400, 570, 295, 439, 300, 2758, 11, 264, 13630, 42990, 1901, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 263506, "start": 2654.04, "end": 2654.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51314, 7587, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 263506, "start": 2654.7999999999997, "end": 2656.54, "text": " It acted as a gravitational lens.", "tokens": [51352, 467, 20359, 382, 257, 28538, 6765, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 263506, "start": 2656.86, "end": 2659.56, "text": " Its immense gravity bent, distorted, and focused.", "tokens": [51455, 6953, 22920, 12110, 14075, 11, 33431, 11, 293, 5178, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15331471641108674, "compression_ratio": 1.5369649805447472, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983229280022715e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 265956, "start": 2659.56, "end": 2662.84, "text": " The faint light coming from LAP1b sitting far behind it,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 21104, 1442, 1348, 490, 441, 4715, 16, 65, 3798, 1400, 2261, 309, 11, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 265956, "start": 2663.12, "end": 2665.2599999999998, "text": " amplifying its apparent brightness by a factor of a hundred.", "tokens": [50543, 9731, 5489, 1080, 18335, 21367, 538, 257, 5952, 295, 257, 3262, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 265956, "start": 2665.6, "end": 2669.42, "text": " So, to read the microscopic diary, you have to get incredibly lucky", "tokens": [50667, 407, 11, 281, 1401, 264, 47897, 26492, 11, 291, 362, 281, 483, 6252, 6356, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 265956, "start": 2669.42, "end": 2673.66, "text": " and find a giant cosmic magnifying glass floating in space,", "tokens": [50858, 293, 915, 257, 7410, 27614, 4944, 5489, 4276, 12607, 294, 1901, 11, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 265956, "start": 2674.04, "end": 2675.7599999999998, "text": " perfectly aligned between you and the text.", "tokens": [51089, 6239, 17962, 1296, 291, 293, 264, 2487, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 265956, "start": 2676.16, "end": 2676.72, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51195, 48746, 736, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 265956, "start": 2677.18, "end": 2680.16, "text": " But fliction expands on the philosophy of observability here.", "tokens": [51246, 583, 932, 4105, 33706, 322, 264, 10675, 295, 9951, 2310, 510, 13, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 265956, "start": 2680.34, "end": 2684.14, "text": " And this is where the grand unification of the theory really solidifies.", "tokens": [51404, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 2697, 517, 3774, 295, 264, 5261, 534, 5100, 11221, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 265956, "start": 2684.54, "end": 2688.4, "text": " The gravitational lens isn't just a lucky technical convenience for astronomers.", "tokens": [51614, 440, 28538, 6765, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 6356, 6191, 19283, 337, 43151, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1459364697216003, "compression_ratio": 1.5876923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.5308659288143511e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 268840, "start": 2688.4, "end": 2693.2200000000003, "text": " It functions structurally as a physical sparse inference operator.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 6828, 6594, 6512, 382, 257, 4001, 637, 11668, 38253, 12973, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 268840, "start": 2693.6, "end": 2695.42, "text": " A physical sparse inference operator.", "tokens": [50625, 316, 4001, 637, 11668, 38253, 12973, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 268840, "start": 2695.56, "end": 2695.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50723, 1079, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 268840, "start": 2696.2400000000002, "end": 2699.1, "text": " It is a physical mechanism embedded in the geometry of the universe", "tokens": [50757, 467, 307, 257, 4001, 7513, 16741, 294, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 6445, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 268840, "start": 2699.1, "end": 2702.86, "text": " that extracts a coherent signal from a source that would otherwise be", "tokens": [50900, 300, 8947, 82, 257, 36239, 6358, 490, 257, 4009, 300, 576, 5911, 312, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 268840, "start": 2702.86, "end": 2705.04, "text": " permanently physically inaccessible.", "tokens": [51088, 24042, 9762, 33230, 780, 964, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 268840, "start": 2705.2200000000003, "end": 2705.7000000000003, "text": " Wait a second.", "tokens": [51206, 3802, 257, 1150, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 268840, "start": 2706.08, "end": 2707.2400000000002, "text": " A sparse inference operator.", "tokens": [51249, 316, 637, 11668, 38253, 12973, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 268840, "start": 2707.36, "end": 2710.2000000000003, "text": " This connects all the way back to the cognitive projection we talked about at the very beginning.", "tokens": [51313, 639, 16967, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 264, 15605, 22743, 321, 2825, 466, 412, 264, 588, 2863, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 268840, "start": 2710.56, "end": 2712.9, "text": " The RSVP framework applied to the brain.", "tokens": [51473, 440, 25855, 53, 47, 8388, 6456, 281, 264, 3567, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 268840, "start": 2713.2200000000003, "end": 2715.2000000000003, "text": " The CLIO holographic observer.", "tokens": [51606, 440, 12855, 15167, 38541, 2662, 299, 27878, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 268840, "start": 2715.6600000000003, "end": 2716.6600000000003, "text": " It absolutely does.", "tokens": [51728, 467, 3122, 775, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1522785723209381, "compression_ratio": 1.7619047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216092917590742e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 271666, "start": 2716.66, "end": 2720.62, "text": " CLIO stands for Constrained Learning and Inference Optimizer.", "tokens": [50365, 12855, 15167, 7382, 337, 8574, 31774, 15205, 293, 682, 5158, 35013, 6545, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 271666, "start": 2721.58, "end": 2723.56, "text": " In the cognitive domain affliction's math,", "tokens": [50611, 682, 264, 15605, 9274, 2096, 75, 4105, 311, 5221, 11, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 271666, "start": 2723.8999999999996, "end": 2728.44, "text": " the human brain cannot possibly process every single piece of raw sensory data hitting it.", "tokens": [50727, 264, 1952, 3567, 2644, 6264, 1399, 633, 2167, 2522, 295, 8936, 27233, 1412, 8850, 309, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 271666, "start": 2729.22, "end": 2734.98, "text": " It has to reconstruct sparse, weak signals from highly attenuated projections of the outside world.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 575, 281, 31499, 637, 11668, 11, 5336, 12354, 490, 5405, 951, 268, 27275, 32371, 295, 264, 2380, 1002, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 271666, "start": 2735.3599999999997, "end": 2736.7599999999998, "text": " It relies on inference.", "tokens": [51300, 467, 30910, 322, 38253, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 271666, "start": 2736.94, "end": 2737.48, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51379, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16924522583743176, "compression_ratio": 1.493212669683258, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493987607333558e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 273748, "start": 2737.48, "end": 2742.7400000000002, "text": " Observational cosmology, Flickshen argues, operates on the exact same thermodynamic principle.", "tokens": [50365, 42547, 1478, 22207, 1793, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 38218, 11, 22577, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 8810, 34988, 8665, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15910410158561938, "compression_ratio": 1.535, "no_speech_prob": 1.958288999709401e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 273748, "start": 2743.2400000000002, "end": 2747.52, "text": " We cannot simply gather larger data sets from brighter sources to understand the early universe", "tokens": [50653, 492, 2644, 2935, 5448, 4833, 1412, 6352, 490, 19764, 7139, 281, 1223, 264, 2440, 6445, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15910410158561938, "compression_ratio": 1.535, "no_speech_prob": 1.958288999709401e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 273748, "start": 2747.52, "end": 2752.96, "text": " because bright sources are mature galaxies, and mature galaxies are heavily overwritten.", "tokens": [50867, 570, 4730, 7139, 366, 14442, 28755, 11, 293, 14442, 28755, 366, 10950, 670, 26859, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15910410158561938, "compression_ratio": 1.535, "no_speech_prob": 1.958288999709401e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 273748, "start": 2753.2400000000002, "end": 2754.62, "text": " They are muddy brown paint.", "tokens": [51153, 814, 366, 38540, 6292, 4225, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15910410158561938, "compression_ratio": 1.535, "no_speech_prob": 1.958288999709401e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 275462, "start": 2754.62, "end": 2758.54, "text": " So we are entirely dependent on the universe to do the magnifying for us.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 321, 366, 7696, 12334, 322, 264, 6445, 281, 360, 264, 4944, 5489, 337, 505, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914895881306041, "compression_ratio": 1.7902439024390244, "no_speech_prob": 2.8432544946915828e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 275462, "start": 2758.54, "end": 2764.22, "text": " We are entirely dependent on the universe's own geometry, gravitational lenses, re-ionization quenching", "tokens": [50561, 492, 366, 7696, 12334, 322, 264, 6445, 311, 1065, 18426, 11, 28538, 18059, 11, 319, 12, 313, 2144, 421, 268, 17354, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914895881306041, "compression_ratio": 1.7902439024390244, "no_speech_prob": 2.8432544946915828e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 275462, "start": 2764.22, "end": 2766.8599999999997, "text": " to decode and amplify its hidden signals for us.", "tokens": [50845, 281, 979, 1429, 293, 41174, 1080, 7633, 12354, 337, 505, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914895881306041, "compression_ratio": 1.7902439024390244, "no_speech_prob": 2.8432544946915828e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 275462, "start": 2767.12, "end": 2769.02, "text": " We cannot force the data out of the cosmos.", "tokens": [50990, 492, 2644, 3464, 264, 1412, 484, 295, 264, 41794, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914895881306041, "compression_ratio": 1.7902439024390244, "no_speech_prob": 2.8432544946915828e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 275462, "start": 2769.56, "end": 2773.56, "text": " We are waiting for the universe to perform the first stage of cognitive inference on our behalf.", "tokens": [51112, 492, 366, 3806, 337, 264, 6445, 281, 2042, 264, 700, 3233, 295, 15605, 38253, 322, 527, 9490, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11914895881306041, "compression_ratio": 1.7902439024390244, "no_speech_prob": 2.8432544946915828e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 277356, "start": 2773.56, "end": 2778.58, "text": " Okay, let's take a deep breath and try to pull all of these incredibly dense threads together.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 2452, 6045, 293, 853, 281, 2235, 439, 295, 613, 6252, 18011, 19314, 1214, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 277356, "start": 2779.1, "end": 2781.42, "text": " This has been a monumental journey.", "tokens": [50642, 639, 575, 668, 257, 43105, 4671, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 277356, "start": 2781.94, "end": 2786.86, "text": " We started with the RSVP triplet, the scalar, vector, and entropy fields.", "tokens": [50784, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 1376, 14657, 11, 264, 39684, 11, 8062, 11, 293, 30867, 7909, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 277356, "start": 2787.4, "end": 2794.22, "text": " We realized that reality is essentially the literal pressure, wind, and heat of a continuous geometric fluid,", "tokens": [51057, 492, 5334, 300, 4103, 307, 4476, 264, 20411, 3321, 11, 2468, 11, 293, 3738, 295, 257, 10957, 33246, 9113, 11, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 277356, "start": 2794.68, "end": 2798.42, "text": " and that gravity isn't a pull, but a falling down an entropy drain.", "tokens": [51421, 293, 300, 12110, 1943, 380, 257, 2235, 11, 457, 257, 7440, 760, 364, 30867, 12339, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 277356, "start": 2798.66, "end": 2798.92, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51620, 1079, 13, 51633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15518848263487525, "compression_ratio": 1.5542168674698795, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485568114955496e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 279892, "start": 2798.92, "end": 2804.36, "text": " We then saw how the continuous flow is violently chopped into discrete history by the refuse operator,", "tokens": [50365, 492, 550, 1866, 577, 264, 10957, 3095, 307, 46728, 16497, 666, 27706, 2503, 538, 264, 16791, 12973, 11, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 279892, "start": 2804.58, "end": 2807.3, "text": " which creates the arrow of time by destroying information,", "tokens": [50648, 597, 7829, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 538, 19926, 1589, 11, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 279892, "start": 2807.56, "end": 2810.8, "text": " proving that identity is nothing more than your irreversible history.", "tokens": [50797, 27221, 300, 6575, 307, 1825, 544, 813, 428, 16014, 840, 964, 2503, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 279892, "start": 2811.04, "end": 2813.32, "text": " We then turned to the crisis of quantum gravity.", "tokens": [50971, 492, 550, 3574, 281, 264, 5869, 295, 13018, 12110, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 279892, "start": 2813.98, "end": 2816.4, "text": " We shed our 50-year fear of quantum ghosts,", "tokens": [51118, 492, 14951, 527, 2625, 12, 5294, 4240, 295, 13018, 21744, 11, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 279892, "start": 2816.82, "end": 2821.3, "text": " realizing that mathematical infinities and negative probabilities are just coordinate pathologies,", "tokens": [51260, 16734, 300, 18894, 7193, 1088, 293, 3671, 33783, 366, 445, 15670, 3100, 6204, 11, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 279892, "start": 2821.64, "end": 2822.86, "text": " smudges on the x-ray film.", "tokens": [51501, 899, 532, 2880, 322, 264, 2031, 12, 3458, 2007, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 279892, "start": 2822.94, "end": 2823.1800000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51566, 1779, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 279892, "start": 2823.32, "end": 2826.12, "text": " The universe's own geometry, utilizing the Born rule,", "tokens": [51585, 440, 6445, 311, 1065, 18426, 11, 26775, 264, 29808, 4978, 11, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16786871837968587, "compression_ratio": 1.6378205128205128, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897977599834245e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 282612, "start": 2826.12, "end": 2830.16, "text": " squares away those negative ghosts before they can become observable physical tumors.", "tokens": [50365, 19368, 1314, 729, 3671, 21744, 949, 436, 393, 1813, 9951, 712, 4001, 38466, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 282612, "start": 2830.7799999999997, "end": 2832.9, "text": " And because we aren't afraid of the ghosts anymore,", "tokens": [50598, 400, 570, 321, 3212, 380, 4638, 295, 264, 21744, 3602, 11, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 282612, "start": 2833.12, "end": 2836.16, "text": " that freed us from needing string theory and ten dimensions.", "tokens": [50715, 300, 21796, 505, 490, 18006, 6798, 5261, 293, 2064, 12819, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 282612, "start": 2836.7599999999998, "end": 2840.96, "text": " It allowed us to see the Big Bang as a perfect CPT symmetric mirror,", "tokens": [50897, 467, 4350, 505, 281, 536, 264, 5429, 11538, 382, 257, 2176, 22431, 51, 32330, 8013, 11, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 282612, "start": 2841.48, "end": 2843.7999999999997, "text": " predicting the exact mass of dark matter,", "tokens": [51133, 32884, 264, 1900, 2758, 295, 2877, 1871, 11, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 282612, "start": 2844.2799999999997, "end": 2849.02, "text": " and the exact requirement of three generations of particles without needing cosmic inflation.", "tokens": [51273, 293, 264, 1900, 11695, 295, 1045, 10593, 295, 10007, 1553, 18006, 27614, 15860, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 282612, "start": 2849.2799999999997, "end": 2850.44, "text": " Huge simplification.", "tokens": [51523, 37043, 6883, 3774, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17369633532584983, "compression_ratio": 1.606060606060606, "no_speech_prob": 1.9347635472899416e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 285044, "start": 2850.44, "end": 2854.84, "text": " And finally, we looked through a giant cosmic magnifying glass", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 2956, 807, 257, 7410, 27614, 4944, 5489, 4276, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 285044, "start": 2854.84, "end": 2858.88, "text": " to see LAP-1b, a pristine fossil galaxy,", "tokens": [50585, 281, 536, 441, 4715, 12, 16, 65, 11, 257, 582, 42745, 18737, 17639, 11, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 285044, "start": 2859.02, "end": 2861.3, "text": " acting out the refuse operator in real time,", "tokens": [50794, 6577, 484, 264, 16791, 12973, 294, 957, 565, 11, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 285044, "start": 2861.44, "end": 2863.5, "text": " its oxygen trapped forever in a black hole.", "tokens": [50915, 1080, 9169, 14994, 5680, 294, 257, 2211, 5458, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 285044, "start": 2863.7400000000002, "end": 2866.84, "text": " It is a profound, sweeping synthesis of multiple disciplines.", "tokens": [51030, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 11, 33285, 30252, 295, 3866, 21919, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 285044, "start": 2867.2400000000002, "end": 2869.42, "text": " And it naturally raises the ultimate question.", "tokens": [51205, 400, 309, 8195, 19658, 264, 9705, 1168, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 285044, "start": 2869.7400000000002, "end": 2873.44, "text": " Why should you, sitting here listening to this, going to your job, living your life,", "tokens": [51330, 1545, 820, 291, 11, 3798, 510, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 516, 281, 428, 1691, 11, 2647, 428, 993, 11, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 285044, "start": 2873.8, "end": 2876.18, "text": " why should you care about this dense mathematical unification?", "tokens": [51533, 983, 820, 291, 1127, 466, 341, 18011, 18894, 517, 3774, 30, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 285044, "start": 2876.4, "end": 2877.8, "text": " Because it sounds very theoretical.", "tokens": [51663, 1436, 309, 3263, 588, 20864, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1384746327119715, "compression_ratio": 1.5746753246753247, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813268442425477e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 287780, "start": 2877.8, "end": 2878.7400000000002, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 775, 13, 50412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 287780, "start": 2879.38, "end": 2880.38, "text": " But we should care.", "tokens": [50444, 583, 321, 820, 1127, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 287780, "start": 2880.7400000000002, "end": 2885.04, "text": " Because it fundamentally and irrevocably changes how we view our place in reality.", "tokens": [50512, 1436, 309, 17879, 293, 16014, 20836, 1188, 2962, 577, 321, 1910, 527, 1081, 294, 4103, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 287780, "start": 2885.42, "end": 2888.2000000000003, "text": " Our physical universe, our own internal cognition,", "tokens": [50746, 2621, 4001, 6445, 11, 527, 1065, 6920, 46905, 11, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 287780, "start": 2888.5600000000004, "end": 2893.4, "text": " and the societal institutions we build are all governed by the exact same", "tokens": [50903, 293, 264, 33472, 8142, 321, 1322, 366, 439, 35529, 538, 264, 1900, 912, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 287780, "start": 2893.4, "end": 2898.0800000000004, "text": " underlying thermodynamic rules of constraint, resolution, and entropic flow.", "tokens": [51145, 14217, 8810, 34988, 4474, 295, 25534, 11, 8669, 11, 293, 948, 39173, 3095, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 287780, "start": 2898.48, "end": 2903.1000000000004, "text": " The barriers we build between physics, biology, and sociology are artificial.", "tokens": [51399, 440, 13565, 321, 1322, 1296, 10649, 11, 14956, 11, 293, 41744, 366, 11677, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 287780, "start": 2903.6600000000003, "end": 2904.84, "text": " It is all one substrate.", "tokens": [51658, 467, 307, 439, 472, 27585, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876017784585758, "compression_ratio": 1.6186770428015564, "no_speech_prob": 2.2276961091777236e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 290484, "start": 2904.84, "end": 2908.26, "text": " It leaves us with one final, deeply provocative thought.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5510, 505, 365, 472, 2572, 11, 8760, 47663, 1194, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 290484, "start": 2908.92, "end": 2910.7000000000003, "text": " In the closing pages of the monographs,", "tokens": [50569, 682, 264, 10377, 7183, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 82, 11, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 290484, "start": 2910.78, "end": 2914.08, "text": " Flixson introduces something called the derived interface conjecture.", "tokens": [50662, 3235, 970, 3015, 31472, 746, 1219, 264, 18949, 9226, 416, 1020, 540, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 290484, "start": 2914.6400000000003, "end": 2916.6400000000003, "text": " Think about the screen of the smartphone in your pocket.", "tokens": [50855, 6557, 466, 264, 2568, 295, 264, 13307, 294, 428, 8963, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 290484, "start": 2917.04, "end": 2920.6600000000003, "text": " When you look at it, you see apps, colorful icons, folders, photographs.", "tokens": [50975, 1133, 291, 574, 412, 309, 11, 291, 536, 7733, 11, 18506, 23308, 11, 31082, 11, 17649, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 290484, "start": 2921.1200000000003, "end": 2923.02, "text": " But inside the phone, none of that exists.", "tokens": [51179, 583, 1854, 264, 2593, 11, 6022, 295, 300, 8198, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 290484, "start": 2923.28, "end": 2928.6400000000003, "text": " Inside the phone is just billions of microscopic transistors violently flipping ones and zeros at the speed of light.", "tokens": [51287, 15123, 264, 2593, 307, 445, 17375, 295, 47897, 1145, 46976, 46728, 26886, 2306, 293, 35193, 412, 264, 3073, 295, 1442, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 290484, "start": 2928.78, "end": 2931.6400000000003, "text": " The colorful apps aren't real in a fundamental physical sense.", "tokens": [51562, 440, 18506, 7733, 3212, 380, 957, 294, 257, 8088, 4001, 2020, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14678572057708492, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051771878858537e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 293164, "start": 2931.64, "end": 2933.44, "text": " They are a constructed interface.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 257, 17083, 9226, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997482158519603, "compression_ratio": 1.5695067264573992, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 293164, "start": 2933.7, "end": 2940.2, "text": " They are designed specifically so that you, a human, can interact with the machine without your brain exploding from the complexity.", "tokens": [50468, 814, 366, 4761, 4682, 370, 300, 291, 11, 257, 1952, 11, 393, 4648, 365, 264, 3479, 1553, 428, 3567, 35175, 490, 264, 14024, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997482158519603, "compression_ratio": 1.5695067264573992, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 293164, "start": 2941.2599999999998, "end": 2946.04, "text": " The conjecture proposes that the reality we see, touch, and measure every single day,", "tokens": [50846, 440, 416, 1020, 540, 2365, 4201, 300, 264, 4103, 321, 536, 11, 2557, 11, 293, 3481, 633, 2167, 786, 11, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997482158519603, "compression_ratio": 1.5695067264573992, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 293164, "start": 2946.2599999999998, "end": 2952.02, "text": " the positive probabilities, the solid 3D space, the steady forward flow of time, is exactly that.", "tokens": [51096, 264, 3353, 33783, 11, 264, 5100, 805, 35, 1901, 11, 264, 13211, 2128, 3095, 295, 565, 11, 307, 2293, 300, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16997482158519603, "compression_ratio": 1.5695067264573992, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228919250127483e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 295202, "start": 2952.02, "end": 2959.28, "text": " It is merely the observable interface of a much stranger, wilder, mathematically terrifying internal state space.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 17003, 264, 9951, 712, 9226, 295, 257, 709, 18834, 11, 4868, 260, 11, 44003, 18106, 6920, 1785, 1901, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09834134088803644, "compression_ratio": 1.438423645320197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551303292673293e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 295202, "start": 2959.4, "end": 2959.84, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50734, 3153, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09834134088803644, "compression_ratio": 1.438423645320197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551303292673293e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 295202, "start": 2960.28, "end": 2970.42, "text": " The true universe, the true RSVP plenum, is full of hidden directions, negative norms, indefinite inner products, and ghost symmetries that we simply aren't equipped to see.", "tokens": [50778, 440, 2074, 6445, 11, 264, 2074, 25855, 53, 47, 499, 268, 449, 11, 307, 1577, 295, 7633, 11095, 11, 3671, 24357, 11, 24162, 5194, 642, 7284, 3383, 11, 293, 8359, 14232, 302, 2244, 300, 321, 2935, 3212, 380, 15218, 281, 536, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09834134088803644, "compression_ratio": 1.438423645320197, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551303292673293e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 297042, "start": 2970.42, "end": 2972.54, "text": " They secretly hold the whole thing together.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 22611, 1797, 264, 1379, 551, 1214, 13, 50471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 297042, "start": 2972.6800000000003, "end": 2977.8, "text": " We look at the X-ray of reality, and we desperately want to see clean binary engineering precision.", "tokens": [50478, 492, 574, 412, 264, 1783, 12, 3458, 295, 4103, 11, 293, 321, 23726, 528, 281, 536, 2541, 17434, 7043, 18356, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 297042, "start": 2978.38, "end": 2979.5, "text": " Broken or not broken.", "tokens": [50763, 46624, 420, 406, 5463, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 297042, "start": 2979.6800000000003, "end": 2980.5, "text": " Positive or zero.", "tokens": [50828, 46326, 420, 4018, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 297042, "start": 2980.96, "end": 2983.3, "text": " But the universe isn't a simple broken bone.", "tokens": [50892, 583, 264, 6445, 1943, 380, 257, 2199, 5463, 9026, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 297042, "start": 2983.6, "end": 2988.86, "text": " It is a vast, murky, incredibly beautiful system of hidden fluid flows and refused histories.", "tokens": [51024, 467, 307, 257, 8369, 11, 5257, 4133, 11, 6252, 2238, 1185, 295, 7633, 9113, 12867, 293, 14654, 30631, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 297042, "start": 2989.2000000000003, "end": 2994.56, "text": " And maybe, just maybe, the fact that we can't see the ghost, the fact that we only see the clean interface,", "tokens": [51304, 400, 1310, 11, 445, 1310, 11, 264, 1186, 300, 321, 393, 380, 536, 264, 8359, 11, 264, 1186, 300, 321, 787, 536, 264, 2541, 9226, 11, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 297042, "start": 2994.7000000000003, "end": 2996.92, "text": " is exactly what allows us to exist at all.", "tokens": [51579, 307, 2293, 437, 4045, 505, 281, 2514, 412, 439, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16158230048565825, "compression_ratio": 1.6401384083044983, "no_speech_prob": 2.4468480627065636e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 299692, "start": 2996.92, "end": 3026.9, "text": " We'll see you next time.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 603, 536, 291, 958, 565, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.93270263671875, "compression_ratio": 0.75, "no_speech_prob": 1.800412249841621e-11}], "language": "en"}
